{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast","id":907934,"title":"Sell me on Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-05T15:45:22-07:00","id":907934,"title":"Sell me on Beast","content":"A little background: I was around for Beast's Kickstarter, but did not end up getting the final product. As such, my view of the game is colored heavily by the first draft, and my awareness of what has changed is limited to what changes were revealed during the Kickstarter. What <i>has</i> changed, and why should I give the game a second look?<br /> <br /> (Also: I've forgotten more than I remember about the game; so feel free to post as if I don't know anything about the game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-05-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:11:48-07:00","id":907957,"title":"","content":"I'm in the same Boat as the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:41:40-07:00","id":907969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=907957#post907957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the same Boat as the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>As am I. So bring it on Beast fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:42:36-07:00","id":907971,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Beast, my go-to references are <i>Burn Notice</i> and <i>Leverage</i>. If you haven't see them, those shows are about an ex-spy/ex-insurance investigator and his crew of criminal associates utterly ruining the lives of people who have it coming for one reason or another. If you've seen the trailers for Persona 5, that's looking like a good reference as well, if you want to play a more moral game of Beast.<br /> <br /> For example!<br /> <br /> Spoiler for Burn Notice:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> There's an episode of Burn Notice where this rich asshole - this is a recurring theme - frames someone else for the theft of a jewel so he can get the insurance money and then sell the jewel anyway. The team approaches the guy about buying the jewel, scope out his security, try to bribe one of his guards just so the guy gets more paranoid and fires his entire security team, and when the pressure gets too much and the guy decides to put the jewel in his deposit box so it can be safe, the mean knows exactly what he's going to do. They get to the bank first, call in a robbery, shoot out the camera and jam the bank's security. The cops get there, immediately suspect the armed security team, search the rich asshole, and find the jewel.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Spoiler for Leverage:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> There's an episode where an Irish mobster is running an extortion racket and squeezing money out of people. The team suckers him into a poker game, get him to confess to smuggling in front of three off-duty cops who are running the poker game, find out where he's keeping his money while he's distracted, steal the money, bet his own money at the poker game, break his fingers, and then run him out of town so they can give the money back.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Beast is like that, only instead of doing it to help people, you're doing it to feed. Also, you've got nightmare powers and you can turn into a dragon. That helps, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:51:19-07:00","id":907980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=907971#post907971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is like that, only instead of doing it to help people, you're doing it to feed. Also, you've got nightmare powers and you can turn into a dragon. That helps, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>See? I can't put myself in that mindset. Then it becomes kind of repetitive. There's no downward spiral in Beast, you're basically a third party psychopath/asshole.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-05-2016, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:59:14-07:00","id":907984,"title":"","content":"I should warn I have poor sales skills and probably couldn't sell a bucket of water to a man on fire.<br /> <br /> Part of it might be if your group is playing one thing, like vampire, and you don't want to play a vampire. But you don't want to have something entirely thematically different. So you can be a Beast, which can help out the other players and still be its own, powerful creature.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I guess a lot of it is what originally sold me on Changeling. You can be, basically, any of the other monsters, and you don't have to do 'their' thing, whether it's Humanity and Wisdom or Lineages and Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:06:24-07:00","id":907987,"title":"","content":"I think my main issue with Beast is that it seems to be treading a lot of the same water that Vampire does; &quot;I'm a hungry monster who teaches mortals with fear&quot; has been the schtick of the Lancea Sanctum for over a decade now, and vampires are a lot easier to grok than incarnate fears of humanity who may have always been you or maybe ate your soul? Even ignoring the first draft debacle, it remains that the game largely feels kind of directionless (do Beasts just go out and fuck with people until they need to fight the inexplicably-coded-as-evil Heroes?) and that the crossover element seems less baked in and more there because the dev said so. Hell, Mage feels more like a crossover game than Beast does.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear some non-confrontational pitches from folks, because I have a hard time seeing the appeal of Beast and am still very much haunted by the initial draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:42:46-07:00","id":908004,"title":"","content":"They say not to shoot the messenger, but banshees still get a bad rep. When your legend overshadows your life for too long, you become a particularly unsubtle siren warning of a particular flavor of The World Is Not Safe. Even if you're not starving yourself, people will pick up on something from the big and little bite marks you and yours make at the edges of their social circles.<br /> <br /> They called Satan the dragon and his fellows great beasts; you're the Adversary. You live in the Id Vortex. You're a <i>de facto</i> potent chunk of the narrative-driven collective human unconscious trying to find its nuances in how other monsters shake the mortal soul, and one of the easiest ways to accomplish that is to learn by doing.<br /> <br /> They say that life is suffering; subject or object, you are Suffering. Your ties to other supernatural beings manifest in the ability to refine grains of terror from the fears they express and inhabit \u2014 not just the things that make them scary, but the things that make them scared. Experiencing a monster's powers firsthand is one of the easiest ways to learn what makes them scary. All of them save the most patient (and as an etymology nerd I implore you to examine the root of that adjective) will eventually be driven away unless they have nowhere else to go.<br /> <br /> They say monsters are selfish, but the self is a deep road with many turnings. You offer self-knowledge of the fundamental sort: what are the people you interact with as a monster like at their cores, in their hearts-of-hearts? What are they like in the dark? You are uniquely well-placed to find out.<br /> <br /> They always describe the old monsters in terms of other creatures. The chimera doesn't have three chimera heads, it has the heads of a lion and a snake and a goat just like Cousin Ferdinand has the same eyes you got from Grandma Maggie. The dragon keeps many beasts inside its skin, and it partakes of those qualities that make it strongest and most terrifying.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Beasts as a whole are hooked up to almost every supernatural actor in the setting at the level of theme and motif; making and testing personal connections does triple duty as a course of self-discovery, a means of gaining supernatural power, and a process of exploring the innermost depths of the universal human psyche; and the stories that can be spun from having to balance hungers that threaten to drive a wedge between you and human society with the common need for a place to belong are potent, if heavy, stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-05-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:50:58-07:00","id":908006,"title":"","content":"Alright, like nofather, I'm not exactly a professional at this, so forgive any missteps.<br /> <br /> <i>The monster haunted your dreams for so long. Maybe you confronted it on your own, facing down the thing that haunted you only to see that it was just a potential part of yourself waiting for you to embrace it. Maybe another aided you in doing so. Whatever the case you chose to be Devoured, and in doing so were reborn anew.<br /> <br /> Now your Soul is a mighty beast, an incarnation of the fears within the souls of man. This gives you power, from inhuman strength or beauty or intellect to more supernatural gifts like a flaming breath or the form of a swarm of insects. You also have more subtle gifts, psychic scalpels born from the fault-lines of the human and abhuman mind.<br /> <br /> But at the same time you bear a terrible Hunger, for it is the nature of monsters to be driven by such wants. You hoard or hunt or ruin because your nature requires it, like your human peers require water. The other monsters speak of teaching through fear, an imperfect mission that never the less gives a purpose to what would otherwise be mindless feeding.<br /> <br /> Of course, not all agree with this. Many would argue that you are a blight that should not exist. Maybe they're right. Some among these are brave humans who hold a candle to light the darkness you call home. Others, the stories say, were once your partners in a great dance of hope and fear that made mankind stronger; now they come to you mad-eyed and bearing power ripped from the corpses of your fallen brothers and sisters, seeking validation in murder to assuage the holes in their soul.<br /> <br /> But not all being in this world are you foes. Many of the creatures normal people fear you call Kin, whether from a single progenitor or through the primordial ooze of your nature. Not all are things you would join with, and many you might find abhorrent. Others are like you, once-men who struggle to find a place between survival and morality. Your souls touch each other, and you may grant them strength even as they grant you succor and unknowingly teach you the fears of their soul.<br /> <br /> So what will you do, little Timori, one both fearsome and fearful? Will you feed and feed and feed until the light fades from your eyes and the Heroes are made righteous merely through your slaying? Will you seek to make yourself useful through fear, punishing the wicked or trying to teach what others need to learn? Will you immerse yourself in your Kin, giving them strength so you can be a net gain to someone? Or will you seek your Inheritance, throwing away your humanity in hopes it will numb your pain?*<br /> <br /> No matter what, you are Begotten. Either find a way to live with that, or do not live at all.</i><br /> <br /> Beast the Primordial,as I see it, is a game of monstrous Hungers and finding a purpose, of defining yourself and making a niche, whether in the monsters you call family or trying to benefit the world or even just being a jerk because doing so means you don't have to be human enough to care anymore. But no matter what, you must find a path to walk down, a way to be. Otherwise, why not listen to the calls of the slayers that name themselves Heroes and save the world from your existance?<br /> <br /> Sorry if that's not a good pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:53:05-07:00","id":908007,"title":"","content":"This is the way that I look at Beast. You are someone with a problem, a hunger that will cause bad things to happen if you feed it and bad things to happen if you don't feed it. It's a shitty situation, but you didn't choose it and there's no way to undo it. What matters are the choices you make to deal with it. You can try to starve it, feeding that hunger just enough that the monster doesn't go out on its own rampage, but you'll pretty much be throwing away any hope of having a normal life. Some would say that's a worthy sacrifice, others won't accept that. You can try to keep it fed as best you can, making the monster pliant and docile, so you can have something resembling an actual human existence. Feeding is perilous though, how do you do it? Do you try to find a method of feeding that will inflict the least harm, living conservatively enough that you don't have to feed more than once in a while? Do you try to embrace the whole &quot;teaching through fear&quot; thing? Do you try to use the normal life it gives you to do good in the world to make up for the harm you cause by feeding? Its all up to you. Alternatively you can flip the whole thing on its side, cultivating kinship with the other supernatural denizens and feeding vicariously through them, a method that is kind of a separate game from the rest of Beast but one that some might consider to be the least objectionable option presented to you. <br /> <br /> Dealing with Heroes is very much the same way. How self conscious you want to be about the way Heroes get made and how they're also stuck with a raw deal they didn't ask for is entirely in your court. Meaningful reflection on the topic is made more difficult by the fact that they're still trying to kill you most of the time and their particular neuroses can make them hard to sympathize with, but who said the right thing was always the easy thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:07:02-07:00","id":908016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908004#post908004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. It's pretty much my view of it, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:59:21-07:00","id":908059,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I don't like a lot of the changes they made. The original draft may have been controversial, but it was controversial in a cool, thought-provoking way. The finished draft is still controversial, but more over accusations of being watered down and needlessly PC. However, here are some of the key changes (for better or worse):<ul><li>The &quot;ugly duckling&quot; theme has been removed. Rather than being born a monster, Beasts are now closer to a Dreamspeaker (<i>Awakening</i>-style) gone wrong, one that's fused with a goetic demon</li> <li>Many of the examples have been toned down. Rather than slaughter people, a number of sample Beasts now only scare people. And examples formerly involving children (such as Mrs. Winters preying on the neighborhood bully) have had the ages changed, or been dropped entirely</li> <li>Heroes have been beefed up, apparently with an eye to making them available as PCs in a later supplement. They're no longer obsessed psycophaths provoked by Beast hunts - such characters still exist, but now they're just insane/degenerate members of the Hero splat.</li> <li>New rules for merging Lairs, along with the introduction of the Apex - the supernatural creature that most terrifies the locals, and whose existence colors all the Lairs in the region</li> </ul>And yet, there are still a lot of good ideas, and memorable color. <b>Satchel </b>and<b> Zealous Christian24 </b>have very good pitches, but here's an excerpt from the book, where a werewolf encounters a Beast for the first time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>THE VIEW FROM WITHOUT:</u><br /> GIANNA IONESCU, IRRAKA STORM LORD</b></div> <br /> I had a bad night, once.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to talk about how I got there. Let\u2019s just say there was no moon and no one to see it. I ran them off the road. The car was smashed up against the tree, and I walked down from the street. I wanted blood and flesh and bone, and I found it. Two of them were dead and one was gasping his last.<br /> <br /> And then in the trees above me, I smelled her. She was\u2026slinking, I guess. She smelled like cinnamon and metal, and I looked up and saw her eyes. She wasn\u2019t there to judge me. She was there to join me, I think.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t do it. I thought about it, thought about changing and feasting, but I didn\u2019t. I ran, got back in my car, and went back to my pack.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what I saw that night, but I think it was there to show me what I might have become. If I\u2019d eaten</div> </div> </div> </div>As for what Beast <i>do</i>, there are a number of ideas, besides teaching through fear, including:<ul><li>Pull a Batman/Punisher/Spawn, and try to clean up a town</li> <li>Become a supernatural bounty hunter, hunting the worst of the worst</li> <li>Join a group of mages, and start raiding tombs and lost temples. Lost arcane knowledge for the mages, while the Beast explores forgotten terrors (perfect fodder for new Nightmares - the spell-like powers of Beasts)</li> <li>Build a multi-splat empire</li> <li>Explore the meaning of friendship with a Promethean (Beasts are immune to Disquiet)</li> <li>Wage war against the God-Machine</li> <li>Feud with the Gentry, and/or protect a freehold of changelings</li> <li>Attempt to become a god</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:30:26-07:00","id":908112,"title":"","content":"\u25cf So if I'm understanding you correctly, Beasts are like Sin-Eaters, except that they're \u201cClaimed\u201d by fear-spirits? (One of the problems I had during the KS was that I could never quite get a handle on <i>what a Beast is</i>.)<br /> \u25cf Where <i>do</i> Heroes come from, if not Beast hunts?<br /> <br /> Those, I think, would be my top two questions for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:04:56-07:00","id":908130,"title":"","content":"1) Claimed is not quite correct, as the Horror is still pretty much the whole of their soul-The act of Devouring, at a minimum, makes the Horror what it eats in this case.<br /> <br /> 2) Heroes emerge from the Primordial Dream as well, but where the Beast's connections comes from the depths, the Heroes belong to the breadth and shallows of the Dream-their dreams are a 'broad picture' of the Dream. Ideally, this makes them skalds, warrior-poets and prophet-soldiers who interpret the currents before the Beast comes, and responds(and teaches) accordingly. For a wide variety of reasons, that hasn't been the case as humanity has become more and more divorced in their attentions, and most Heroes tend interpret their dreams as calls to destiny and glory, paranoia and visceral response.<br /> <br /> That second one might not be wholly accurate, somehow that got fuzzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:32:09-07:00","id":908137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908007#post908007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the way that I look at Beast. You are someone with a problem, a hunger that will cause bad things to happen if you feed it and bad things to happen if you don't feed it. It's a shitty situation, but you didn't choose it and there's no way to undo it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, don't you <i>actually</i> choose it now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908130#post908130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Claimed is not quite correct, as the Horror is still pretty much the whole of their soul-The act of Devouring, at a minimum, makes the Horror what it eats in this case</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Claimed is a fusion of two beings. Beasts seem to be an Astral entity (the Horror) that eats you, then thinks it is you. Kinda. I think it is interesting that in none of the Inheritances, does the person before the Devouring survive, it's always the Horror (or the &quot;Beast&quot; in the case of Incarnate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:35:35-07:00","id":908139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908112#post908112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf So if I'm understanding you correctly, Beasts are like Sin-Eaters, except that they're \u201cClaimed\u201d by fear-spirits? (One of the problems I had during the KS was that I could never quite get a handle on <i>what a Beast is</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside all the problems of particulars? Yes, the Begotten are people who have supernatural resonance with the archetypes of monsters.<br /> <br /> Most of their powers at least touch on notions of sympathetic connection \u2014 Atavisms work more easily in places that resonate with the Lair, new Nightmares are developed from characters you have Family Ties with, Primordial Pathways need the outside end to resemble the inside at least conceptually \u2014 and with time a lot of Beasts edge closer to retreating from engagement with society in favor of holing up in the Lair or wandering the stranger parts of the cosmology that tend to echo their nature back at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:41:14-07:00","id":908145,"title":"","content":"Here's a couple questions: in the final draft, have Beasts always been Beasts and eventually metaphysically realize that (much like the First Change of a Werewolf), or are they normal mortals that one day get hollowed out and inhabited by a Horror? How intelligent is a Horror; is it just a hunger and a couple notable traits, or could you settle down and talk to it with deep enough meditation? What is the final origin for Heroes, and are they still utterly demonized or were they made more humane? And lastly, what would the average supernatural get out of a Beast's company? I can't imagine the Lost feeling comfortable around something both so profoundly other and also so borderline abusive, and even the book itself says that Mummies and Beasts don't really have a reason to hang around.<br /> <br /> I also have to wonder if the initial feeling that the game was about being an abuser still remains, because that soured me on things far more than the general What Do We Do? feeling or hamfisted attempts at feeling progressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:42:45-07:00","id":908146,"title":"","content":"My opinions on Beast are...divided, the splat is mechanically fine, but everything surrounding it, the fluff, antagonists, the whole crossover focus, everything falls flat for me. I can shit talk Beast all day, and have, but this thread is about selling Beast, so let me pitch what I personally like about the splat:<br /> <br /> Fundamentally Beast is about playing a total fuckwad, an expression of the human Id that justifies pure self-indulgence with the notion that they are &quot;educating&quot; people, if they bother to justify it at all. Now, one might read that last sentence as me decrying Beast, but that'd be wrong. Beast isn't attractive if you are looking to be the good guy, Harry Dresden, 80s TV show protagonist sort, but if you want an ambiguous character who makes others questions their core self-assumptions Beast is your game.<br /> <br /> Now one might say that such characters are untenable as PCs, but let me pitch you the two Beast PCs I've played with (both as a Storyteller and a Player) and hopefully they can speak for themselves:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast #1: Kwame Bonsu<br /> <br /> Kwame was introduced to my Mage/Werewolf game set in Kyoto, a spidery fellow based on the Anansi myth he was (like his inspiration) a gregarious trickster. Also a self interested sociopath. In a game of spirit politics, schemes, inherited duties and grave perils Kwame was a breath of fresh air: a lying theif who just wanted to steal as much as he possibly could and gave not one shit about the repercussions to others. He enjoyed causing commotion for no reason and bullied characters for no other reason than it entertained him. Now that might sound like bad PC material, and I'd be first to admit he was absolutely an antagonist, but he did a good job of putting other character's interests in perspective and pointing out that, at their core, all the high minded talk of duties and schemes was motivated by very simple instincts.<br /> <br /> Kwame was a splendid PC...everyone greatly enjoyed when he, in the classic Anansi way, overstepped himself and got his ass beat by the two &quot;weakest&quot; PCs whom he'd been dicking over most of the game. Good chatharsis. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast #2: Logam Moore<br /> <br /> Logan was a Wendigo, a shepherd of the natural world who taught people that the wild was a scary, primal place where they didn't belong. I believe his pitch line was &quot;The wild is a cold and vicious place, stay in your cities, you don't belong here&quot;. The game being set in Antarctica meant Logan had a lot of opportunity to 'educate'. Logan sat at the edge, he rarely spoke and indeed was rarely seen by anyone. He haunted other PCs, murdered NPCs and threatened everyone with a cold, vicious terror of the outdoors. But, in the end Logan was also heroic, being the only PC who could confront and defeat the Abyss tainted Mastigos (another PC...me) who was busily damning the entire expedition for his own, impossible salvation.<br /> <br /> Did that make Logan good? No. He was a mass murderer. Yet his actions saved hundreds, and in the end gave the 'villain' his comeuppance. </div> </div> </div>Both the above characters were <b>great, </b>they challenged the players and the narrative, and taught lessons the old fashion way: brutally. That's where Beast excels, as visions of human nature without self-delusion. Don't try to shoehorn in why the Beast is a good guy, he's not. Even if he happens to do 'good' (if you can ever call terrorizing others good) he's not doing it for good reasons, he's doing it because it sates his primal thirst. That's part of the splat's charm, in a world where other monsters obsess over their humanity Beasts are monsters without regret, begging the question of what's so wrong with that?<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR</b>: Beasts are great antagonists, and good PCs for games where interparty conflict and antagonistic players are welcome. They shed light on the monstrousness of other splats and pose serious questions about the concepts of good and evil. Don't try to make them into good guys, that's not their point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 06-06-2016, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:54:46-07:00","id":908157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908145#post908145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a couple questions: in the final draft, have Beasts always been Beasts and eventually metaphysically realize that (much like the First Change of a Werewolf), or are they normal mortals that one day get hollowed out and inhabited by a Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;hollowed out&quot; perspective has basically no actual support in part due to the undercurrent of fatalism in mainstream Beast society and a not-uncommon background of playing Cassandra with secondhand accounts of prophetic nightmares and in part due to that second bit precluding any pretension of being &quot;normal.&quot; The mortals that go on to become Beasts have always had nightmares that touched the Primordial Dream deeply enough to glean clear understanding of varying levels of danger in their lives from the symbolism of those dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Dropped preposition. 06-06-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:53:29-07:00","id":908242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908059#post908059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Heroes have been beefed up, apparently with an eye to making them available as PCs in a later supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as Matt remains Beast's line developer, he has said this will categorically never happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:56:42-07:00","id":908244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908112#post908112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf So if I'm understanding you correctly, Beasts are like Sin-Eaters, except that they're \u201cClaimed\u201d by fear-spirits? (One of the problems I had during the KS was that I could never quite get a handle on <i>what a Beast is</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters are resurrected humans being Ridden by a weirdly twisted Geist.<br /> <br /> Beasts are human shells with monster souls.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T03:57:09-07:00","id":908245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908242#post908242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as Matt remains Beast's line developer, he has said this will categorically never happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/olB0hX5.gif?noredirect\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T06:51:25-07:00","id":908306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908242#post908242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as Matt remains Beast's line developer, he has said this will categorically never happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth reinforcing: This.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:13:17-07:00","id":908318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=907987#post907987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my main issue with Beast is that it seems to be treading a lot of the same water that Vampire does; &quot;I'm a hungry monster who teaches mortals with fear&quot; has been the schtick of the Lancea Sanctum for over a decade now, and vampires are a lot easier to grok than incarnate fears of humanity who may have always been you or maybe ate your soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mean, that's like saying Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and Beast are the same because they're all highly territorial.<br /> <br /> Vampire is an extremely physical game. No matter how much you drink, how many drugs you do, how many people you fuck, you're nothing more than a walking corpse. You cling to your touchstones in order to maintain some semblance of humanity, but where does that leave you when your touchstones grow old and die, and what does it say about you if your only link to your old life is your own gravestone? You hunt people down to drink their blood because that's the only thing that can satisfy the hunger, but no matter how much warm blood you drink, it's just a reminder that you're a stone-cold corpse. <br /> <br /> In comparison, Beast is entirely psychological. You're born from primordial nightmares, a reminder that fear, much like pain, is necessary to humanity's survival. You dwell in the Astral realm and breach the barrier that separates it from the physical world. You hunger, but not for a false semblance of life. You feed on fear, anxieties, insecurities, and on the epiphanies people have when they're pushed to their breaking point. You're the Ghost of Christmas Future pointing at Ebenezer Scrooge's gravestone; it doesn't matter that he's going to die, it matters that he's confronting his death. Maybe you really do care and you're doing him a favour and giving him a chance to turn his life around. Maybe you don't, and you just want to ruin him to satisfy the Horror. That part is up to you. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:23:29-07:00","id":908321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908137#post908137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, don't you actually choose it now?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908145#post908145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a couple questions: in the final draft, have Beasts always been Beasts and eventually metaphysically realize that (much like the First Change of a Werewolf), or are they normal mortals that one day get hollowed out and inhabited by a Horror? .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good question. One problem I feel the finished product has is that in trying to balance the initial version with the significant revisions that came as a reaction to that it creates several contradictions. In a number places it feels like it wants to have its cake and eat it too, unfortunately to the detriment of overall clarity. One area where I feel this comes up is in Homecoming versus Devouring. Officially Devouring is the new way that Beasts are made, but they don't seem to want to commit to that one hundred percent so several elements suggestive of the Homecoming remain. My personal preference is to excise Homecoming entirely as Devouring is the far more compelling version to me. If one is not aware going in though that they'll have to sort out the text of two different games I can understand how it can come off as very schizophrenic and confusing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:08:11-07:00","id":908492,"title":"","content":"I don't feel the Devouring is meaningfully different from the Homecoming in its core significance or workings (although the book's introduction does give a different idea compared to where it's actually explained), particularly considering that the participation of another Horror is heavily toned as something that facilitates a natural process and is not responsible for it. You're required to be of a certain supernatural persuasion from the onset to undergo the Devouring at all; see Satchel's post above for a more detailed explanation of that factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-06-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:20:48-07:00","id":908502,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I went over that section again while digging for Heroes, and I reminded myself that basically other Horrors are there to incubate, in the way nightmare symbols do best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:47:52-07:00","id":908567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908492#post908492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're required to be of a certain supernatural persuasion from the onset to undergo the Devouring at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where I feel in trying to have it both ways it accomplishes neither to satisfaction. It started as an innate template (like Werewolf), then morphed into an inflicted template (like Vampire or Changeling), but still carried over caveats that imply you were always destined to be Devoured while also saying that you were given a choice about it. Its all over the place and I feel it would benefit from picking a spot and staying there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:56:27-07:00","id":908581,"title":"","content":"I think at its heart Beast is about subverting the trope. The old tale of hero-kills-monster has been done over and over again (and indeed, we have Hunter for it in CoD) but what if it wasn't clear cut? What if the monster at least <i>tried </i>to live its life straight? Does it really deserve to die for what it is?<br /> <br /> Beasts have no natural inclination toward being good - and they can easily become very, very bad. But while the hunger drives them, they are always in control of their actions, and how they shape the world around them is, to a large extant, their decision. The tagline of the game is &quot;A storytelling game of endless hunger&quot;. In many ways the game is about addiction, or about madness - that nasty part of you you can never excise, but which you have to deal with one way or another.<br /> <br /> That, plus you can be a m************ dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:04:32-07:00","id":908602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908567#post908567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's where I feel in trying to have it both ways it accomplishes neither to satisfaction. It started as an innate template (like Werewolf), then morphed into an inflicted template (like Vampire or Changeling), but still carried over caveats that imply you were always destined to be Devoured while also saying that you were given a choice about it. Its all over the place and I feel it would benefit from picking a spot and staying there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf edition-shifts and fandom myopia regarding what gaining the &quot;inflicted&quot; templates actually entails notwithstanding, we're talking about a splat that wrestles with inevitability on a fairly frequent basis and claims its strongest thematic connections to gods and monsters of the sort that generally decide who becomes a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> The &quot;choice&quot; is a formality. Whether you are or aren't going to turn into a Beast is ultimately out of your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:28:41-07:00","id":908621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908602#post908602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf edition-shifts and fandom myopia regarding what gaining the &amp;quot;inflicted&amp;quot; templates actually entails notwithstanding, we're talking about a splat that wrestles with inevitability on a fairly frequent basis and claims its strongest thematic connections to gods and monsters of the sort that generally decide who becomes a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;choice&amp;quot; is a formality. Whether you are or aren't going to turn into a Beast is ultimately out of your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the book it specifically says that although a Beast may offer to Devour another, they are under no obligation to, not to mention spontaneous Devourings, and the only true choice the nascent Beast has is whether or not to turn around and face the monster. And if someone's systematically destroying your life to get you to do it, chances are you'll eventually break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:55:57-07:00","id":908639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908112#post908112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf So if I'm understanding you correctly, Beasts are like Sin-Eaters, except that they're \u201cClaimed\u201d by fear-spirits? (One of the problems I had during the KS was that I could never quite get a handle on <i>what a Beast is</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>A Beast is a protean horror, a thing of nightmares that's (literally) clawed its way out of the collective unconsciousness, and found itself a human host. How much of the human host remains is open for debate, but the result is something that resembles a lot of different splats: a mage who's Awakening went horribly wrong, a goetic demon with a human body, a Sin-Eater with a focus on fear, a nightmarish cousin of the Gentry . . .<br /> <br /> Which is appropriate. Beasts claim to be the <i>original</i> monsters of the nWoD, and that all the other splats are descended from them - a theory that's hard to dispute, given all the template changes they can experience. Many fans, though, have noted that the other splats could've given rise <i>to</i> the Beasts, as they gave humanity new things to fear.<br /> <br /> Whatever the truth, Beasts have a primal tie to the other splats. They can boost their powers through Mother's Kiss, or feed right alongside their &quot;cousins&quot;. Exploiting their protean nature, they can mimic the auras (et al) of the other splats, becoming virtually indistinguishable from them. Heck, Beasts can even develop powers that approximate those of the other splats. Beasts are living nightmares, after all, and nightmares have a disturbing habit of bending the rules . . .<br /> <br /> The result is a splat that draws spell-like powers from the collective subconscious (rather than the objective truths of Mage), that can hunt the Shadow or Hedge like a native, and has a disturbing fascination with the darker aspects of the other splats. And only a fool would challenge a Beast in their Lair, where they can take full advantage of their monstrous side . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:00:24-07:00","id":908679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908602#post908602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf edition-shifts and fandom myopia regarding what gaining the &quot;inflicted&quot; templates actually entails notwithstanding, we're talking about a splat that wrestles with inevitability on a fairly frequent basis and claims its strongest thematic connections to gods and monsters of the sort that generally decide who becomes a supernatural being.<br /> <br /> The &quot;choice&quot; is a formality. Whether you are or aren't going to turn into a Beast is ultimately out of your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908621#post908621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the book it specifically says that although a Beast may offer to Devour another, they are under no obligation to, not to mention spontaneous Devourings, and the only true choice the nascent Beast has is whether or not to turn around and face the monster. And if someone's systematically destroying your life to get you to do it, chances are you'll eventually break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which begs the question of why choice even comes up in the text. I'm all for &quot;predestination is awful&quot; and &quot;choice is an illusion&quot; but said illusion should serve a purpose. To me it feels more like they tried to preserve the Homecoming hidden inside the Devouring, when really in my opinion they should have committed to the thematic shift that creates. I can get behind the idea of one being always destined for the Devouring, in a kind of Calvinist horror sort of way, but I feel its a discussion that should be happening more in-universe than laid out in authorial voice. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:18:33-07:00","id":908692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908145#post908145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a couple questions: in the final draft, have Beasts always been Beasts and eventually metaphysically realize that (much like the First Change of a Werewolf), or are they normal mortals that one day get hollowed out and inhabited by a Horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unclear. In the original draft, Beasts were always monsters in human flesh (hence the use of terms like &quot;homecoming&quot;). In the new version . . . well, the new version is pushing the idea that they are, or were, humans who bonded with their &quot;Horror&quot; after touching the primal Darkness a bit too closely. However, the new version doesn't rule out the original concept, either, and some Beasts claim they were always monsters.<br /> <br /> Whether the human being actually survives the process, or whether a Beast is just a monster wearing the human (and its memories/personality) like a suit, is left up to the players/Storyteller to decide<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How intelligent is a Horror; is it just a hunger and a couple notable traits, or could you settle down and talk to it with deep enough meditation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's unclear. We don't have rules for a &quot;pure&quot; Horror yet, only ones that have become Beasts. Those are pretty mindless when the Beast is out of the Lair, although they seem to respect deals the Beast has made, and - you know - not eat invited guests. Its possible that the Horror's higher mental functions are permanently intertwined with its Beast, leaving it more-or-less animalistic in its absence. Or its possible the Horror never had any to being with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the final origin for Heroes, and are they still utterly demonized or were they made more humane?</div> </div> </div> </div> Heroes are now people who've touched the Primordial Dream (like Beasts), and taken on the mythic role of champions. And yes, they were made more humane. Heroes can still end up the obsessed fanatics from the original draft, but that's not a prerequisite. However, the average Beast may not know that's a possibility - they have to deal primarily with the crazed kind, after all.<br /> <br /> If it helps, you can think of a Horror as a super-Goetic demon, a tangible manifestation of a problem that humanity is trying to grapple with: nuclear weapons, child abuse, pollution, Ebola . . . Its job is to keep humanity focused on the problem it represents, and make sure they don't forget about it. Ever time a Beast feeds, it forces humanity - at least for a moment - to think about the problem that gave birth to its Horror, rather than sink back into complacency.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Hero is a tangible manifestation of humanity's effort to <i>solve</i> that problem. They draw their powers from humanity's effort to develop new vaccines, care more about each other, work for nuclear disarmament . . .<br /> <br /> Theoretically, the two should be compatible - the Beast keeps humanity focused on the problem, and the Hero(es) lead the local humans in efforts to resolve the underlying issue. Unfortunately, that's gotten corrupted somewhere along the line. And many Heroes think the &quot;solution&quot; is to just start killing Beasts. Sure, that stops the Beasts' hunts . . . but it also takes humanity's focus off the underlying problem (a Beast preying on the populace is a symptom, not the cause). So the underlying issue will keep killing people, and generating new Beasts . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly, what would the average supernatural get out of a Beast's company? I can't imagine the Lost feeling comfortable around something both so profoundly other and also so borderline abusive, and even the book itself says that Mummies and Beasts don't really have a reason to hang around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power. Sanctuary. Friendship. Beasts really do see the other splats as family, and enjoy having them around. And being wanted is incredibly attractive . . . There's also the fact that a Beast can boost powers via Mother's Kiss, and a powerful Beast is virtually a god in its Lair.<br /> <br /> If you get a chance to look at the book, I recommend looking at the sections on how the other splats view Beasts - its well written, with a lot of good color. But here are some ideas:<ul><li>What vampire wouldn't want an ally who approves of their bloodlust, and who can walk in broad daylight? Plus, a Beast's Lair makes a great safe house - few beings know how to get into one, let alone get past the defenses. And some Lairs are shrouded in permanent darkness . . .</li> <li>Even if they don't realize what they are (at first), a Beast makes a great ally to a party of mages. Many Beasts are just as obsessed with the Mysteries as the average mage, and have their own (Paradox-free) powers. Plus, if the mages <i>do </i>realize the nature of their ally, they've got a brand new set of Mysteries to study.</li> <li>Beasts are immune to Disquiet. They can't stop it from bothering ordinary humans, but they can walk with a Promethean during their Pilgrimage.</li> </ul>As for the changelings:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\"><b>THE VIEW FROM WITHOUT:<br /> MICAH, OGRE EARTHBONES OF THE SUMMER COURT</b></div> <br /> Here\u2019s what I know. I pulled myself out of a goddamn swamp, so filthy I thought I\u2019d never see my real skin again, mouth full of peat and eyes burning, and Nyx offered me a hand up. I went back to my house and found another guy wearing my clothes and kissing my wife, so Nyx lured the fucker to the swamp so I could send him back.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know what she does. I know she chases people down, jumps on them from rooftops, marks them. I know it, and it turns my stomach a little. But you know what? I asked her, &quot;you never take them? Never take them away.&quot; And without missing a beat, she says, &quot;god, no. They get to go home. I just want them to look around a little more.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019m OK with that. Wish I\u2019d looked around a little more, myself</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of changelings are (at least initially) afraid of Beasts. But a Beast is one of the few beings in existence that the Gentry respect, and deal with as (near) equals. And taking a changeling from a Beast's Lair would just be <i>rude</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have to wonder if the initial feeling that the game was about being an abuser still remains, because that soured me on things far more than the general What Do We Do? feeling or hamfisted attempts at feeling progressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read the feeding rules, I don't think Beasts would turn abusive. Oh, sure, they could try . . . but I think they'd quickly use up their victim. A Beast doesn't feed on pain, per se. Instead, they feed on <i>reaction</i>. A Collector sates their hunger by the emotional value of the treasure they steal, a Nemesis on the shock their prey feels when they're punished (and possibly society's reaction to that punishment). If a Beast kept preying on the same target, they'd eventually beat the ability to feel out of them (rendering them completely unsuitable for future feedings).<br /> <br /> Batman keeps coming up as an example of a Beast, because he simply works very well as a Nemesis (a Beast with a Hunger for Punishment). Bruce Wayne doesn't want to hurt anyone, he just wants them to be too scared of Batman to commit a crime. That's why he goes out every night, and beats up crooks. Every bad guy who wets himself when he sees the Bat signal is another meal for him. And the more untouchable his target feels, the better the meal is (i.e. the more Satiety/power he gains)<br /> <br /> Mind if I ask you a question, though? What is it about <i>Beast</i> that makes it so much worse than the other White Wolf/Onyx Path games? Other lines have slave raids, human cannibalism, rules that encourage players to turn people into mind-controlled junkies . . . In light of that, I don't really see what the issue is with <i>Beast.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 06-06-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:44:29-07:00","id":908709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908679#post908679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which begs the question of why choice even comes up in the text. I'm all for &quot;predestination is awful&quot; and &quot;choice is an illusion&quot; but said illusion should serve a purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feeds into the final draft's stronger thematic basis for how Kinship contrasts with Hunger and relates to the wider world; the Beasts less likely to offer a choice are the ones who are more strongly aligned with the drives their Mother gave them, and those Beasts tend to be the more powerful specimens who keep to their Lairs and more fully embrace their roles as monsters.<br /> <br /> The younger Children more often haven't been driven to that excess yet and stay pliable to others' wishes for longer besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:21:14-07:00","id":908734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908709#post908709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feeds into the final draft's stronger thematic basis for how Kinship contrasts with Hunger and relates to the wider world; the Beasts less likely to offer a choice are the ones who are more strongly aligned with the drives their Mother gave them, and those Beasts tend to be the more powerful specimens who keep to their Lairs and more fully embrace their roles as monsters.<br /> <br /> The younger Children more often haven't been driven to that excess yet and stay pliable to others' wishes for longer besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really answer the question though. Why present an explicitly illusory choice in text? What does a false belief in the choice add to the game?<br /> <br /> EDIT: To make my own question a little clearer. The idea of a false choice would make more sense if there were factors in the game that believed the choice to be real, like individuals pointing to Beasts and claiming they were debased humans who chose wickedness (signing their name in the black book and what-not), while the truth is at once more tragic and much darker. Pretty much everyone already treats Beasts as being innately abominable and worthy of scorn for that reason alone though, so the idea of a false choice doesn't really do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 06-06-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:28:27-07:00","id":908738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908734#post908734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really answer the question though. Why present an explicitly illusory choice in text?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many choices are illusory and all-but-explicit and I was under the impression from the way you were talking that you were aware of what assuming this particular type of choice was entirely genuine implied about those who made it with full knowledge of its consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does a false belief in the choice add to the game? </div> </div> </div>You are asking what the purpose of hope is and I'm not sure how I'm supposed to explain that besides pointing again to the generally despairing framework of fatalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:43:04-07:00","id":908748,"title":"","content":"Yeah, again, having re-read the pertinent sections earlier today, I'm siding with Satchel on this one-in line with the themes, a Beast's choice is illusory. The Beast was always for this thing, and their main choice is to sink or swim to the bottom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:43:08-07:00","id":908749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908738#post908738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many choices are illusory and all-but-explicit and I was under the impression from the way you were talking that you were aware of what assuming this particular type of choice was entirely genuine implied about those who made it with full knowledge of its consequences.<br /> <br /> You are asking what the purpose of hope is and I'm not sure how I'm supposed to explain that besides pointing again to the generally despairing framework of fatalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me try and lay it out more explicitly.<br /> <br /> We are presented with the idea that people are fated for the Devouring. For the most part this is presented as an objective fact.<br /> <br /> Simultaneously we are presented with the idea that some Beasts are offered a choice.<br /> <br /> If the first part is objectively true what purpose does the second part serve? What <i>specifically</i>?<br /> <br /> If we want to say that it is <i>not</i> objectively true that Devouring is predestined then wiggle room exists and there is less of a problem because it allows for the possibility of the choice being legitimate both in terms of those who weren't fated for it making a deliberate decision about their monstrosity and those who were not fated for it but were not given a choice. <br /> <br /> If we maintain that it is objectively true though we must follow through with &quot;It is important that some people believe there was a choice, even though there was not one, because...&quot; and I've not really seen anything that fills in the blank. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:50:19-07:00","id":908757,"title":"","content":"To misquote the Lutece's on this one, &quot;The mind of the subject will desperately struggle to create <i>meaning</i> where none exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> The acceptance-and possible defiance-of this quote is the heart of Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:54:25-07:00","id":908759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908749#post908749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simultaneously we are presented with the idea that some Beasts are offered a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are presented with the idea that some Beasts <i>were</i> offered a choice.<br /> <br /> Some deep-dreamers <i>are</i> offered a choice.<br /> <br /> Where you are tripping up is in conflating these two, discounting what it means that someone <i>would choose</i> to be Devoured and why, and ignoring that the aspects of fatalism that Beasts truck with include &quot;what has happened <i>was going to happen</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the anthropic principle of RPGs: what has happened before must ultimately produce what now is.<br /> <br /> Or, as Beast puts it: You don't choose your family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-06-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:57:49-07:00","id":908761,"title":"","content":"No I understand the distinction you're drawing, you're just still failing to actually answer the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:58:51-07:00","id":908762,"title":"","content":"I agree with Arc here, for me the importance to many Beasts to have that agency in their existence is incredibly important. Knowing as readers that it is (in some or all cases depending) an illusion underscores the deeper ideas the game itself is trying to get at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 06-06-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:04:55-07:00","id":908765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908757#post908757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To misquote the Lutece's on this one, &quot;The mind of the subject will desperately struggle to create <i>meaning</i> where none exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> The acceptance-and possible defiance-of this quote is the heart of Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is something I'd prefer be under discussion in-character without the looming weight of metaphysical certainty that comes with internalizing the secret knowledge of authorial fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:07:14-07:00","id":908766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908761#post908761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I understand the distinction you're drawing, you're just still failing to actually answer the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your question is &quot;Why do people prefer to think they have control over their lives even in situations where they do not?&quot;<br /> <br /> You appear unwilling to accept &quot;because it allows them to think of themselves as people&quot; as an answer and you've brought in a definition of fate that is incompatible with how predestination is actually being used as a leg for the notion that the Devouring not <i>having been</i> predestined is &quot;less of a problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't &quot;actually answer&quot; a question that isn't actually the question it claims to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:16:14-07:00","id":908771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908765#post908765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is something I'd prefer be under discussion in-character without the looming weight of metaphysical certainty that comes with internalizing the secret knowledge of authorial fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the choice being false is for when creating a character whole hog, if you are getting the beast template during play, well then i think it is more real of a choice (at least i made it more real of a choice for the PC that wanted to become a beast in one of my games) as to what the beast you are thinking about playing feels about their devouring/homecoming, that is kind of up to you in my eyes. one character i have definitely viewed it as a choice, for the other it was her birthright. neither is wrong, it just changes the way your character sees him or herself... at least thats my feeling on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:16:37-07:00","id":908772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908765#post908765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is something I'd prefer be under discussion in-character without the looming weight of metaphysical certainty that comes with internalizing the secret knowledge of authorial fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the question why some Horrors seem to offer a choice and some don't?<br /> <br /> Because collective humanity has desperately struggled to create meaning where there is none. Anything Astral up to the Omphalos Stone is nothing more than the collected sound and fury of a species, their Horrors nothing more than the faces they make to subjugate a world they have no real power over. Mimicry and hollow echoes are to be expected, even in warped mirrors and twisted sound chambers.<br /> <br /> At least, that's one way to read the coin.<br /> <br /> This presumes I'm understanding your question right, of course. Given how you've argued, I'm not so sure it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:42:31-07:00","id":908783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908766#post908766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your question is &quot;Why do people prefer to think they have control over their lives even in situations where they do not?&quot;<br /> <br /> You appear unwilling to accept &quot;because it allows them to think of themselves as people&quot; as an answer and you've brought in a definition of fate that is incompatible with how predestination is actually being used as a leg for the notion that the Devouring not <i>having been</i> predestined is &quot;less of a problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't &quot;actually answer&quot; a question that isn't actually the question it claims to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to climb down off that horse? It's pretty high up. <br /> <br /> That wasn't my question at all. I'm asking how the idea of an illusory choice adds to the game, what impact does it have on playing the game other than being metagame knowledge?<br /> <br /> Also, you don't get to tell me what my question is. Don't do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:48:54-07:00","id":908786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908772#post908772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the question why some Horrors seem to offer a choice and some don't?<br /> <br /> Because collective humanity has desperately struggled to create meaning where there is none. Anything Astral up to the Omphalos Stone is nothing more than the collected sound and fury of a species, their Horrors nothing more than the faces they make to subjugate a world they have no real power over. Mimicry and hollow echoes are to be expected, even in warped mirrors and twisted sound chambers.<br /> <br /> At least, that's one way to read the coin.<br /> <br /> This presumes I'm understanding your question right, of course. Given how you've argued, I'm not so sure it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually kind of a separate discussion. More about preference than anything else. My contention there is that the idea of predestination ought to be presented as a popular theory rather than as an undeniable fact, with the debate over it occurring within the context of the game itself. When an explanation is laid out in game text that is not told through the voice of a particular character (i.e. it is presumed to be in the voice of the omniscient author) it tends to be taken at face value and treated as truth. Even if your character has no way of knowing it, the knowledge of that truth still tends to seep into the game and bias the conversation over it in-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:58:03-07:00","id":908792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908786#post908786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually kind of a separate discussion. More about preference than anything else. My contention there is that the idea of predestination ought to be presented as a popular theory rather than as an undeniable fact, with the debate over it occurring within the context of the game itself. When an explanation is laid out in game text that is not told through the voice of a particular character (i.e. it is presumed to be in the voice of the omniscient author) it tends to be taken at face value and treated as truth. Even if your character has no way of knowing it, the knowledge of that truth still tends to seep into the game and bias the conversation over it in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find it much easier to not treat anything in the rules aside from mechanics as &quot;Truth&quot; coming from a &quot;omniscient author&quot; it interferes too much with my fun in the game and leads me too far into pointless arguments based on something written by a freelancer, and edited by the poeple who rushed out to read it first thing(this is admittedly a over-gereralization of the OPP process which is awesome). Instead, it is all suggestion, and open to re-skinning, (and even mechanics need fiddling with every once and a while)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:01:11-07:00","id":908794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908792#post908792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I find it much easier to not treat anything in the rules aside from mechanics as &quot;Truth&quot; coming from a &quot;omniscient author&quot; it interferes too much with my fun in the game and leads me too far into pointless arguments based on something written by a freelancer, and edited by the poeple who rushed out to read it first thing(this is admittedly a over-gereralization of the OPP process which is awesome). Instead, it is all suggestion, and open to re-skinning, (and even mechanics need fiddling with every once and a while)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which from my perspective merely reinforces that great care should be taken with the way in which information is presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:50:52-07:00","id":908861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908783#post908783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Care to climb down off that horse? It's pretty high up.<br /> <br /> That wasn't my question at all. [\u2026]<br /> <br /> Also, you don't get to tell me what my question is. Don't do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel that I've mischaracterized your question you can say so without pulling the frankly useless &quot;Satch is arrogant&quot; card, particularly when the worst I did was imply that you weren't listening to the whole &quot;post-facto fatalism&quot; spiel on the evidence of you presenting an argument that directly ignored it.<br /> <br /> Making an ultimatum banning declarative statements of understanding just because you were misunderstood does very little to clarify your portion of the discussion into something that can be engaged with constructively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm asking how the idea of an illusory choice adds to the game, what impact does it have on playing the game other than being metagame knowledge? </div> </div> </div>And &quot;the idea of an illusory choice&quot; is only actually relevant in the abstract as part of the larger thematic framework of how the Begotten tend to think as a consequence of frequent exposure to the most desperate and deautonomized elements of the supernatural world.<br /> <br /> The impact it has on playing the game is that most Beasts who've been around the block are going to recognize that there are a lot of things that can't be helped, many of them due to having already happened (or worse, being necessary to allow some sympathetic actor to live or suffer less), and that a significant majority of monsters did not ask to be as they are and do not have the luxury of actively pursuing a way out.<br /> <br /> It's &quot;metagame knowledge&quot; of the same sort as &quot;Luna makes people into werewolves in a fashion that their culture attributes to her being a capricious god of fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> The nearest thing to your &quot;the omniscient narrator said it so it must be objectively true!&quot; bit comes as a rider on the line that essentially just says &quot;a Beast can't not be a Beast&quot; and frames the non-choice as &quot;they're choosing to acknowledge what they are in full, not choosing to be a monster,&quot; not &quot;whether or not they're Devoured is only in their hands as far as their elder sibling is willing to honor their refusal,&quot; which is part of the section talking about how the Devouring tends to happen in those cases where another Beast comes across a deep-dreamer by chance.<br /> <br /> In-context the thing you're worrying about is a non-issue because every &quot;caveat that impl[ies] you were always destined to be Devoured&quot; is presented as an in-character personal/cultural view based in the fact that if you're Devoured, you undergo the Devouring. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-07-2016, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T01:37:36-07:00","id":908983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908692#post908692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically, the two should be compatible - the Beast keeps humanity focused on the problem, and the Hero(es) lead the local humans in efforts to resolve the underlying issue. Unfortunately, that's gotten corrupted somewhere along the line. And many Heroes think the &quot;solution&quot; is to just start killing Beasts. Sure, that stops the Beasts' hunts . . . but it also takes humanity's focus off the underlying problem (a Beast preying on the populace is a symptom, not the cause). So the underlying issue will keep killing people, and generating new Beasts . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just say how much I like how succinct and well stated this explanation is. Good work, One Vorlon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T02:11:13-07:00","id":908989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908783#post908783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That wasn't my question at all. I'm asking how the idea of an illusory choice adds to the game, what impact does it have on playing the game other than being metagame knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no illusory choice. Some Beasts claim to have been born this way. Others say they chose it. Whether your character had choice or not is up to you.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, no character ever has choice - the player is making a Beast character in a game called Beast. The character's fate was sealed when the players picked up the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:43:55-07:00","id":909113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908861#post908861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In-context the thing you're worrying about is a non-issue because every &quot;caveat that impl[ies] you were always destined to be Devoured&quot; is presented as an in-character personal/cultural view based in the fact that if you're Devoured, you undergo the Devouring. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's where we're getting our wires crossed. I'm fine with that. I honestly had assumed that was the way it was, something seemingly backed up by a freelancer (though if I'm mistaken and he wants to correct his meaning please do.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I brought it up as part of acknowledging ambiguity in the text in response to a question from one of the OPs. To which you said,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908602#post908602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;choice&quot; is a formality. Whether you are or aren't going to turn into a Beast is ultimately out of your hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>and<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908759#post908759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are presented with the idea that some Beasts <i>were</i> offered a choice.<br /> <br /> Some deep-dreamers are offered a choice.<br /> <br /> Where you are tripping up is in conflating these two, discounting what it means that someone <i>would choose</i> to be Devoured and why, and ignoring that the aspects of fatalism that Beasts truck with include &quot;what has happened was going to happen.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which seemed to indicate you felt there was no ambiguity and that the predestination of being Devoured was objectively true in the text, which I found confusing. So the back and forth went based on the idea that it was true because that was what I thought your thesis was. I may have been mistaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908861#post908861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you feel that I've mischaracterized your question you can say so without pulling the frankly useless &quot;Satch is arrogant&quot; card, particularly when the worst I did was imply that you weren't listening to the whole &quot;post-facto fatalism&quot; spiel on the evidence of you presenting an argument that directly ignored it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have no idea if &quot;Satch is arrogant.&quot; I don't know you. What you <i>have</i> been is rather obtuse and condescending, in my view. I apologize if you felt my rebuff was unduly brusque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 06-07-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:45:26-07:00","id":909334,"title":"","content":"Erm.... you're mixing up two different posters there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:50:02-07:00","id":909338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909334#post909334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm.... you're mixing up two different posters there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually, I was using the other quote to illustrate a point, but I have removed it for the sake of clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:52:33-07:00","id":909341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=908692#post908692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind if I ask you a question, though? What is it about <i>Beast</i> that makes it so much worse than the other White Wolf/Onyx Path games? Other lines have slave raids, human cannibalism, rules that encourage players to turn people into mind-controlled junkies . . . In light of that, I don't really see what the issue is with <i>Beast.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail the current thread of conversation, but this point stuck out to me. <br /> <br /> I see this particular complaint get thrown around, that Beasts are inherently &quot;more evil&quot; then the other CRoD supernaturals, both in the fluff and how the mechanics support and encourage Beasts to act more &quot;evil&quot;, while the others do not. <br /> <br /> ...aside from, y'know, the whole blood drinking thing in Vampire, or the consuming a human's soul from Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:55:56-07:00","id":909344,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm wondering if Satiety not having any &quot;Breaking Points&quot; like Humanity or even Cover have anything to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:08:15-07:00","id":909356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909344#post909344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm wondering if Satiety not having any &amp;quot;Breaking Points&amp;quot; like Humanity or even Cover have anything to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always found this design choice interesting, as it implies that Beasts have either already fallen to monstrosity and become utter horrors whose only moral direction is that which they impose on themselves or that they are, in a way, the splat which is closest to true (real-world) humanity, in that they are free to decide what they are and will become. The thing is that if a Beast is a monster, it is because he chooses to indulge his darker side. If he is a murderer, it is because he chose not to satisfy his Hunger in a gentler way. If he goes mad, it is because his mind could not handle the stress of his life, not because some outside factor such as the integrity of his soul, his closeness to humanity or his balance between the spirit and human worlds. A Beast is, in all ways but the Devouring itself, what he has made of himself.<br /> <br /> And I would like to say that I'm not getting involved in the 'choice vs Fate' argument with this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:26:15-07:00","id":909364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909341#post909341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to derail the current thread of conversation, but this point stuck out to me.<br /> <br /> I see this particular complaint get thrown around, that Beasts are inherently &quot;more evil&quot; then the other CRoD supernaturals, both in the fluff and how the mechanics support and encourage Beasts to act more &quot;evil&quot;, while the others do not.<br /> <br /> ...aside from, y'know, the whole blood drinking thing in Vampire, or the consuming a human's soul from Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is the obligate abuse (mental, if not physical) that Beasts conduct. There really is no way out of it - any and every Beasts' existence means someone is getting hurt. Even if they don't &quot;feed&quot; directly, their Horror will on its own eventually. Even their &quot;Family Dinner&quot; means someone gets hurt by proxy (either their monster buddy's victim, or the monster themselves through encouraging self-destructive behavior).<br /> <br /> Vampires need blood, but they don't have to take it - it can be offered, and there are other methods for Vitae acquisition.<br /> Werewolves don't need to harm people for their Hunts.<br /> Mages <i>really</i> don't need to inflict harm to survive.<br /> Prometheans' harm is more incidental, and can be manage to the point they don't inflict major Disquiet or Wastelands.<br /> Changelings can farm Goblin Fruit, or low level harvest Glamor.<br /> Sin-Eaters don't need to cause any harm (depending on Archetype).<br /> Mummies can minimize the exposure others have to Sybaris, and refrain from causing harm at higher Memory.<br /> Demon's don't need to inflict harm either. (They don't need to &quot;consume souls&quot;, and in fact some/many refrain from doing so)<br /> <br /> Beasts are about the only supernatural where they <i>only</i> exist through harming others, rather than it being a risk or byproduct. That they try to justify their abuse through a &quot;teaching&quot; metaphor that even they largely don't take seriously doesn't really help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:53:41-07:00","id":909390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909364#post909364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is the obligate abuse (mental, if not physical) that Beasts conduct. There really is no way out of it - any and every Beasts' existence means someone is getting hurt. Even if they don't &quot;feed&quot; directly, their Horror will on its own eventually. Even their &quot;Family Dinner&quot; means someone gets hurt by proxy (either their monster buddy's victim, or the monster themselves through encouraging self-destructive behavior).<br /> <br /> Vampires need blood, but they don't have to take it - it can be offered, and there are other methods for Vitae acquisition.<br /> Werewolves don't need to harm people for their Hunts.<br /> Mages <i>really</i> don't need to inflict harm to survive.<br /> Prometheans' harm is more incidental, and can be manage to the point they don't inflict major Disquiet or Wastelands.<br /> Changelings can farm Goblin Fruit, or low level harvest Glamor.<br /> Sin-Eaters don't need to cause any harm (depending on Archetype).<br /> Mummies can minimize the exposure others have to Sybaris, and refrain from causing harm at higher Memory.<br /> Demon's don't need to inflict harm either. (They don't need to &quot;consume souls&quot;, and in fact some/many refrain from doing so)<br /> <br /> Beasts are about the only supernatural where they <i>only</i> exist through harming others, rather than it being a risk or byproduct. That they try to justify their abuse through a &quot;teaching&quot; metaphor that even they largely don't take seriously doesn't really help.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is an extremely important part of the game though. Beast is a game about feeding (more so than even Vampire); and it's still a horror game. In a horror game about feeding, the feeding needs to be horrific. The stories the game tell come from dealing with that fact, both in-character and in a more general sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:56:55-07:00","id":909392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909390#post909390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think this is an extremely important part of the game though. Beast is a game about feeding (more so than even Vampire); and it's still a horror game. In a horror game about feeding, the feeding needs to be horrific. The stories the game tell come from dealing with that fact, both in-character and in a more general sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I never said it wasn't important (nay, <i>core</i>) to the game, merely identifying what issues some might have with it, and why Beasts are inherently &quot;worse&quot; than the other games' protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:03:46-07:00","id":909401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909392#post909392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I never said it wasn't important (nay, <i>core</i>) to the game, merely identifying what issues some might have with it, and why Beasts are inherently &quot;worse&quot; than the other games' protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to keep in mind is that Beasts don't really have a choice in the matter either. They <i>have</i> to eat. If they don't not only will they starve but in all likelihood even more people will get hurt.<br /> <br /> I'd also make the argument that a lot of human beings, especially in the developed world, harm and exploit in order to eat. It's just a difference of degrees of separation and the assignment of values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:25:35-07:00","id":909418,"title":"","content":"One thing about the way that Hunger works is that if you try to sate it socially, I've found that a lot of the time you don't have to do things which are that far outside the norm for humans, especially Tyrants and at Low Satiety. Heck, for a Tyrant, earning a promotion over someone else, something that people do all the time, is a High Satiety meal. <br /> <br /> This just reinforces the thing, for me, about how Beasts are, in an odd sort of way, the most human of the splats. The game explores (and explores well) themes of how, all to often, the monsters we denounce are all too close to us. Perhaps that's why the word 'monster' comes from the Latin for 'warn', because these monsters warn us that there is only a thin line separating us from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:26:22-07:00","id":909420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909401#post909401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to keep in mind is that Beasts don't really have a choice in the matter either. They <i>have</i> to eat. If they don't not only will they starve but in all likelihood even more people will get hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know - that the <i>point</i>. A Beast's Horror <b>will</b> eat, and harm <b>will</b> be inflicted. If any of the other supernaturals cause harm, that is often because they chose to do so. For a Beast, it is automatic. In no situation can you have a Beast and no one comes to harm - it is what they are. Now, whether they are at <i>fault</i> for this is a different matter (though if you support the &quot;they chose to become Beasts&quot; model, then they kinda are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T13:38:55-07:00","id":909434,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to claim that Beasts' necessity to cause harm so less harm is inflicted in the larger scheme makes it a justifiable lesser evil, just that like most things its a complicated and uncomfortable mess where no one wins and the moral high ground never really existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:49:39-07:00","id":909542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909390#post909390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is an extremely important part of the game though. Beast is a game about feeding (more so than even Vampire); and it's still a horror game. In a horror game about feeding, the feeding needs to be horrific. The stories the game tell come from dealing with that fact, both in-character and in a more general sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The catch is it's not a personal horror game. It's about you inflicting it. Over and over. Without your guts batting a eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:05:56-07:00","id":909604,"title":"","content":"We have come far afield from selling the game, just noticing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:28:39-07:00","id":909621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909604#post909604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have come far afield from selling the game, just noticing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, nothing wrong with not pointing out any perceived flaws. Mostly to check on if it could be something that the players and Storyteller are willing to work with or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:29:15-07:00","id":909622,"title":"","content":"Beast is Monsters Inc. as made by Guillermo del Toro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:57:21-07:00","id":909703,"title":"","content":"The thing I find most appealing about Beast is the challenge of trying to reconcile the monster to a strong human code of ethics. It's difficult, and it will never be a perfect fit, but to me that's sort of the point and I'm actually glad there's no mechanical carrot for morality, and that it's left up to roleplay. 2e as a whole is much better about making sanity meters instead, but Beast in particular inverts it and encourages you to give into the monster. It demands that you make some concessions, and rewards you for making bigger ones. Being a good person is hard for Beasts.<br /> <br /> All the same, you can play Beasts who are decent people, as long as you're willing to spend most of your time at Low Satiety. You can find ways to feed that are minimally harmful, or that do harm in one way but offset it with good in another. <br /> <br /> The Apex in one of my games is an EMT with the aspect of the grim reaper. She makes sure people know how close they came to the brink and encourages them to be more careful and aware of how fragile life is. Nights when she's not working she joins the Autumn Scarecrows skulking around the bad parts of town, scaring the shit out of would be criminals. She's responsible for a lot of nightmares (bad dreams, but also the power of the same name), hence her position as Apex, but she's also responsible for lowering the city's mortality rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:10:00-07:00","id":909845,"title":"","content":"OK; so if I'm reading this right: <br /> <br /> a Beast is a dragon, kraken, gorgon, or other mythical monster \u2014 but only in her dreams. When she's asleep, she becomes the Horror (which, in Mage terms, is basically a monstrous Daemon) and roams the Primordial Dream, invading peoples' dreams and giving them nightmares in order to sate her Hunger. When she's awake, the Horror lurks in its Lair (analogous to a mage's Oneiros) and she walks the material world as a mostly-normal human with a limited ability to manifest powers based on her Horror (Atavisms) and Lair (by inflicting appropriate Environmental Tilts) and an ability to mess with peoples' minds (Nightmares). In theory, the Beast does what it does to teach people caution, humiity, and other \u201cschool of hard knocks\u201d lessons; in practice, Beasts often ignore that and feed solely to sate their Hunger. <br /> <br /> The ability to physically manifest as her Horror is not something the Beast is capable of, but it <i>is</i> an ability available to the Incarnate Inheritance, the \u201cGood Ending\u201d state that a Beast can work toward, akin to a mage becoming an archmaster \u2014 in fact, it's the <i>defining</i> characteristic of the Incarnate Beast. (the other two Inheritances are \u201cbad endings\u201d where she becomes a feral entity, either by physically dying in a way that leaves the Horror and its Lair intact or by having the Horror abandon the Primordial Dream by, in effect, \u201cClaiming\u201d her physical form.)<br /> <br /> The crossover aspect of the game exists in the Kinship mechanics which allow a Beast to identify, befriend, aid, vicariously feed through, and hide among other supernaturals. As well, Kinship lets the Beast develop additional Nightmares inspired by the other supernaturals that she hangs out with. This Kinship is part of the game's subversion of other games' themes, in that the Beast's view is that their monstrous natures are the best part of them while what's left of their human natures is an impediment. Complementing this is the Beast's relationship with deranged self-described Heroes who see Beasts as little more than creatures to kill in their quest for glory. <b>Beast</b> admits that there are Heroes who are sane and who serve a purpose that's complementary to the Beast's supposed \u201cdrill sergeant from hell\u201d role \u2014 the carrot to the Beast's stick \u2014 but for the most part, it concentrates on those Heroes who slay Beasts. <br /> <br /> Am I right so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:36:18-07:00","id":909857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909845#post909845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Beast is a dragon, kraken, gorgon, or other mythical monster \u2014 but only in her dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the only part that's off. It's not entirely untrue, it's just that the perspective is a bit too clinical for the game. Using Mage terms is kind of telling here. Mages want to study, classify, and categorize things that most Beasts would not see a particular point to drawing lines between. A Beast cannot manifest as a giant dragon of yore in the physical world like they can as a Horror in dreams, but that Horror cannot truly be it's full self in just dreams and has to resort to squeezing into a mortal form and walking the physical world. Basically, Beasts generally are not two separate entities. They're one being that's being pulling in to two different worlds. As you noted the &quot;endings&quot; represent this tug-of-war, with the two &quot;bad&quot; ones being pulled in one direction too hard, and the &quot;good&quot; one managing to find the mid-point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:48:37-07:00","id":909862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909622#post909622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is Monsters Inc. as made by Guillermo del Toro.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including the part where after learning to emphases with Boo, Scully is devastated to see that scaring kids actually hurts them and ends up redesigning the monster's entire economy around laughter instead?<br /> <br /> Because that would be a pretty cool WoD story actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909845#post909845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, the Beast does what it does to teach people caution, humiity, and other \u201cschool of hard knocks\u201d lessons; in practice, Beasts often ignore that and feed solely to sate their Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to keep in mind is that (unless they were added after the kickstarter documents) a Beast does not have any supernatural ability to know who needs a lesson or any supernatural ability to create a good lesson appropriate to the pupil.<br /> <br /> The &quot;neglectful&quot; parent a Beast decides to torment until they realise family is more important than career could in fact be someone who grew up in abject poverty and works so hard to make sure the people they love don't have to ever go hungry.<br /> <br /> There is so much potential for horror in unconsenting therapy (after all there's a reason why medical ethics requires consent) even before you start asking if primordial beings will teach lessons that a modern human would agree with in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-08-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T23:15:23-07:00","id":909877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909845#post909845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> a Beast is a dragon, kraken, gorgon, or other mythical monster \u2014 but only in her dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just in her dreams. A beast can open a primordial pathway at certain locations [1] which allows the beast to merge the area with its lair and transform into the mythical monster it is (with all the associated bonus on the attributes). Anyone in the affected area also ends up in the lair and has to face the monster in flesh. So if a beast is only a monster in her dreams she has the ability to pull other people bodily into her dreams.<br /> <br /> [1] The location must resemble the lair in some ways for this to work, the larger the similarities are the easier it is to open a pathway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:39:10-07:00","id":909901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909364#post909364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is the obligate abuse (mental, if not physical) that Beasts conduct. There really is no way out of it - any and every Beasts' existence means someone is getting hurt. Even if they don't &quot;feed&quot; directly, their Horror will on its own eventually. Even their &quot;Family Dinner&quot; means someone gets hurt by proxy (either their monster buddy's victim, or the monster themselves through encouraging self-destructive behavior).</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts with a Hunger for Prey can explicitly feed on animals at Low Satiety. They'll never be full, but it's enough to stop their Horror from rampaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:15:49-07:00","id":910202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909542#post909542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The catch is it's not a personal horror game. It's about you inflicting it. Over and over. Without your guts batting a eye.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without a game mechanic or you (for a starting character) fairly recently new/newly transformed Beast soul yeah. But the character was still (raised) human right up to then, they would still wrestle with the act they are doing. They would still try to justify it (the lessons paradigm) or target it (the Dexter comparison). Those are personal horror. Just becuase a gameline uses an Integrity analog instead of Integrity doesn't mean they suddenly don't care about their previous morality or worldview, just that it is less important for the game mechanics to strictly re-enforce it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:26:12-07:00","id":910210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910202#post910202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a game mechanic or you (for a starting character) fairly recently new/newly transformed Beast soul yeah. But the character was still (raised) human right up to then, they would still wrestle with the act they are doing. They would still try to justify it (the lessons paradigm) or target it (the Dexter comparison). Those are personal horror. Just becuase a gameline uses an Integrity analog instead of Integrity doesn't mean they suddenly don't care about their previous morality or worldview, just that it is less important for the game mechanics to strictly re-enforce it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are explicitly stated to be biologically unable to feel fear. No fear = No horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:42:28-07:00","id":910218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910210#post910210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts are explicitly stated to be biologically unable to feel fear. No fear = No horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't recall this, could you provide a page ref?<br /> <br /> Also, horror is defined as: <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200b</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">an intense feeling of fear, shock, or disgust. </span></span></i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A Beast can still be shocked and disgusted at their own actions.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mirriam-Webster does drop disgust for dread, but the other major dictionaries all agree.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:05:06-07:00","id":910233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910218#post910218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall this, could you provide a page ref?<br /> <br /> Also, horror is defined as: <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200b</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">an intense feeling of fear, shock, or disgust. </span></span></i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A Beast can still be shocked and disgusted at their own actions.<br /> <br /> Edit: Mirriam-Webster does drop disgust for dread, but the other major dictionaries all agree.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: There's absolutely nothing to emphasize those elements. There's only feeding. In fact? If you want to rid yourself of Beast-hood all you have to do is sate your Horror completely, and then forget about it.<br /> <br /> Welcome back to human kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:08:59-07:00","id":910235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910233#post910233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome back to human kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Heroes quite possibly hunting you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:14:35-07:00","id":910239,"title":"","content":"You're human now. You call the police for stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:26:50-07:00","id":910244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910239#post910239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're human now. You call the police for stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, <i>Beasts</i> can still call the police on Heroes. After all, they look human too (mostly).<br /> <br /> Doesn't the Horror wake up on its own after a period of time when Satiety drops due to hunger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:37:19-07:00","id":910250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910244#post910244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, <i>Beasts</i> can still call the police on Heroes. After all, they look human too (mostly).<br /> <br /> Doesn't the Horror wake up on its own after a period of time when Satiety drops due to hunger?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the mechanics as written, when you get to Satiety 10, the Horror stays asleep until you fill your health track with Lethal, collapse a Chamber or the Horror itself suffers 3 or more Bashing. Other than that, it remains Slumbering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:40:51-07:00","id":910252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910233#post910233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing: There's absolutely nothing to emphasize those elements. There's only feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the 'fluff' does a pretty decent job of emphasis personally. There is only so much room for mechanics in a core book. Emphasizing feeding with Satiety means less mechanics for Integrity. Also, as discussed in some other threads, not all players like the Integrity(-equivelent) mechanics as punishment, moralizing, or role-play enforcing mechanics; possibly the change here was in some ways a nod to that desire.<br /> <br /> That said, this conversation has actually made me think of a Hack that I was gonna talk about in a general thread. There isn't a whole lot stopping Beasts (or other splats) from having Integrity too. Some mechincal things, more bookkeeping, and a general dillution of themes, but that might be worth it if it helps the game emphasize what the players want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:03:09-07:00","id":910262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910250#post910250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the mechanics as written, when you get to Satiety 10, the Horror stays asleep until you fill your health track with Lethal, collapse a Chamber or the Horror itself suffers 3 or more Bashing. Other than that, it remains Slumbering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you/it are still subject to the periodic loss of Satiety over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:16:43-07:00","id":910275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910262#post910262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you/it are still subject to the periodic loss of Satiety over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. The way the Slumbering Condition was worded it sounded like those were the only ways to get rid of it. I would personally run it like you said, but according to the hard-and-fast rules as I understand them, that doesn't seem to apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:36:46-07:00","id":910330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910275#post910275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure. The way the Slumbering Condition was worded it sounded like those were the only ways to get rid of it. I would personally run it like you said, but according to the hard-and-fast rules as I understand them, that doesn't seem to apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Losing Satiety and staying slumbering aren't mutually exclusive: you still lose Satiety over time, but retain the Slumbering Condition...eventually you get to 0 and now gain the Ravenous Condition... which does 1 Lethal each day. If the Beast still refuses to wake the Horror (while starving to death from something decidely not what a human should die from), then the Horror wakes up after 10 days and feeds itself in the Primordial Dream. If the Beast manages to survive she has to deal with the fallout of trying to keep the Horror asleep. Now that's some personal horror right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:29:24-07:00","id":910368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910330#post910330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing Satiety and staying slumbering aren't mutually exclusive: you still lose Satiety over time, but retain the Slumbering Condition...eventually you get to 0 and now gain the Ravenous Condition... which does 1 Lethal each day. If the Beast still refuses to wake the Horror (while starving to death from something decidely not what a human should die from), then the Horror wakes up after 10 days and feeds itself in the Primordial Dream. If the Beast manages to survive she has to deal with the fallout of trying to keep the Horror asleep. Now that's some personal horror right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the way Satiety works states that you can have multiple such conditions in play at the same time. They're all mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:39:22-07:00","id":910373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910368#post910368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in the way Satiety works states that you can have multiple such conditions in play at the same time. They're all mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, page 111 does say that. Hmm, the Condition itself though works as ajf115 listed. So either: Slumbering stops you from losing Satiety overtime (which is somewhat backed up by the second version of losing satiety at Storyteller discretion explicitly saying it doesn't work when Slumbering), or losing Satiety due to time automatically wakes the Horror up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Moved a derailing question to its own thread. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/910383-why-can-you-only-have-one-satiety-condition-at-a-time\">Here</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 06-08-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:04:54-07:00","id":910382,"title":"","content":"We aren't discussing RAI vs RAW. We're discussing why we should pick up Beast, if then we'd have to hack all the shit they tried to sloppily fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:09:35-07:00","id":910385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910382#post910382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We aren't discussing RAI vs RAW. We're discussing why we should pick up Beast, if then we'd have to hack all the shit they tried to sloppily fix.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I realized that this was the wrong place and moved to a new thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:00:28-07:00","id":910445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910210#post910210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts are explicitly stated to be biologically unable to feel fear. No fear = No horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page Citation, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:49:02-07:00","id":910524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910445#post910445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page Citation, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only things remotely near analogous that I can think of are that Beasts no longer dream after the Devouring and that Nightmares still work on things that are immune to fear, which\u2026 yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=910233#post910233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: There's absolutely nothing to emphasize those elements. There's only feeding. In fact? If you want to rid yourself of Beast-hood all you have to do is sate your Horror completely, and then forget about it.<br /> <br /> Welcome back to human kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed the part where humans recover Willpower from playing to expectations of monstrosity or highlighting contrasting sympathetic personality traits, have magical blood and paranormal charisma, can pass themselves off as supernatural beings to casual scrutiny, and don't have to worry about being unable to open magical gateways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:05:35-07:00","id":911453,"title":"","content":"As someone who missed the kickstarter and is catching up, what would you be doing in a typical Beast chronicle? What I've heard so far is pretty... sparse. There's the Beast and their Hunger, the people they hurt to feed it, and the Heroes who oppose them. Is that it? Vampires have their political games, Prometheans have their journey to humanity, Demons have their guerilla rebellion, etc. Playing Magic Dexter who messes with normal people and fights the occasional Hero seems like a pretty thin Chronicle if that's really all there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:26:10-07:00","id":911463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=911453#post911453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who missed the kickstarter and is catching up, what would you be doing in a typical Beast chronicle? What I've heard so far is pretty... sparse. There's the Beast and their Hunger, the people they hurt to feed it, and the Heroes who oppose them. Is that it? Vampires have their political games, Prometheans have their journey to humanity, Demons have their guerilla rebellion, etc. Playing Magic Dexter who messes with normal people and fights the occasional Hero seems like a pretty thin Chronicle if that's really all there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exploring your Legend and expanding your Lair through Kinship and less conversational varieties of investigation are more the bulk of the default setup, really.<br /> <br /> Do the memetic legwork necessary to build a balcony for the birdhouse in your soul. Poke around the spooky places of your local municipality. Find other monsters and find out why they're scary as part of the ongoing process of figuring out why <i>you're</i> scary so that you can get stronger and prevent your power from being exploited by others more than you're willing to tolerate. Get dragged into ideological struggles you are frightfully ill-informed to fully participate in and entirely too invested in one side or the other to opt out of. Look for kin. Hell, look for Mom if you're feeling particularly adventurous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-10-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:40:01-07:00","id":911474,"title":"","content":"If it helps as a reference, it would be somewhere between Mage and Promethean in how things tend to go. As Satchel covered, there's a lot of investigation of the strange any mysterious to explore kinship with other monsters, which will end up a lot like Mage in terms of the mystery angle. However unlike Mage where there's no real &quot;end goal&quot; to this, like Promethean you're on a journey to a different state of being. You're not seeking to become human, but you and your fellow Beasts are looking to figure out your place in the world and what you'll become as you grow in power. Also similar to both is the consequences matter. There's stuff like what Satchel said, but Heroes fill a similar game play aspect as Paradox and Disquiet to tie specific narrative obstacles into the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:00:47-07:00","id":912065,"title":"","content":"Beast is, to put it simply, SJW: the Crybullying. Beasts are strictly banned in all of my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer","name":"TheStranjer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:08:52-07:00","id":912071,"title":"","content":"Yes, because that's helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:32:29-07:00","id":912075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912065#post912065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is, to put it simply, SJW: the Crybullying. Beasts are strictly banned in all of my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">The people you refer to as SJWs are a group, and calling them crybabies and bullies is an attack against them. Group attacks are against the forum rules. Thos post is also bordering on threadcrapping, which is also against the forum rules. This is your warning, posts like this can and will result in suspensions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:18:09-07:00","id":912097,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10158_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10158\" data-vbnamecard=\"10158\">TheStranjer</a> Calling something &quot;SJW&quot; is childish. It's barely even true, and if you're running a game where Beasts would be allowed that isn't a Beast game, &quot;banning&quot; people from playing that is silly.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11959\" data-vbnamecard=\"11959\">Niknokk</a> That at it's heart is why Beast is a game that needs to be sold to someone. It's not really got any focus. It's got less reason for you to do any particular thing than Geist, and also has plenty of mechanics that get in the way of any sort of narrative. If you want to focus on scaring people (as the game wants you to), well, much like with Vampire and Changeling, that's treated as a pretty solitary thing. Even in the examples, your Brood or whatever they call it tends to wait outside while you spook your victim. If you want to focus on building up your secret base mechanic, you're not really doing anything besides playing WoD: Animal Crossing. If you go try and meet new monsters or do the crossover the game is intended for, Heroes get in the way. If you ignore Heroes, you've just cut out a portion of the game.<br /> <br /> It simultaneously wants to do too much and too little at the same time, so it doesn't really have any niche to hang it's hat on. A lot of the themes feel like they come right from Masquerade, others are from Changeling, and the most interesting part of the setting is tacked onto a side-realm from Mage, which is a thing the rest of the WoD tries to avoid so much that Changeling dreamworld and Mage dreamworld are different. On top of that, I feel like &quot;no social splats&quot; in a WoD game is something they tried with Geist and failed at. &quot;There's no reason to <i>do</i> anything&quot; is true of both that and Beast.<br /> <br /> So, if I were going to, how would I &quot;sell&quot; someone on the concept? If your group loves the Hunter and Mage style of proactive &quot;go find a problem and mess with it&quot; style of gameplay over more political focused &quot;the Elders make you do a thing&quot; type games, then chances are you'll be able to enjoy Beast as a game with Thing of the Week stories. I only really looked over Tokyo, but there are plenty of things for your group to poke their noses in, even if the only reason to do so is &quot;might be neat&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T00:39:04-07:00","id":912137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=909845#post909845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK; so if I'm reading this right:<br /> <br /> a Beast is a dragon, kraken, gorgon, or other mythical monster \u2014 but only in her dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>. . . Sort of.<br /> <br /> Did you ever see <i>Wes Craven's New Nightmare</i>? The one that got really meta? In it, he explained that Freddy Krueger was never a &quot;real&quot; person. Rather, it was a supernatural entity that humans started thinking of as a badly burnt dream predator (named Freddy Krueger). In time, though, it came to think of itself as Freddy Krueger, to the point that it took that shape, and even played by the fictional character's rules.<br /> <br /> A Horror is a lot like that. Its a super-goetic demon, a gestalt entity born from one of the shared fears of humanity. As it congeals into a discrete entity, it starts to take on the shape and personality of a monster that embodies that fear for humanity. Something that makes intuitive sense to a human - it is the spawn of the human subconscious, after all (&quot;form follows function&quot;)<br /> <br /> For example, Anakim are Horrors born of the fear of helplessness, of being weak and powerless. By the time an Anakim Horror is ready to evolve into a Beast, it has taken on a form that personifies brute force and strength. Ogres, giants, minotaurs . . . An Anakim is big enough to crush a human underfoot like a bug, or has impenetrable iron skin that no human could hope to scratch. Everything about it screams physical strength and brutality - the oldest, most primitive form of power.<br /> <br /> Now, there are some &quot;repeats&quot;. In becoming a unique entity, Horrors often do end up as &quot;mythic monsters&quot; - or even &quot;real&quot; ones. But that's because they've been shaped by the human subconscious (and those forms make sense to humanity). Each one is still a unique entity, and colored by their nightmarish birth. So a &quot;werewolf&quot; Horror will be some twisted monstrosity, with razor sharp claws, blood-stained fur, a necklace of human skulls . . . its a nightmare wearing the shape of a werewolf, not an actual werewolf out of <i>Forsaken. </i><br /> <br /> A Beast is what happens when a Horror gets itself a human body &amp; mind, evolving into something that can think beyond the simplistic purity of the Hunger. If you strip away all the fluff &amp; color of the game, a Beast is basically a psychic vampire that feeds by forcing people to experience fear (particularly deep seated or repressed fear).<br /> <br /> However, that's not really the vibe the game's going for. Rather, Beasts are supposed to be the &quot;monsters&quot; of ghost stories and slasher movies. Seemingly human characters that scare people on a very fundamental level. One of the sample characters, for example, is basically the Hook-hand Killer - you know, the one who went after the two teens parked at Make Out Point? Meanwhile &quot;Skeleton Key&quot;, a starting power, allows them to pull a &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gpCUMdfRa9w\" target=\"_blank\">Here's Johnny</a>&quot; (from <i>the Shining</i>), while a Promethean-inspired Nightmare allows a Beast to do the whole invulnerable Michael Myers thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she's asleep, she becomes the Horror (which, in Mage terms, is basically a monstrous Daemon) and roams the Primordial Dream, invading peoples' dreams and giving them nightmares in order to sate her Hunger. When she's awake, the Horror lurks in its Lair (analogous to a mage's Oneiros) and she walks the material world as a mostly-normal human with a limited ability to manifest powers based on her Horror (Atavisms) and Lair (by inflicting appropriate Environmental Tilts) and an ability to mess with peoples' minds (Nightmares). In theory, the Beast does what it does to teach people caution, humiity, and other \u201cschool of hard knocks\u201d lessons; in practice, Beasts often ignore that and feed solely to sate their Hunger. </div> </div> </div>Again, sort of.<br /> <br /> A Beast is simultaneously both a human in the waking world, and the monstrous Horror lurking in its Lair. As long as the human half is keeping it fed, the Horror is generally content to stay in its Lair . . . Doing whatever animalistic nightmare creatures do, in their spare time (although it will generally respect the human half's decisions - i.e. no eating the invited guests).<br /> <br /> If the human half doesn't keep it fed, though, the Horror will start hunting. Breaking into the dreams of others, and twisting those dreams into nightmares. Its <i>hungry</i>, after all.<br /> <br /> However, while the Horror normally can't come to earth, the human half can usually enter the Lair at will. All it takes is finding a place in the waking world that mirrors conditions in the Lair, and the Beast can withdraw to the Primordial Dream - and even take other people with them. That's often a combat tactic, actually. When their psychic powers aren't enough, Beasts retreat to their Lair, and (temporarily) merge with their Horror - which often has impressive combat abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . . . Kinship is part of the game's subversion of other games' themes, in that the Beast's view is that their monstrous natures are the best part of them while what's left of their human natures is an impediment. </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Beast. During the Devouring/Homecoming, the latent Beast's soul is destroyed, and the Horror's nature floods in to replace it. (Some Beasts find this a huge relief, by the way, particularly those that had a tight bond with their Horror even before the Devouring).<br /> <br /> The result is a being that's as smart as human . . . but doesn't think like one anymore. The new Beast has the same memory, personalities, quirks . . . but it now looks at the world from the perspective of a nightmare creature. As much as it might want to, a Beast will never see things quite the same, ever again. And many revel in their new, darker nature - for many, the Horror fills a hole in their life they never knew existed.<br /> <br /> At the same time, though, the new Beast often finds new appreciation for the positive aspects of human existence. A Beast can't feed on hope, friendship, kindness . . . but being permanently joined to a being from the darkest depths of the collected subconscious shows them just how valuable those things actually are.<br /> <br /> The balance a Beast strikes between its urge to revel in its inner darkness, versus their desire to hold on to those few glimpses of light, generally define whether the Beast ends up a good guy or a bad guy. Relatively speaking, of course.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, Reapers - mages who steal souls - <i>can</i> try to take a Beast's Horror. That's incredibly dangerous, though, since the Horror - unlike a human soul - can and will fight back.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Complementing this is the Beast's relationship with deranged self-described Heroes who see Beasts as little more than creatures to kill in their quest for glory. <b>Beast</b> admits that there are Heroes who are sane and who serve a purpose that's complementary to the Beast's supposed \u201cdrill sergeant from hell\u201d role \u2014 the carrot to the Beast's stick \u2014 but for the most part, it concentrates on those Heroes who slay Beasts. </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Technically, a Beast's &quot;job&quot; is just to force humans to admit there's a problem. Its the responsibility of Heroes to help humanity grow strong, and fix the problem.<br /> <br /> But that was before the average Hero degenerated into little more than a rampaging murder hobo. And thanks to their own evolution, most Beasts want to do more than just terrorize and destroy. They want to make a difference. Such Beasts often adopt the idea of teaching lessons, or work on a pet cause (protect an orphanage, track down war criminals, etc) that allows them to feed in a &quot;constructive&quot; manner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 06-11-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T01:45:48-07:00","id":912149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=911453#post911453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who missed the kickstarter and is catching up, what would you be doing in a typical Beast chronicle? What I've heard so far is pretty... sparse. There's the Beast and their Hunger, the people they hurt to feed it, and the Heroes who oppose them. Is that it? Vampires have their political games, Prometheans have their journey to humanity, Demons have their guerilla rebellion, etc. Playing Magic Dexter who messes with normal people and fights the occasional Hero seems like a pretty thin Chronicle if that's really all there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding your Hunger is actually a great story element. For a vampire, a pint of blood is a pint of blood. There's no practical difference between drinking one pint from ten people, or draining one person dry.<br /> <br /> That's not true for Beasts. If they want a big feed, they have to do something <i>big</i>. A Collector can squeak by through buying gold from a local jeweler, or ordering first editions through eBay, it they're willing to live on the metaphysical equivalent of bread and water, and don't want to use their powers. But if they want to gorge themselves sick, and actually recharge their power pool, they have to do something equally <i>huge</i>. Steal the cure for AIDS from a corrupt pharmaceutical company. Recover a Brahmastra (Atlantean superweapon) from a forgotten temple. &quot;Liberate&quot; the only known map to Irem from an ancient vampire's library.<br /> <br /> If you tweak the mythos a bit, Magneto's arc from <b>X-men: First Class</b> works as an excellent example. In pursuit of the Mysteries, Sebastian Shaw (an evil mage), forces him to undergo the Devouring young, and in a very horrific manner. Shaw later throws him away, and forgets about the young Beast.<br /> <br /> Magneto doesn't forget Shaw, though. A Nemesis (a Beast with a Hunger for Punishment), the adult Magneto starts by tracking down a Swiss banker, forces information from him, and then punishes him for laundering blood money. Its a serviceable meal for his Hunger, and sends him to Argentina. There, he finds a couple minor Nazi fugitives, who tell him how to find Shaw . . . and who make an even bigger and better meal.<br /> <br /> Working with Xavier, Magneto is able to track down Shaw, and build a team to stop him. Using Mother's Kiss, they boost the team's power, and Xavier is able to help Magneto recover some of his favorite (and purely human) memories of lighting the menorah.<br /> <br /> So of course Xavier is completely shocked when Magneto kills Shaw. He assumed that helping Magneto remember his humanity would make him a better person. But even though Magneto treasures those recovered memories, he's not human - he's a Beast now. Showing mercy to Shaw isn't even on the table. Killing him is not merely personally satisfying to Magneto, but a <i>massive</i> feed. After all, is there anyone more evil and deserving of punishment than a high ranking Nazi butcher who just tried to kill all humanity in a plot for personal power?<br /> <br /> Saving the world, getting personal revenge, attracting followers, and recharging your batteries to full power - sounds like a pretty successful campaign, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: In a different direction, you can also use most campaigns designed for other lines as a <i>Beast</i> game. Between the protean nature of their Horrors, and ability to mimic the powers of others, Beasts can substitute for . . . practically anything. For example, if the Beast community is well-established, with a powerful Incarnate as Apex (basically Beast king), and a lot of intrigue between broods, then you can swap them in for the vampires in a <i>Requiem</i> campaign. If the Apex actively hates them, and tries to persecute them, you've got a mock-<i>Demon</i> game . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 06-11-2016, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:54:58-07:00","id":912264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912149#post912149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding your Hunger is actually a great story element. For a vampire, a pint of blood is a pint of blood. There's no practical difference between drinking one pint from ten people, or draining one person dry.<br /> <br /> That's not true for Beasts. If they want a big feed, they have to do something <i>big</i>. A Collector can squeak by through buying gold from a local jeweler, or ordering first editions through eBay, it they're willing to live on the metaphysical equivalent of bread and water, and don't want to use their powers. But if they want to gorge themselves sick, and actually recharge their power pool, they have to do something equally <i>huge</i>. Steal the cure for AIDS from a corrupt pharmaceutical company. Recover a Brahmastra (Atlantean superweapon) from a forgotten temple. &quot;Liberate&quot; the only known map to Irem from an ancient vampire's library.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing this does is force you to think about &quot;how&quot; you feed in a very central and important way, especially if your goal is High Satiety. You can either try to go for a big feeding, using a single act of terror to keep your Horror asleep and then never have to worry about it or do anything similar for a while, or you can try and space it out into more acts that are less destructive individually but will probably have to be inflicted on more people. The act of feeding itself, the planning of how you go about it, basically forms a mini passion play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:10:52-07:00","id":912272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912097#post912097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10158_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10158\" data-vbnamecard=\"10158\">TheStranjer</a> Calling something &quot;SJW&quot; is childish. It's barely even true, and if you're running a game where Beasts would be allowed that isn't a Beast game, &quot;banning&quot; people from playing that is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it's silly to control which splats people are allowed to play on a game that you own and operate. In fact, doing so has been done for decades at this juncture, literally. It's par for the course.<br /> <br /> There are some pretty serious issues with the splat that make me not want to allow people to play them.<br /> <br /> For one, it stresses very early on how Beasts are the Good Guys and how them fucking people up is really for their own good because humanity needs to be taught &quot;lessons.&quot; It also stresses early on how Beasts were all &quot;different&quot; as children, and typically got bullied, abused, neglected, etc, as a consequence of this. It's also stressed how Heroes aren't really heroic, and are really just egomaniacs, evil jocks, etc. There is a lot of effort put into making these antagonists unsympathetic. Thing is, sympathetic antagonists are good antagonists. They make storytelling more fun, not less fun. This effort to make Beasts (creatures who fuck people up to teach them &quot;lessons&quot;) look sympathetic while making Heroes (the people who try to stop them from doing this) look like stupid bullies who hurt innocent Beasts who dindu nuffin because they don't &quot;get it&quot; is extremely cringey to me. This is where I get the crybullying part of my statement from: Beasts do bad things, terrible things to people, and them playing the victim when Heroes consequence them for it is built right into the game's lore. <br /> <br /> Another issue is how ideology is injected into the game. One of the sample Heroes (of only a handful) is a m'ladying MRA incel with a trilby. This is where I get the &quot;SJW&quot; part from. If you're going to insert ideologically charged stereotypes into your game, be prepared for people who don't agree with your politics to dislike that game.<br /> <br /> The final issue that I'm going to raise in this post is how overpowered they are. Abruption is a Condition that someone can face because an exceptional success was landed against them, or the Bad Blood Nightmare was used against them, etc. What Abruption does is it disables all supernatural effects, and the only way to resolve it is by admitting your &quot;inferiority&quot; to the Beast who gave it to you. You do not get a Beat for this. Also doing this gives you the Beaten Down Tilt, which basically removes him from the fight. Not only is this overpowered, but it's reminiscent of Maoist <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Struggle_session\" target=\"_blank\">struggle sessions</a>. From Wikipedia: &quot;In general, the victim of a struggle session was forced to admit to various crimes before a crowd of people who would verbally and physically abuse the victim until he or she confessed. Struggle sessions were often held at the workplace of the accused, but were sometimes conducted in sports stadiums where large crowds would gather if the target was famous enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> So feel free to suspend or ban me for stating this opinion, but no, I don't like your game about being a smug SJW crybully with struggle session magic powers, I'm not paying money for it, and I'm not participating in any games that involve them. Just no. Deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer","name":"TheStranjer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:16:41-07:00","id":912274,"title":"","content":"Narrow read if ever I read one, but sure, you do you.<br /> <br /> Just don't waste the time of the people who are in a thread about Selling Beast. There's threads a-plenty to rant in, this is not it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:28:47-07:00","id":912278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912274#post912274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narrow read if ever I read one, but sure, you do you.<br /> <br /> Just don't waste the time of the people who are in a thread about Selling Beast. There's threads a-plenty to rant in, this is not it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to sell Beast, errata that shit out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer","name":"TheStranjer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:34:32-07:00","id":912280,"title":"","content":"OK, so now I'm getting that sort of creepy/chummy &quot;we're all monsters here&quot; vibe I got from talking to Pischa in the old hospital in V:tM Bloodlines. That's kind of cool.<br /> I've heard a lot of complaints about the crossover elements, and I think I understand why. No matter how crossover-friendly Beast is, the other gamelines are generally pretty crossover-unfriendly. Beasts feel like they make sense more often as NPCs or antagonists in something like Mage or Changeling.<br /> If, on the other hand, you want to do a general Chronicles of Darkness game and play with a grab bag of random splats, then Beast would make sense as a springboard for that.<br /> <br /> As for feeding, eh. It still feels like I'm being given a choice of playing Dexter or Principal Ed Rooney. It just about makes sense as a mechanic for forcing players to get involved in important story-stuff (the Magneto approach), but the &quot;lessons&quot; thing seems pretty weak. And also insufferable. Would you rather be screwed over by a random asshole, or by someone who insists there's a &quot;lesson&quot; in it and they're really doing you a favor? If I had to play one or the other, I'd definitely prefer the random asshole approach and not pretend there was anything more to it.<br /> What I can say, is that while playing a deliberately low-Wisdom mage never appealed, for example, playing a deliberately low-Saitiety Beast at odds with their Horror actually seems fairly compelling.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Heroes as narrative obstacles, similar to Paradox, though. That's a cool read. One other thing I noted is that becoming a Hero is really similar to becoming a Mage: you have to lean in to the supernatural weirdness and pursue it. If you back out, no Mage, no Hero. On the one hand, it makes me wonder a little why mages are seen as kin. On the other, could be a pretty good hook. A mage meets an old friend that they investigated a mystery with, the friend didn't Awaken, they drifted apart. And now the friend is back, and there's something different about them... Any maybe they're hunting a proper monster who pals around with slashers and liches, and maybe they're just hunting a jerk, or maybe they're hunting a genuinely nice person who is paying the price for not hurting people.<br /> <br /> Also, whoa, Irem?! Google tells me it's a thing in Mummy, but now I kind of want to do Chronicles of Darkness: Sunless Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:37:14-07:00","id":912281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912272#post912272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So feel free to suspend or ban me for stating this opinion, but no, I don't like your game about being a smug SJW crybully with struggle session magic powers, I'm not paying money for it, and I'm not participating in any games that involve them. Just no. Deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meaning no offence, if you're not paying money for the game and don't want to play it... why are you here? It's an honest question. Would it not be more constructive of you to argue points A) on a thread which is devoted to that argument and/or B) leave alone those who are having a conversation you clearly are against on a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> The point of the game is that of Beasts and Heroes, the only ones who have the moral high ground are those Heroes who refrain from hunting Beasts and work to make the world a better place. Beasts can try, and they can do good, but that good will always be stained by their arguably inherently evil natures. Heroes who succumb to the Monomyth <i>are</i> deluded and misguided individuals, many caring little for those around them in their quest for a nebulous 'glory'. The reasons that the book stresses that of these latter, Beasts are the good guys are twofold: 1) the book is written from the perspective of Beasts, not Heroes or mortals and 2) we instinctively see monsters as evil. Therefore effort must be put in to soften this, in order to let the player characters be 'good' at all. I agree that the book could have perhaps done this in a better way but this conflict, with deep self-delusion on both sides, is an inherent part of it. It's not explained the best but the idea and concept are an excellent attempt to grasp the relationship of humanity with the monsters that we fear and give power through our fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:45:17-07:00","id":912284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912280#post912280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OWould you rather be screwed over by a random asshole, or by someone who insists there's a &quot;lesson&quot; in it and they're really doing you a favor? If I had to play one or the other, I'd definitely prefer the random asshole approach and not pretend there was anything more to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could pretty much play this exercise with any game (even beyond the WoD) where the core PCs are also monsters.<br /> <br /> Would you rather play vampires where vampires have ideologies that regard to feeding, or they casually drain people dry and not pretend there's more to vampires than being a parasite?<br /> Would you rather play werewolves that put their unending urge to hunt to philosophic goals,or mindless wolves that hunt on full moons without pretending there's anything more to them than that?<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> The main PCs of the CofD game lines are monsters. They do horrible things by human standards. If the games want to provide any sort of game-play depth to those things, there has to be more to them than just doing them and moving on without consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:47:25-07:00","id":912285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912278#post912278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to sell Beast, errata that shit out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding my inclination one way or another, the thread is Sell Beast the way it is. Not &quot;Sell This Game with tons of hacks&quot;. The audience is curious why people like the game the way it is.<br /> <br /> You don't like it the way it is. You've dropped the curtain on your uncertain and made that quite clear. You are not the target audience of this conversation.<br /> <br /> You are also not adding to the conversation. Like I said, there are tons of threads asking or bemoaning what is wrong with the game. You can go spin your uglies around there. You might even make traction.<br /> <br /> Here, you are useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:15:10-07:00","id":912293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912272#post912272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So feel free to suspend or ban me for stating this opinion, but no, I don't like your game about being a smug SJW crybully with struggle session magic powers</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">If you insist.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:37:54-07:00","id":912305,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10158_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10158\" data-vbnamecard=\"10158\">TheStranjer</a> You're making some pretty big leaps with your interpretation of Beast. A lot of them aren't really even there in the final product, even if they were there in the original. I'm pretty sure we've had many an anonymous spat about Beast, so I won't really bother to go into it, though. If you don't like the themes you see in the game, then fine, but when you're ranting and raving about how terrible it is to a bunch of people that don't really share your opinion, you're not really doing anything worthwhile.<br /> And don't even act like I'm some militant lover of Beast, either (sidenote: <i>Militant Lover of Beasts</i> sounds like a good concept album for an experimental alt-rock group). I managed to point out several of the game's flaws without using loaded anti-progressive buzzwords that tend to be used by the kind of people the book paints as villains, as you see it. More than that, I just flat out don't see most of your argument as being true. Even the Gamergate references were removed last I checked. It's a game about playing horrible assholes who justify their existence as being part of a larger narrative. They don't say that they're the &quot;good guys&quot;. I mean, isn't Abjuration a Condition that an NPC gives as part of the setting, in a way that's intentionally set up to create conflict?<br /> Also, you should really keep the 4chan rhetoric on 4chan. I love that you went and complained. That's what's likely to get you banned, not going &quot;I don't like thing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:11:11-07:00","id":912331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912284#post912284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could pretty much play this exercise with any game (even beyond the WoD) where the core PCs are also monsters.<br /> <br /> Would you rather play vampires where vampires have ideologies that regard to feeding, or they casually drain people dry and not pretend there's more to vampires than being a parasite?<br /> Would you rather play werewolves that put their unending urge to hunt to philosophic goals,or mindless wolves that hunt on full moons without pretending there's anything more to them than that?<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> The main PCs of the CofD game lines are monsters. They do horrible things by human standards. If the games want to provide any sort of game-play depth to those things, there has to be more to them than just doing them and moving on without consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. I'm not entirely sure why Beast bothers me more for that than similar games. Lessee;<br /> <br /> In Vampire, &quot;personal horror&quot; is the main theme, or at least A main theme; the tension between &quot;I'm an abominable predator and actually, this feels pretty good!&quot;<br /> The Vampire is explicitly at odds with their Beast. The closest thing to a &quot;default B:tP&quot; mindset seems to be the Lancea Sanctum, but even other Vampires are pretty skeeved out by them.<br /> The game assumes you were a regular person turned into a monster and now you have to cope, and everything in the game flows fairly organically out of that. Bluntly, there ISN'T more to vampires than being a parasite, but you were turned into one anyway, and the drama comes from dealing with that.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble finding a similarly compelling viewpoint into Beast. I'm even kind of unclear if you're playing a human-with-a-passenger, or a monster-with-a-mask. If I'm playing a human, haunted by a kraken, I'm going to feel differently about things than if I am the Kraken. If I'm going to gleefully identify with the Kraken, I need to be the Kraken. If I am the Kraken, then yes, absolutely, lets sign on with Sea Shepherd and gorge ourselves on illegal fishermen. If I'm a regular person haunted by a Kraken, I think I'd be horrified if it suggested that, and I don't think compromising on &quot;lets go flood someone's house while they're asleep&quot; would make me feel much better, even if the person was also a jerk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:25:56-07:00","id":912341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912331#post912331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm having trouble finding a similarly compelling viewpoint into Beast. I'm even kind of unclear if you're playing a human-with-a-passenger, or a monster-with-a-mask. If I'm playing a human, haunted by a kraken, I'm going to feel differently about things than if I am the Kraken. If I'm going to gleefully identify with the Kraken, I need to be the Kraken. If I am the Kraken, then yes, absolutely, lets sign on with Sea Shepherd and gorge ourselves on illegal fishermen. If I'm a regular person haunted by a Kraken, I think I'd be horrified if it suggested that, and I don't think compromising on &quot;lets go flood someone's house while they're asleep&quot; would make me feel much better, even if the person was also a jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, and this is probably going to be the most unsatisfying answer in history, is that different Beasts have different perspectives on this. Some of them see themselves as monsters-with-masks while some of them see themselves as humans-with-passengers. The truth is probably somewhere in between, where the Horror and the human part are not the same thing, but are more like two facets of a gem. They're different (although not necessarily <i>that</i> different) but are ultimately parts of the same whole. If you want a more cliched metaphor, they're sides of a coin. They've got different patterns but they're the same coin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:25:20-07:00","id":912376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912280#post912280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just about makes sense as a mechanic for forcing players to get involved in important story-stuff (the Magneto approach), but the &quot;lessons&quot; thing seems pretty weak. And also insufferable. Would you rather be screwed over by a random asshole, or by someone who insists there's a &quot;lesson&quot; in it and they're really doing you a favor? If I had to play one or the other, I'd definitely prefer the random asshole approach and not pretend there was anything more to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've brought up a particular Tarantino line <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/830051-not-inherently-evil?p=830501#post830501\">twice before</a> in response to this read and I figure one more can't hurt, particularly in a thread for selling the game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jules Winnfield, Pulp Fiction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ezekiel 25:17. &quot;The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the iniquities of the selfish and the tyranny of evil men. Blessed is he who, in the name of charity and good will, shepherds the weak through the valley of darkness, for he is truly his brother's keeper and the finder of lost children. And I will strike down upon thee with great vengeance and furious anger those who attempt to poison and destroy my brothers. And you will know my name is the Lord when I lay my vengeance upon thee.&quot;<br /> <br /> I been saying that shit for years. And if you heard it, that meant your ass. I never gave much thought to what it meant. I just thought it was some cold-blooded shit to say to a motherfucker before I popped a cap in his ass.<br /> <br /> But I saw some shit this morning made me think twice. See, now I'm thinking, maybe it means you're the evil man, and I'm the righteous man, and Mr. 9 Millimeter here? He's the shepherd protecting my righteous ass in the valley of darkness. Or it could mean you're the righteous man and I'm the shepherd and it's the world that's evil and selfish. Now I'd like that. But that shit ain't the truth.<br /> <br /> <b>The truth is\u2026you're the weak, and I am the tyranny of evil men. But I'm trying, Ringo. I'm trying <u>real hard</u> to be the shepherd.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One other thing I noted is that becoming a Hero is really similar to becoming a Mage: you have to lean in to the supernatural weirdness and pursue it. If you back out, no Mage, no Hero. On the one hand, it makes me wonder a little why mages are seen as kin. </div> </div> </div>The thing about Heroes in contrast to mages is that the Awakened lean into the strangeness because they're obsessed; one doesn't &quot;become&quot; a Hero, but reaching the point as a Hero where you think the best use of your life is smashing the <i>divers alarums and excursions</i> that populate the Primordial Dream happens because you don't have a proper handle on your self-image.<br /> <br /> Ritual notwithstanding, Awakened magic draws upon forces that get very messy in the phenomenal world \u2014 just being a mage attracts mysterious shenanigans to you and your loved ones by virtue of your being defined by the heavens as someone who investigates mysterious phenomena, and the deepest form of innate magical analysis available to a mage is effectively the metaphysical equivalent of putting it in your mouth.<br /> <br /> And Beasts know a thing or two about swallowing secrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:36:12-07:00","id":912382,"title":"","content":"Now, where was I?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah. Selling the game. Let me meander my way to that point.<br /> <br /> First thing that I need bring up, in relation to all of this, is that I am the sort of person who doesn't believe you can generate anything 'meaningful' until you've embraced the meaningless nature of...well, everything. It's only when you've accepted that you're nothing that you can be <i>anything</i>. My daily fight is against the omnipotent sense of nihilism being right, and the only to prove it wrong is to prove it right first. So, that said, let's start properly meandering our way down through Beast<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, my middle brother once went camping in the deep, forested wild of Colorado by himself. He describes it as a character changing moment for himself, and I find I have to agree. He seems wiser, more cognizant of his limits and the ways he can overcome them, more inclined to live beyond himself and in the thoughts and feelings of others, even as he disagrees with them. All around, a better person. But it wasn't some cool, kind communion with nature that did it, no.<br /> <br /> It was the night that did it. The cold, suffocating, invasive hours of immutable shade that pressed and grasped at him. The days stripping human civilization from his brain, the night poking his lizard brain. In that infinite dark, he was laid low and forced to confront himself, in all of his deepest, darkest crevices, every fault and failing and sin of his magnified to giants over him in that night. He speaks in reverential tones he never had for church of the horror he experienced those nights. He speaks with gratitude.<br /> <br /> I've had moments like that, but I'm getting tired of semi-painting myself as a tragic figure. Suffice it to say, I've hit lows of in the night where new problems, new solutions, new wisdom hit me, where I learned something about myself and the world, things that felt <i>right</i>.<br /> <br /> Lots of people like to remember the looters of Katrina, the assholes who went around robbing shit because who the fuck was going to stop them. It makes for good press, anytime a catastrophe happens, because the spiral of things getting worse at least increases the drama. For some, it reaffirms the old truths they always knew, the human bastard seen in all it's glory. For others, it's a revelation, a shock and concern, a challenge to their rose-lensed look at the world.<br /> <br /> Lots of people also like to remember governmental failings, how all the systems in the world didn't get fresh water and food to the people who needed the most. Some took the fight to the hill, demanding we work harder than ever to ensure our emergency responses are faster, fuller, better, and plenty took the fight to the labs and the shops to make the tools that could make it happen. Some shook their head in disgust, in disillusionment about the governemnt and distrust of the human bastard getting anything done, realizing that systems cannot save if the human heart is absent. FOr some, that leads to self-reliance. For some, that leads to greater charity.<br /> <br /> Less talked about Katrina, and several other catastrophes, is how the survivors came together, how they worked together to make the fires, spread the food, watch the children. How they kept their backs to their meager coals, kept one eye on each other, and one eye outside their sanctums. How people found new worth in one another, how the racial and class divides broken down somewhat. How a tragedy forged a community.<br /> <br /> Tyler Durden was a &quot;man's man&quot;, an asshole who blame society, women in particular, for his 'problems'-but credit where it's due, the asshole got steam by pointing out some true things. Human society does depend far too much on it's stuff to speak for them. People are their bank accounts, the clothes they wear, the contents of their wallets, their bowel cancer, their grande latte, the car they drive.. People have become their fucking khaki's. They keep building wall after wall after wall between them and the field of corpses and allowing themselves to become useless. The species is always at the risk of stagnating, of not evolving. But the question is whether that's okay or not. There's no answer-that's his sin.<br /> <br /> Buddhists and Hindis alike teach the sins of attachment, how we let ignorance and desire and wrath blind us from true enlightenment and freedom. They ask what in the world is best in life, with an understanding of life that stretches into the abandonment of the illusion we call self. How right are they can be argued about-but one has to wonder what the purpose of the self is in the world.<br /> <br /> Here's a truth: at the end of the day, the world is uncaring, content in it's meaningless nature. Cruelty and Kindness are illusions of circumstance. And yet, in the starkness of the world, in it's vast meaninglessness, mankind gets the grand view of what matters to them, what needs to be accepted in themselves and what needs to be rejected. Any person who is stripped of place, people, and possessions, of ideas and dreams, can stand in that vastness and feel in their hearts the serenity, the acceptance, the peace that comes with being nothing but the self in the world, to <i>be. </i>In this state, they realize that they are not above the world, but part of it, that they have a place in the embrace of the world, and that their nature that brings them to this place is not an evil, merely a certainty. In the depth of that tranquil horror, it's easy to see a dream, of a world in equilibrium with it's people, where that serenity and oneness with the world can be found, and yet it's cruelties may yet be curtailed. In this zero state, such a dream is not a lie, though it is only a possibility. When a person tells of this vision of awe to others, they may only see and hear with the senses of fear.<br /> <br /> Mankind fears this mercurial, meaningless thing, and to shelter from the storm, they hunger for security. They build the spear and the hut, hunt the mammoth and make use of it's meat and bones, they build tribes and govern them with order. As they go on, they will raise kingdoms and walls and servant, gather gold and art, write codes of conduct and dedicate people to their governence, and hunt down their threats. In time, the world through these people takes it's toll. Some will use their power and hoard to hurt and control others, hiding behind the punishments they have decreed. Others will stake their claims and lay ruin on the homes of others and the the prey they cultivate. Others will not predate, but merely bow to these forces, and deny themselves the one possibility even the world may yet allow. They hide behind their homes and blankets, tell themselves their checks from their high-placed job will put the food on the table, sure that the courts will save them if the worst should happen. There is no fault in this, for this is the world-but ignorance binds society to their misery, rather than allowing peace.<br /> <br /> These forces are vast and incomprehensible on their own, and mankind, in their fear of fear and desperation and desire, will develop a defining force, called language, to handle it. They will give the shadows masks, name the storms and disappearances. They will make the vast, meaningless, incomprehensible world and break it down into forms and motives and territories, things to know. From there, they will offer obeisance, or at least seek ways to appease these gods and demons. They seek reconciliation with these monsters. Some think they can be satiated by the very forces they've used to hide from them, with gold or with sheep or with mountain or with taboos or with reverence. Others can only grovel. There is no fault in this, for this is the world.<br /> <br /> This is the Primordial Dream-a roiling ocean of fear and desperation, the twisting roads of entropy that dictates the very powers that may divide humanity from their fear will only bring them down, populated by the Horrors who reflect the tide that builds and destroys as surely as our every breath gives us life, yet continues on the path of slow fire. It's humanity's inherent weaknesses and flaws-and the serenity in knowing themselves, and the wisdom that can lead to a different future.<br /> <br /> The world is uncaring, and these dreams of ourselves will crash upon the rocks of our civilization as it will. Mankind is not free from who they are, at the depths of their souls, and they never will be until they are no longer human. And yet, this fear and serenity, for as much as it is humanity, lacks a human touch. It is merely a storm in and of itself, a thing that preys on the world and nothing more.<br /> <br /> The world is uncaring, content in it's meaninglessness. And You, the Beast, are that world.<br /> <br /> But humans are caring, and always drawing things of meaning, beauty, horror, and more out of that void, of that vast expanse where Things Happen. And You, the Beast, are Human.<br /> <br /> Humans are the world, and the world is humanity. It's easy for both sides to forget, if they even bother to dare comprehend. You stand at the threshold, a nightmare in flesh, and direct the ocean. You take the wisdom and serenity that is found under the fear and desperate desire and use it on the Primordial Dream itself, letting humanity shape itself by way of higher insight.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, you will use fear to lay low the corrupt, making the CEO beg at your knees, the politician give up his manipulated gains, the extremist surrender his fight, the corrupt judge confess his sins, the raping frat boy apologize for breaking into houses. You'll make them see that the walls of civilization are thin, only barely there, and that without the facade, they are naked to their own cruelties, and to the world beyond.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, you'll use strip people of their barriers to raise them up and expose their higher selves. A couple need not doubt any more as one lays aside their ego for the other, confronts the Beast, and begs and pleads to do anything they want with them, so long as the other is let go. A young adult, having all his fantasies stripped from him, goes out into the world, and connects to people, and finds he can bring them great joy. The soldier seeks a better way, not as a fighter, but as a representative of his state, knowing that all the strength in the world cannot protect you, and to possess it is to invite disaster. An internet blogger now seeks to inspire and change his social network, having the cruelties of the un-named justices he assumed shown to him personally. A family gathers-they haven't talked in years, but without a roof over their head, they protect themselves in the storm by mending bridges and finding joy in one another again, content to huddle together in the hope of a rescue helicopter, and the knowledge that if they should pass, they'll pass together, hand in hand.<br /> <br /> There are some who would call this cruelty. Some who would call it presumption and ego. And it can be.<br /> <br /> But pain, while a part of life, is not the whole of it. These things pass. Without the guidance of the Beast, they may be crueler still, because the world does not think about how any given person arrived where they are and where they will go as a result-it just happens, it just strikes. But a Beast can, <i>should</i>, direct the ocean, and tailor the storms that must happen to the benefit of those it strikes. A brief bit of pain can be a worthy price for better lives and better worlds.<br /> <br /> This is Beast the Primordial. It's fear and want and wisdom and serenity. It's the happiness of acceptance and the glory of defiance and the hope that the two can be attained together. It's how humans are the world, a cold, cruel, uncaring place. It's how the world is humans-ever building, ever dreaming, always learning. It's about equilibrium, and all the reasons we stray from it. It's about chaos, and how we carve a world free of it. It's about how, in the end, we are who we are- in all our cyclical imperfections and glorious progress.<br /> <br /> It's about being the monster who cares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-11-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:11:39-07:00","id":912472,"title":"","content":"Kinship: is this just a list of which supernatural types the Beast has encountered, or is it a trait that the Beast must earn in some way and which only provides benefits for those types for which it has been earned? That is, is it possible to have a Beast who can't use Family Dinner with vampires because she hasn't established Kinship with vampires (yet)? <br /> <br /> Frankly, the whole \u201chorror from the collective unconscious that terrorizes people in order to survive\u201d doesn't interest me; so if I'm going to be sold on Beast, it's going to have to be <i>in spite of</i> that \u2014 something else about the game that makes it worth my while to put up with the distasteful part. I think the \u201cfamily\u201d element might be a suitable candidate for that; please tell me more, because I'm getting some cognitive dissonance between that and the \u201csolitary hunter\u201d archetype that most of the monsters featured in <b>Beast</b> tend to have in their source material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:16:15-07:00","id":912475,"title":"","content":"You have Kinship with a being once you've established it with the Family Ties Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:07:55-07:00","id":912504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912472#post912472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship: is this just a list of which supernatural types the Beast has encountered, or is it a trait that the Beast must earn in some way and which only provides benefits for those types for which it has been earned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinship is the name given to the broad affinity the Begotten have for most supernatural beings; most of the pursuit of Kinship concerns developing a closer bond with specific specimens of supernatural beings through the application of the Family Ties Condition, which is helpful or necessary for many of the abilities Kinship provides, like registering as a different kind of monster to passive supernatural observation or enhancing the magical qualities of a given paranormal entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is, is it possible to have a Beast who can't use Family Dinner with vampires because she hasn't established Kinship with vampires (yet)? </div> </div> </div>Family Dinner is half-again to twice as effective if at least one participant is a character the Beast has Family Ties with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the \u201cfamily\u201d element might be a suitable candidate for that; please tell me more, because I'm getting some cognitive dissonance between that and the \u201csolitary hunter\u201d archetype that most of the monsters featured in <b>Beast</b> tend to have in their source material. </div> </div> </div>Most of &quot;the source material&quot; reflects particularly old Beasts who've burned a lot of their bridges, have Lairs vast enough that they can reliably subsist on nightmares, and don't have much to fear from Heroes attracted by particularly deep feedings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-11-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T19:38:22-07:00","id":912587,"title":"","content":"A major element that we haven't really addressed yet is the dungeon building aspect. If you like &quot;Boss Monster&quot;, or other games that involve building a trap-filled labyrinth to crush any interlopers, that's definitely present in <i>Beast</i>.<br /> <br /> A Beast's Lair starts as a single chamber (room/cavern/field) in the Primordial Dream, one that's thematically appropriate to the Horror. But there are lots of places that have echoes in the Primordial Dream - often caused by brushes with the supernatural. By finding the real world counterpart to such a place (and spending a mix of XP and Satiety), a Beast can annex it, adding it on to his Lair. And since most brushes end badly for the human, these new chambers often bring their own nightmarish powers that can be used to defend the Lair.<br /> <br /> If that's an aspect you enjoy, your group can have a lot of fun building unique Lairs - find the right spot, and the sky is literally the limit (got to love airplanes) for what can be added. Arctic, undersea, underground, jungles, riots, temples, prisons, strip malls . . . Beasts can even combine their Lairs, pooling their defenses and powers.<br /> <br /> And as an added benefit, those new chambers also double as warp points back to the original site (that generated them), allowing a well-travelled Beast to (de facto) teleport around the globe, as easily as you or I walk next door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912472#post912472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship: is this just a list of which supernatural types the Beast has encountered, or is it a trait that the Beast must earn in some way and which only provides benefits for those types for which it has been earned? (. . .)</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinship defines a Beast's relationship with all the other splat types (including NPC-only ones), except hunters and the creations of the God-Machine. Somehow, on some level, they are the same.<br /> <br /> Initially, its a very shallow connection, but if a Beast manages to establish a real relationship with a member of another splat, it rapidly deepens (to &quot;Family Ties&quot;), offering many benefits to both sides. Having a Family Tie allows the Beast to impersonate that other splat, learn thematically appropriate Nightmares (spell-like effects) based on the splat, etc.<br /> <br /> So building a big &quot;family&quot; offers immediate and powerful benefits to the Beast. 'Course, that also introduces all sorts of drama . . . But what family doesn't have issues? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, the whole \u201chorror from the collective unconscious that terrorizes people in order to survive\u201d doesn't interest me; so if I'm going to be sold on Beast, it's going to have to be <i>in spite of</i> that \u2014 something else about the game that makes it worth my while to put up with the distasteful part. I think the \u201cfamily\u201d element might be a suitable candidate for that; please tell me more, because I'm getting some cognitive dissonance between that and the \u201csolitary hunter\u201d archetype that most of the monsters featured in <b>Beast</b> tend to have in their source material. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Family&quot; is a huge thematic element in the game. The average Beast literally sees the other supernaturals as kin, and that even carries over to the writing. Heck, the entire section on how Beasts see the other splats is written in terms of filial ties:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a crossover game, <b>Promethean: The Created</b> showcases a side to Family that Beasts don\u2019t always consider \u2014 what &quot;family&quot; means to an orphan, and how an artificial being can hope to fit into the great family of humanity. Even the two beings\u2019 names for themselves, &quot;Begotten&quot; and &quot;Created,&quot; show the contrast between the two (. . .) Beasts and Prometheans can learn a lot from one another about the nature and value of kinship; what it means to (be a parent, or to have children)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Beast\u2019s perspective, mages are the one child in a family who went to college; she comes to family gatherings with her mind on experiences she can\u2019t share and vocabulary her kin can\u2019t understand. Her family feels threatened, and she feels alienated by their reaction. A Beast who takes the time to explore his Kinship with the Awakened finds they have more in common than they think (. . . )</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T23:39:25-07:00","id":912665,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Horror replaces the Beast's soul, and souls in CoD are far from the sum total of personality. Losing your soul doesn't immediately change your personality, it gradually erodes your mental fortitude. You can even replace it with a different soul and return to a largely unchanged self. A Beast is something more and less than fully human, but they aren't totally inhuman until they reach Inheritance. Hell, Inheritance is pretty specifically something for Beasts who can't take the strain between their monstrous and human selves anymore. <br /> <br /> Now, as to what makes this conflict compelling to me, why I find this game so personally important.<br /> <br /> This is painful to talk about, but I have a strong sadistic streak and I <b>HATE</b> it. I have intrusive thoughts a lot and for a long, long time I didn't know that was a thing that happens to lots of people. It's terrifying to get those destructive impulses, and I couldn't tell anyone about it because I couldn't let them know that I was a monster. That I thought about doing really bad things, a lot. Not because I wanted to, but because I couldn't control my thoughts. I wanted to be a trustworthy person so badly, but it felt like a deception. It was a constant battle, not just to resist the intrusive thoughts (relatively easy, although disgusting and scary) but also to never let slip a hint that I was struggling with them (exhausting and demoralizing). It was, quite literally, killing me. I have high blood pressure and I spent years refusing to treat it even when I was getting turned away from blood drives due to critical hypertension, because I wanted to die. I couldn't commit an obvious act of suicide because there are way too many people who would blame themselves for not doing something, but if I succumbed to a freak illness? Well, he was just so stubborn. He was young and he thought he was invincible. I got help and I'm on medication to control my BP now, but it took a long time slowly revealing this shit to some trusted friends and learning that sadism and intrusive thoughts are fairly common and do not make me a monster.<br /> <br /> So when I started reading Beast it really clicked for me. These are people who have a monster in their head driving them to commit horrible acts, but unlike me they don't have the option of telling it to shut the fuck up. If they do it eventually rampages on its own, so something has to give. Maybe it's their conscience, they find it's just easier to wallow in their monstrosity. Maybe it's their humanity, they kill off that part of themselves to achieve Inheritance. Or maybe, just maybe they find a way to put it to constructive ends. They join a Freehold of Changelings and sate their hungers on the servants of the Gentry, supplementing themselves with Family Dinner when the Changelings harvest Glamour. Or they join a Pack of Werewolves and help hunt the hostile spirits and Pure, feeding that way. There are options. None of them are harmless, but some are pretty close, and maybe you can live with that.<br /> <br /> I get Heroes too. I know what it's like to see a monster nobody else sees, and to think: <i>This thing needs to <b>die</b></i>. I know what it's like to want to be the good guy so very badly, and to think there can be no compromise with monsters, even when they fake humanity and have a family that cares about them. It's terrifying to be the focus of that kind of rage, and on the other end to finally realize just what you almost did.<br /> <br /> And that's why family is so important. Other Beasts, and more broadly other supernaturals. People to show you how to be a monster while still being a person, people to help you manage the unmanageable, people who will stick up for you when the rest of the world says &quot;you don't belong.&quot; I might not be here if not for several friends who showed me I wasn't alone in dealing with these things. Beasts can teach you how to be a better Beast, more judicious, more responsible (or not), but other supernats have a whole lot to offer in the way of helping to find more community friendly ways of feeding, which is why I find Beast works much better as part of a crossover. Start thinking about what your favorite line has to offer Beasts, and what Beasts can offer in return, that's where the game really shines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T06:33:11-07:00","id":912766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Beast Corebook</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912587#post912587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>From a Beast\u2019s perspective, mages are the one child in a family who went to college; she comes to family gatherings with her mind on experiences she can\u2019t share and vocabulary her kin can\u2019t understand. Her family feels threatened, and she feels alienated by their reaction. A Beast who takes the time to explore his Kinship with the Awakened finds they have more in common than they think (. . . )</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh God I was riiiiiight... Beast crossover is Goofy. I don't mean the adjective, I mean the Disney character. You're the original monster, you're straight from the source, and it's old and powerful. But you're all out of touch with the youth, and need to learn from your younger, hipper relatives how to be cool and with it if you really wanna teach lessons. &quot;Damnit, you keep messing things up! You killed people in the middle of a mall! That's not what I wanted you to do when I was complaining about Belial's Brood!&quot; &quot;Gorsh, Max, I just wanted your friends to think I was cool...&quot; It's <i>An Extremely Goofy Movie</i> aaaaaaa<br /> As an aside, I think &quot;Teaching Lessons&quot; is a much better focus than &quot;teaching lessons through fear&quot;. I think my own personal biggest problem with Beast is that it's so tied to spooking people. It sort of shoots itself in the foot in that regard. Or at least puts itself in thumbcuffs. Besides, if you allow for non-spooking lessons, you can get inspiration from a Disney remake of a Rodney Dangerfield movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T13:00:51-07:00","id":912956,"title":"","content":"That seems a pretty extreme reading. There's no reason to read that as even trying to imply that Beasts are stupid and unthinking in their actions.<br /> <br /> Beasts might be a bit &quot;out of touch&quot; with their fellow monsters, but they gain power by understanding them; not being Goofy. Forming Kinship bonds is a matter of actually understanding and no longer being out of touch; not a constant state of being the old dog that can't learn new tricks (since, well, you explicitly learn new tricks from Kinship). Beasts aren't (inherently) stupid. You don't have to constantly worry about Monkey's Paw results whenever you ask one for a favor. You might have to worry about them doing things that benefit them instead of you, but that's true for non-Beasts as well. A vampire trying to turn a Beast loose on the Belial's Brood is more far likely to run into the Beast deciding that the Brood are just as interesting to bond with as other vampires, than the vampire is going to need to worry about the Beast being an idiot and killing lots of people in a public space.<br /> <br /> A Beast is only a &quot;Goofy&quot; if you make them one. As written, they're far more likely to be a Littlefinger when things go poorly for the relationship.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> And the book does allow for &quot;non-spooking&quot; lessons. Lesson teaching is ultimately a philosophic choice by a Beast, including how they go around doing it. What matters for them is feeding their Hunger (which there's multiple Hungers, not just &quot;spook&quot; people). The lessons provoked by feeding their Hunger are whatever the Beast wants them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T14:18:43-07:00","id":912994,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> The plot to <i>An Extremely Goofy Movie</i> is that Goofy is going back to college and trying to hang out with Max (it's essentially <i>Back to School</i> with Goofy instead of Rodney Dangerfield). He's an old dog (literally) trying to learn new tricks. And, yeah, the default reason for crossing over is &quot;you can learn from these people&quot;, so it's close enough of an idea for me to make a joking metaphor.<br /> <br /> The problem for me is that Beast feed on fear. All the Hungers ultimately come back to fear or close to it. Beasts can't feed by not being dicks, unless they use Family Dinner. Tying &quot;well I guess we teach lessons&quot; into that works well as in-character justification, but it starts to get in the way of things when you can teach lessons without fear but still have to feed your Hunger through negativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:55:18-07:00","id":913050,"title":"","content":"This topic made me into incorporating a beast detective character that looks in to weird cases for new Chambers and looking over for other supernatural family to join him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will make a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective\">topic for him</a> as I think it can be cool NPC to throw in normal splats games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:35:45-07:00","id":913242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=912994#post912994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;617&quot;]The problem for me is that Beast feed on fear. All the Hungers ultimately come back to fear or close to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Hungers can be twisted back towards fears in a very abstract sense, they aren't about feeding on fear directly. Emotional harm? Yes. But a Collector doesn't have to make you fear for anything while they take something dear to you. They just have to take it. Satiety levels matter for the likely impact this has on the target (a low Satiety Collector can pretty much get away with causing no mental harm what-so-ever if they're clever about it), but the rarity of the item sates the Hunger for the Hoard; not the damage it does to those taken from.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for power can be sated by beating the shit out of the local gang's toughest fighter. Sure, some people might fear you for being that much more badass, but plenty of people might look up to you for being the one to stand up to that asshole, and start to idolize you. It doesn't matter, fear or adoration because you've shown you're the dominant one in the situation is what matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts can't feed by not being dicks, unless they use Family Dinner. </div> </div> </div>They can't feed by not doing things that are ultimately selfish. Curb stomping the local gangs as per my example above is only a &quot;dick&quot; move depending on a lot of personal moral philosophy. Kant might say that it is immoral because you're breaking the law, and causing harm, for the sole reason of feeling like the alpha dog. Mills might argue that you're actually being a good person, because not only is the harm of beating someone up less than the good of breaking a gang's control over the local populace, but sating the Hunger is also better for the local community than having it run wild; so choosing a morally acceptable outlet for it is actually a good thing.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine Utilitarian family ethics are fairly popular among the Beasts that think hard on such things, because it supports the idea that they're not being dicks while being monsters if they put in the effort to feed in a careful and deliberate way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tying &quot;well I guess we teach lessons&quot; into that works well as in-character justification, but it starts to get in the way of things when you can teach lessons without fear but still have to feed your Hunger through negativity. </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> What stops a Beast from teaching someone a lesson even if it doesn't result in something they can feed their Hunger on if they <i>want</i> to teach the lesson anyway?<br /> <br /> There can, of course, be complications in-character, but those are good things because they make the story more interesting. But I don't see what &quot;starts to get in the way,&quot; here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:43:07-07:00","id":913265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913242#post913242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>They can't feed by not doing things that are ultimately selfish.</b> Curb stomping the local gangs as per my example above is only a &quot;dick&quot; move depending on a lot of personal moral philosophy. Kant might say that it is immoral because you're breaking the law, and causing harm, for the sole reason of feeling like the alpha dog. Mills might argue that you're actually being a good person, because not only is the harm of beating someone up less than the good of breaking a gang's control over the local populace, but sating the Hunger is also better for the local community than having it run wild; so choosing a morally acceptable outlet for it is actually a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly there's a philosopher who's name escapes me at the moment who would argue that such a thing is no different from a normal human. The philisophical argument was basically that people can not actually be purely altruistic as even if we do not benefit in any way from it and are doing an action purely because our moral code says we have to, still is selfish because we are making ourselves feel good by following our moral code. I figure that particular train of thought ends up in the heads of a lot of Beasts when they get conflicted about their nature. <br /> <br /> Good Job Heavy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:57:25-07:00","id":913268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913242#post913242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Hungers can be twisted back towards fears in a very abstract sense, they aren't about feeding on fear directly. Emotional harm? Yes. But a Collector doesn't have to make you fear for anything while they take something dear to you. They just have to take it. Satiety levels matter for the likely impact this has on the target (a low Satiety Collector can pretty much get away with causing no mental harm what-so-ever if they're clever about it), but the rarity of the item sates the Hunger for the Hoard; not the damage it does to those taken from.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for power can be sated by beating the shit out of the local gang's toughest fighter. Sure, some people might fear you for being that much more badass, but plenty of people might look up to you for being the one to stand up to that asshole, and start to idolize you. It doesn't matter, fear or adoration because you've shown you're the dominant one in the situation is what matters.<br /> <br /> (. . .)<br /> <br /> They can't feed by not doing things that are ultimately selfish. Curb stomping the local gangs as per my example above is only a &quot;dick&quot; move depending on a lot of personal moral philosophy. Kant might say that it is immoral because you're breaking the law, and causing harm, for the sole reason of feeling like the alpha dog. Mills might argue that you're actually being a good person, because not only is the harm of beating someone up less than the good of breaking a gang's control over the local populace, but sating the Hunger is also better for the local community than having it run wild; so choosing a morally acceptable outlet for it is actually a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something that often gets lost in discussions of <i>Beast</i>. There is enough evil in the nWoD/CoD setting that an army of Beasts could gorge every night for a year, and not once harm an innocent. The signature character of the line is a Nemesis who preys on bullies at school, protecting the weaker kids. A Collector is free to pull a Robin Hood, stealing from the (evil) rich to give to the poor. A Ravager can feed on the destruction of drug labs (and worse). And that's before you even begin to factor in supernatural evil. Can anyone really say that its wrong for a Beast to break up a slavery ring that sells orphans to vampires?<br /> <br /> So you can still play a &quot;superhero&quot; game with Beasts, if you want. Sure, the nature of a Beast tends to skew them more to the antihero/vigilante-type . . . .But there's no reason they can't put on a cape, and go out and save the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:39:43-07:00","id":913287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913265#post913265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusingly there's a philosopher who's name escapes me at the moment who would argue that such a thing is no different from a normal human. The philisophical argument was basically that people can not actually be purely altruistic as even if we do not benefit in any way from it and are doing an action purely because our moral code says we have to, still is selfish because we are making ourselves feel good by following our moral code. I figure that particular train of thought ends up in the heads of a lot of Beasts when they get conflicted about their nature.<br /> <br /> Good Job Heavy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure which philosopher you're thinking of, but any of the egoists would follow this line of thinking, since the unifying trait of egoism is that self-interest is the only true motivator of human behavior, and enlightened self-interest is the foundation of ethical and moral behavior.<br /> <br /> While I don't want to argue the real world merits of such things, I'd imagine egoist Beasts aren't the best PC material because it's hard for them to maintain the idea that enlightened self-interest is often communally focused. Humans are social animals that rely on each other for survival as a species, so our self-interest is frequently in line with doing &quot;good&quot; and &quot;nice&quot; things for each other to keep society going. Beasts, separated from humanity, are less likely to hold on to the idea that mutualistic relationships with humans have long term merit. That said, it is functional and would probably work well in a mixed game (since Kinship with other supernaturals can replace that) or for stable but not-nice NPCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913268#post913268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can still play a &quot;superhero&quot; game with Beasts, if you want. Sure, the nature of a Beast tends to skew them more to the antihero/vigilante-type . . . .But there's no reason they can't put on a cape, and go out and save the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've even had threads about Batman and Ghost Riders done up as Beasts.<br /> <br /> Since most superheros are also vigilantes in some sense (few are direct agents of the law and all), it's surprisingly easy to twist most of them into Beasts. Even ones that are much &quot;lighter&quot; than the dark heroes that come to mind first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T01:02:39-07:00","id":913291,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I'm pretty sure both Act and Rule Utilitarianism would be against putting someone's face on the sidewalk ledge and stepping on the back of their head until their teeth and jaws shatter. I mean, I agree that you can be a vigilante in Beast, but you're encouraged to ignore &quot;let the punishment fit the crime&quot;. In the original version of the bit of fluff, Sin-You killed the trucker for being an asshole. When bullies come up, they're psychologically tortured in a way that is worse than what they did to deserve it. I mean, Dexter came up earlier, and feeding like that <i>is</i> perfectly viable. If I remember, the Feeding system still encourages you to go overboard and kill. And that's ultimately what my problem was. Adding on &quot;we teach lessons&quot; doesn't actually have any sort of benefit besides maybe letting your Beast sleep at night (but since you have a Horror instead of a Soul, it's more like letting the player sleep at night; and it was after all a hastily conjured way to make the game feel less abusive, that isn't exactly worked in well). It'd be nice if the Lessons and the Feeding parts were more tied together.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> I've always found that kind of argument to be pretty silly. Terms like &quot;edgy&quot; and &quot;fedora&quot; come to mind. Getting a good sense of self is rarely equivalent to the good you actually do, but that kind of moral philosophy treats it as being roughly equivalent to gold<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4624\" data-vbnamecard=\"4624\">One Vorlon</a> Iunno, I've brought it up a lot before. The issue comes up that it's encouraged to feed as abusively as possible. I don't necessarily mind it, and I'm fine with Vampion Beast, but it can feel tonally dissonant. As an aside, Batman is a great Beast because, frankly, he does no real good. Bruce Wayne has enough money that he could probably create housing for all of Gotham's homeless, but instead he'd rather punch and cripple criminals. Netflix's Daredevil is a better example, since he admits he does it because he enjoys it much more often.<br /> I mean, not that &quot;Vampion&quot; style gameplay is ever worried about morality; that tends to be more Punisher, from what I hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T01:56:25-07:00","id":913309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913291#post913291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure both Act and Rule Utilitarianism would be against putting someone's face on the sidewalk ledge and stepping on the back of their head until their teeth and jaws shatter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the fact that Act and Rule are not the only two forms of utilitarian thought, not really. Utilitarianism doesn't prohibit specific actions in a vacuum; that's sort of the whole point. While I meant my use of the phrase curb stomp figuratively over literally, it would still have to be seen in the light of an analysis of utility. Act utilitarianism is actually pretty easy to use to justify such things (part of some of its major criticisms), because it argues that each act is individual and you don't have to worry about creating moral rules that stem from how you apply utility to a given situation.<br /> <br /> You're also ignoring how Hunger would interplay with utilitarian thought. Since sating Hunger is generally better than starving until bad stuff happens on its own, any situation that allows you to sate your Hunger with out tipping the scales of utility into overall harm would be a net positive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, I agree that you can be a vigilante in Beast, but you're encouraged to ignore &quot;let the punishment fit the crime&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> First off, the idea that you &quot;ignore&quot; this only applies to sating the Hunger for Punishment. And you don't have to ignore just punishment options, it just isn't what matters to sating the Hunger. Punishing transgressions is what matters, and the more punishing (even out of proportion for the crime) the more potential to sate.<br /> <br /> Second, encouraged isn't really present. The book is stating what actually sates the different Hungers, not what the characters should or shouldn't do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I remember, the Feeding system still encourages you to go overboard and kill. </div> </div> </div>Killing is a bonus to the roll.<br /> <br /> But that's not inherently a good/encouraged thing. Overfeeding in Beast is a pretty bad thing because it means getting stuck with the Slumbering Condition.<br /> <br /> If you have Low Satiety and you need a fast meal, killing can help a lot. If you have time to plan and considering your feeding, there are other options that are easily equal to killing (and can make it so that killing doesn't have any additional mechanical impact).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd be nice if the Lessons and the Feeding parts were more tied together. </div> </div> </div>No, it wouldn't. If Feeding and teaching lessons were more tied together, the lessons aspect is no longer a philosophic choice by the Beast, but a optimization choice by the player. Leaving them separate is important because it stresses that trying to be &quot;good&quot; is not something a Beast has to do to maintain their existence. It's something they choose to do for their own personal reasons.<br /> <br /> As for this being &quot;tacked on,&quot; remember that Beasts have Legends and Lives. A Beast's Life is always part of the character even if these sorts of conversations tend to skip over it. Lessons are a balancing point between Legend and Life, not a Feeding modifier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue comes up that it's encouraged to feed as abusively as possible. </div> </div> </div>Again, this isn't accurate. You get the most dice on your Feeding roll for indulging your Hunger as much as possible. For some Hungers this is more likely to be abusive than others, but the point is never actually abuse itself. As well, having a lot of dice for Feeding isn't inherently good for you mechanically, and thus isn't inherently &quot;encouraged&quot; just because it means more dice. Low dice-pools more frequently are easier to ensure you stay in the Satiety levels you want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T02:27:27-07:00","id":913318,"title":"","content":"First don't bring fedoras into it it just makes you sound silly. Particularly since the entire case was merely pointing out that there is a school of thought that says that doing something good because it benefits you does not immediately make you a bad person since people are always trying to get at least some self benefit out of good acts. Whether or not you agree is irrelevant since the point was merely to bring up that such a school of thought exists. <br /> <br /> Now onto your other complaints. The Horror the part that actually feeds is basically pure Id. Of course the lessons are barely relevant to feeding, that's part of the point. Your Horror doesn't care what you're doing so long as it gets fed. If decide to take out a group of thugs your Horror's only concern in how you deal with them is the feeding (and you not dying, but not entirely relevant to topic) it won't judge you less if you decide to off the lot of them or spare them. It won't care about your reasoning if you decide to kill them all to prevent them harming anyone else the Horror doesn't pay any more attention than if you had let them all live because dead people turn up more of an investigation than just a bunch of people beaten bloody.<br /> <br /> To put it simply. Of course the game's system favors the play of the over the top monster to Mother Teresa. You have the power, you have societal justification (teaching lessons to make the world better), and environmental justification (if you don't feed your Horror will feed on it's terms, and you need to feed to survive), and you can go as nuts as you want and likely never feel bad. You want to teach people to lock their doors, so do you go do some research and start handing out pamphlets that handle crime statistics, do you break into a few people's houses and let them see a burglar who panicked and left without their loot, do you actually rob the people, do you walk into someone's house and redecorate the place with the viscera of all who lived there? None of it is going to hamper your sleep tonight, so how do you handle it? Your power set isn't derived from the Justice League or the Avengers your power set is derived from Hellsing's Alucard. So are you going to try and be a good person despite the difficulties therein or are you just going to take the easy way and disembowel a few people for your convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T14:59:57-07:00","id":913675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> When I say that you're meant to ignore &quot;let the punishment fit the crime&quot;, I don't just mean in regards to Hunger for Punishment. Whatever way you feed, you're encouraged to do it as much and as big as possible. The feeding rules encourage a hammer, not a scalpel. Killing is a bonus to the roll, which is why it's encouraged. It's also really hard to go overboard, since the rules don't really provide enough threat or flexibility for you to ever overfeed unintentionally. You can keep saying that things aren't encouraged, but there is a clear mechanical incentive. Yeah, low dice pools but being a dick more often is possible, but now we get back into one of the more common complaints about Beast.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> My point is that because the two are mutually exclusive, there's ludonarrative dissonance. No matter what kind of changes to your personality or attitude or even body the Beast as through crossover experience, they're still all about Badfeels and can only tap into the scary darkbad part of the Temenos. Also, man, looking over the Kinship Nightmares again I'm reminded that Beast really isn't for everyone. It's hard to even <i>be</i> Mother Theresa. Beast in my opinion is a game that would benefit greatly from a morality meter but doesn't have one. This game is all carrot, no stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:37:58-07:00","id":913723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913675#post913675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[When I say that you're meant to ignore &quot;let the punishment fit the crime&quot;, I don't just mean in regards to Hunger for Punishment. Whatever way you feed, you're encouraged to do it as much and as big as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... you might want to work on your phrasing. Because those are not equivalent statements. And it's particularly misleading to use phrases that are explicitly referenced in one of the Hungers.<br /> <br /> And you're still wrong about &quot;encouragement&quot; because it assumes that having the most dice possible and getting the most successes possible is the optimal result.<br /> <br /> When there's a Merit in the book that lets you <i>lower</i> your feeding roll, it says something about whether dice bonus = encouragement to do whatever grants that bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The feeding rules encourage a hammer, not a scalpel. </div> </div> </div>The rules reward both. It's very easy to use the scalpel and gain as big of a bonus as killing does, and you can opt to not go for various options if you want to reduce your risk of overfeeding, while killing is a flat modifier that you'd have to purposefully try to negate if you don't want to go overboard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also really hard to go overboard, since the rules don't really provide enough threat or flexibility for you to ever overfeed unintentionally. </div> </div> </div>If you have 7 Satiety, and you kill to feed, you're looking at 9 dice... which is really easy to hit 10 Satiety with, and unlikely to result in an exceptional success. Then you're Slumbering, which sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, low dice pools but being a dick more often is possible, but now we get back into one of the more common complaints about Beast. </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there. But it isn't going to work.<br /> <br /> Low dice pools and feeding more often is both possible, and less likely to result in having to engage in your Hunger in extreme fashions; <b>which isn't being a dick no matter how often you try to sneak it in as &quot;fact.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> This is a thread about selling people on Beast, not a thread for unselling people by posting repeatedly misleading statements about the text regardless of the number of times you're corrected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is that because the two are mutually exclusive, there's ludonarrative dissonance. </div> </div> </div>Since they're not actually mutually exclusive, the rest of this doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, man, looking over the Kinship Nightmares again I'm reminded that Beast really isn't for everyone. </div> </div> </div>Such is the truth of most games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This game is all carrot, no stick. </div> </div> </div>Yeah...no sticks in the Satiety Conditions... no sticks in Heroes... no sticks in non-mental consequences for your actions...no sticks at all...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T18:10:47-07:00","id":913774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913723#post913723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low dice pools and feeding more often is both possible, and less likely to result in having to engage in your Hunger in extreme fashions; <b>which isn't being a dick no matter how often you try to sneak it in as &quot;fact.&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Truth is spoken here.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms, in fact, has got this argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T18:51:57-07:00","id":913790,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> How is it an example of ludonarative dissonance? Many a Beast tries to justify their actions as right or not. With regards to feeding the game's narrative is &quot;Your character has been cast by the universe as the monster and it is rather insistent that you play the role of the monster. What do you do?&quot; In which case that the game makes it easy for you to be a complete monster is perfectly in keeping. Though I'm with Heavy your argument doesn't really work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T18:59:47-07:00","id":913795,"title":"","content":"See, the idea that there's no stick to discourage people from being as abusive as possible to feed ignores the fact that not wanting to be an intensely abusive person can be more than enough incentive by itself. The assumption seems to be that every Beast wants to feed as much as possible, and that just isn't true. Many Beasts feed because the alternatives, the Horror feeding on its own and eventual starvation, are worse. <br /> <br /> In fact, I would argue that the mechanics incentivizing more brutal feeding adds far more weight to choosing not to do that. It's easy to resist the temptation to do something nasty when it doesn't further your own self interest, taking the high road when it hurts you is far more interesting. I can see why people would be more comfortable with a more direct mechanical penalty for cruel behavior, but from where I'm standing it would take away from the narrative. How many games have binary morality choices that fall flat because the evil choice doesn't make things any easier, it's just evil for the sake of evil? Being good *should* be the difficult path, otherwise where's the significance in choosing it? There's no meaning in resisting a temptation that isn't tempting, that's just balking at rotten carrots.<br /> <br /> And that's not even considering that Low Satiety comes with some pretty hefty benefits that give you good reason to not want to go above it all that often. <br /> <br /> Of course, for some people the game serves as an unrestrained sadist fantasy. If that's the game they want to play, and it stays confined to the game? I'm glad they have an outlet.<br /> <br /> Really though, every Hunger has options for feeding in ways that deal minimal harm or even benefit the people around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T19:24:51-07:00","id":913800,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see that put to the test, considering that the core book describes even the seemingly most innocuous Hunger \u2014 collecting \u2014 as something that inherently causes suffering (you have to take something that someone else values away from them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:10:30-07:00","id":913822,"title":"","content":"Low Satiety feeding generally ignores the need to cause significant suffering. At low Satiety, pretty much anything that fits the Hunger works. A Collector that takes stamps can just steal stamps form the post office at low Satiety instead of having to find and steal rare and collectible stamps that are going to impact individuals that own them. A Tyrant can flash a wad of cash to get the best seat in a restaurant to show off how awesome they are and feed off the reactions at this. A Predator just needs to hunt something like taking a .22 and shooting a squirrel since challenge and even being human doesn't matter to one at low Satiety. A low Satiety Nemeses and Ravagers aren't as easy, but they can easily deal in short term sufferings that don't result in lasting trauma. Burning a drunk driver's car while he sleeps is punishment or destruction enough for low Satiety here, but for most people it's still a minor inconvenience via insurance and rentals.<br /> <br /> If your Beast prefers to hover between Moderate and Low Satiety, they can easily stack on minor bonuses for 6-8 dice, which is more than enough to move from Low to Moderate in roll on average. <br /> <br /> So one feeding where you're at Low Satiety, but you take extra time (+2 or +4 bonus), perform the act a few times during the scene (+2), it's oriented around your character's preferences (+1), and deals with a current Aspiration (+1, +2 if you fulfill it), you can do something pretty minor and still have a nice feeding roll out of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:10:53-07:00","id":913823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913800#post913800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see that put to the test, considering that the core book describes even the seemingly most innocuous Hunger \u2014 collecting \u2014 as something that inherently causes suffering (you have to take something that someone else values away from them).</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that a lot of people keep describing feeding Hunger in vastly misleading terms like &quot;abuse&quot; and &quot;suffering&quot; is skewing the read. Before everything else, you feed the Horror through <i>shock</i>.<br /> <br /> I was in a car accident a year or two back. I came out of it uninjured and, outside of the immediate consequences of colliding with a moving vehicle and having to experience the relevant paperwork and make the relevant phone calls for the first time in my life, untraumatized.<br /> <br /> I still learned very definitely to stay vigilant behind the wheel, and the lack of lasting damage to my mind and body would not have disqualified that moment of shock as a feeding opportunity had the guy in the other car been a Ravager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:13:11-07:00","id":913825,"title":"","content":"Power: It's pretty easy to spin a Hunger for Power into an &quot;I want to be the very best&quot; type of journey, and there's nothing saying the power you get has to be abused or unearned to qualify. Climbing the company ladder could mean backstabbing, but it could also come from merit and long hours. Becoming an MMA champion means punching a lot of people in the face, but they accepted that risk when they entered the ring. Power can also mean the strength to defend those weaker than yourself. One of my all time favorite characters, Drake Thorn, is an Anakim who joined the Summer Court. Changelings have a lot of powerful enemies, so Drake is rarely without an opportunity to demonstrate his considerable martial prowess. Protecting Changelings from Arcadian kidnappers is pretty damn heroic, I'd say. <br /> <br /> Hoard: This one is kind of weird, because a lot of the examples in the corebook aren't really things most people value. Roadkill and cracked safes are two examples, which lends to the idea that some hoards have value only to the owner. But, even sticking to things other people do value: Grace is an incredibly competitive athlete. She'll try any sport if there's a trophy to be won, and when she can't find trophies she'll make bets. Whatever someone is willing to wager, as long as she can win it fair and square in a competition. If she's starving she's willing to bend the fair and square bit, but for the most part she earned each item in the vast pile of trophies in her lair.<br /> <br /> Punishment: Pretty easy, and even straight up legal in many cases. The prosecutor who makes sure the guilty are convicted as such, etc. Anybody who works through legal channels and does their job strictly but by the book has plenty of opportunity to feed without causing undue harm. <br /> <br /> Prey: Straight from the Core &quot;The victim needs to be at the Beast's mercy ...[but] the victim doesn't need to know it.&quot; Killing is not required (some Horrors are exceptions but that's the general rule). See the Reaper from my earlier post. Just about every night she deals with people on death's doorstep, but she saves every one she can. It's enough that they know she was the only thing keeping them alive, and if they live more judiciously because of it so much the better<br /> <br /> Ruin: This was the hardest Hunger for me to paint positively until I remembered how sometimes fire has to purge old growth before new growth can begin Some things need to be broken, either because they're toxic and people won't acknowledge it, or because they need fixing and nobody sees it yet. Ravagers can be the ones to lance the boil and force a painful but rapid healing in place of lingering decay. TJ works with the Dawn Court to promote change and growth. Sometimes when the municipal government is dragging its feet with funding for social programs a select bit of arson or vandalism can convince them there's a problem to be addressed, and TJ's the man for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:26:20-07:00","id":913833,"title":"","content":"Ravager dream job: Demolition technician.<br /> <br /> Am I the only picturing a Predator, Tyrant duo who's favored hobby are paintball tournaments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:52:24-07:00","id":913841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913823#post913823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that a lot of people keep describing feeding Hunger in vastly misleading terms like &quot;abuse&quot; and &quot;suffering&quot; is skewing the read. Before everything else, you feed the Horror through <i>shock</i>.<br /> <br /> I was in a car accident a year or two back. I came out of it uninjured and, outside of the immediate consequences of colliding with a moving vehicle and having to experience the relevant paperwork and make the relevant phone calls for the first time in my life, untraumatized.<br /> <br /> I still learned very definitely to stay vigilant behind the wheel, and the lack of lasting damage to my mind and body would not have disqualified that moment of shock as a feeding opportunity had the guy in the other car been a Ravager.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>All of this.</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:26:20-07:00","id":913857,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> You know, it really irritates me the way that you go through my post sentence by sentence instead of as a coherent whole. We're talking about how any Beast could be a vigilante, and only harm &quot;bad people&quot;. So, yes, the punishment--little p--doesn't need to fit the crime, and there is mechanical incentive to go all out. That Hunger Management lets you remove dice from your feeding pool isn't as useful as the fact that it allows you to remove dice, since you can just... not do more things in the first place. Each dice bonus on the Satiety roll represents something you actively have to work at. If you don't consider that a mechanical incentive, then that's just something we're going to disagree with.<br /> Likewise, &quot;if you're in this situation and you do this thing&quot; is not really a counter to me pointing out that you need to be in very specific situations. If you're at 7 Satiety, there's really very little incentive to feed in the first place. Even if you did (maybe you feel you need to &quot;bank&quot; some Satiety so you can spend it while you do something) you could also just spend a point of Willpower. It's possible to get three successes on five dice, but difficult. You could also spend a Satiety on the hunt, which drops you down to 6 but doesn't increase the Satiety roll passed 10. If I'm understanding right (I might not be), you can also just do a small petty feeding that murders someone. A Collector with an Aspiration of &quot;get a new watch&quot; killing some rich man over his watch. Provided you have 7 dice, you still roll Satiety. If you disagree on whether you <i>need to be a dick</i>, that's really just a quibble. The description of <i>shock</i> certainly spells out that you have to in some way effect someone, though, and most people would argue that abusing power, stealing, enforcing your own morality, chasing, or destroying are all &quot;being a dick&quot;.<br /> Although, as an aside, we're now... took me all day to write the post, 146 posts. If someone hasn't made up their mind by now, nothing anyone says for or against Beast is likely to change that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913723#post913723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...no sticks in the Satiety Conditions... no sticks in Heroes... no sticks in non-mental consequences for your actions...no sticks at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Easily managed, nonthreatening, and generally ignored, in order. Other games have mechanical incentives and punishments that help the themes of both the game and the gameline. Beast doesn't, because it eschews the Morality system that's so often lurking in the background of the other games. Humanity highlights how much of a monster you're becoming, and Touchstones give incentives to keep from ignoring everything but the Beast (the vampire one, since comparing these two games about feeding your hunger is needlessly confusing). Harmony, lopsided as it is, helps underscore the fact that you have competing natures. Beast doesn't really have mechanics that punish you. Satiety is easily managed, and Heroes <i>aren't</i> created by Beasts. People tend to ignore or unintentionally forget non-mechanical drawbacks, like &quot;feeling bad&quot;.<br /> But yes, you're right, this thread is about selling people on Beast, not unselling them. I'm not really trying to &quot;unsell&quot; anyone. I just don't ascribe to the school of thought that to sell something you need to lie about or ignore its shortcomings. It's not like I came into the thread to say how terrible the game is in the first place; I was throwing in my two cents for why people might like Beast. I'm just also pointing out ways that I feel it falls short, which you clearly don't agree with.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913774#post913774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms, in fact, has got this argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? This isn't some contest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913790#post913790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> How is it an example of ludonarative dissonance? Many a Beast tries to justify their actions as right or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why it's dissonant. That's the only story you can tell. As written, a Beast is not able to feed &quot;safely&quot;. It's not like Vampire where the parasitism metaphor can be stretched to the point that you do very little harm and feed safely from your willing blood dolls. You <i>have</i> to do harm. And since you need to get Potential Satiety over your current Satiety, that often means doing a lot of harm. That you do harm and justify it with &quot;this is for your own good&quot; is why a lot of people see Beast as an abuse metaphor. And it would be nice if you could move beyond that. Consider for a moment &quot;shock&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feeding, page 108, bolded for emphasis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts feed by satisfying their Hungers. Doing so can be as simple as a Tyrant shoving a victim up against a wall and screaming in his face, or as elaborate as a Ravager slowly dismantling a victim\u2019s life, piece by piece, until he\u2019s either completely ruined or he breaks off contact with the Beast. In either case, the moment of feeding happens when the victim experiences the <i>shock</i>.<br /> <b>The shock happens at the moment where a victim realizes what is happening. If he learns a lesson, the shock is the instant in which it crystalizes. Beasts liken the shock to the moment when one awakens, startled, from a nightmare</b> \u2014 a moment that every Beast is well familiar with, having experienced it many times before the Devouring. This comparison is not completely apt, however; a victim can also experience the shock at the moment of death.<br /> Shock is not dissimilar to a breaking point for Integrity (see p. 155) insofar as it impacts the victim\u2019s soul. A shock can be a breaking point, but it doesn\u2019t need to be. <b>The important thing is that the victim\u2019s unconscious response impacts the Primordial Dream</b>, strengthening the Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now, let's put aside how reasonable a conclusion it is whether or not &quot;lock your doors&quot; constitutes a lesson, as if all Beasts were members of <s><a href=\"http://metalgear.wikia.com/wiki/Dead_Cell\" target=\"_blank\">Dead</a></s><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Cell\" target=\"_blank\">Red Cell</a>, testing out security weaknesses by staging fake terrorist attacks. <i>Shock</i> is a moment of profound realization. Why does this have to come at the result of harm? Why does only negative emotion strengthen the Primordial Dream? Yes, yes, it's the Darkbad Shadowlands of the Temenos, but that's part of the problem. It's kind of arbitrary. Why shouldn't a Beast be able to work <i>with</i> their Horror when they change their outlook and work towards actually doing good in the world? If the Beast can potentially learn positive, helpful traits (even if they really only benefit those they have Kinship with), why can't they alter their Beast to not feed from misery? Maybe an example would be in order.<br /> <br /> You're a Beast. You buy into the notion of teaching Lessons. You could try to teach a lesson against assault by assaulting someone. It's big, bad, harmful, gorges the Beast, and says &quot;see how you like when it's done to you&quot;. That's more or less what the book encourages you to do. But let's be honest, in the real world if people having bad things done to them ever actually taught them a lesson, we wouldn't live in such a crappy world that isn't a <s>World</s>Chronicle of Darkness. More often than not, the lesson people get taught is &quot;no one cares about you&quot; or even &quot;this is normal, so it will be okay when you do it&quot;. There's a reason abused kids grow up to be abusers. It's because their parents taught through example that abuse is an acceptable response.<br /> But, <i><b>what if</b></i> instead of beating someone up or raping them or stealing their shit or abusing your authority over them, you instead make them empathize? What if instead of tormenting them you make them feel <i>for</i> someone <i>else</i>, instead of for themselves. What if you do something like <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6s3Fx0lq9Ws\" target=\"_blank\">this ad</a> to cause <i>shock</i>? What about making someone realize the gays are just like them? The book would have you teach a bully a Lesson the old fashioned way, bullying them right back and making them to afraid to retaliate, but why can't you feed from the <i>shock</i> of showing them that the people they torment are just like them? I mean, I know the reason; &quot;teach a Lesson&quot; was thrown in at the last minute to appease people because Beast's first draft was received negatively. It's not a bad idea, but by necessity as a last minute addition, it's pretty much tacked on.<br /> <br /> Hopefully in a Player's Guide or STG, we will see ways to feed that don't have to directly involve harming people. Even if it was <i>harder</i> to feed this way, it would at least be something working towards that theme of teaching a lesson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-14-2016, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:43:36-07:00","id":913861,"title":"","content":"It isn't a contest, and yet when someone's wrong and someone's right....Well, someone's wrong and someone's right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:49:55-07:00","id":913862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913795#post913795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the idea that there's no stick to discourage people from being as abusive as possible to feed ignores the fact that not wanting to be an intensely abusive person can be more than enough incentive by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but then we get into the reality of how easy it is to ignore or forget about things when they don't have mechanical weight. There's a reason in D&amp;D characters are commonly characterized as murderhobos. Killing isn't punished, and neither is looting. Even Lawful Good paladins are better off taking everything not nailed down and murdering the bandits that are terrorizing the village. It's only a problem when one of them swears mercy, and God forbid one of them be a race that's Always Evil. Beast doesn't have mechanics to reinforce it's themes, or at least none that do it well in my opinion. The closest would be the fact that almost everything you do is horrible and abusive. It also doesn't even have to be a &quot;binary morality choice&quot;. Consider that Integrity isn't that, it's what shakes your view of the world. Humanity likewise is less about morality and more about monstrosity. Several things in Werewolf that are good for your Harmony are not very moral. It's also important to note that <i>even with Breaking Points and Persistent mental Conditions, it is often easier, safer, faster, and more beneficial to do the wrong thing</i>. Good is punished in the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness by restricting you. Bad is punished by freeing you, but in such a way that you have long term consequences. That's why the original <i>Bioshock</i> was praised, even though it's morality choices were pretty simple, and even fell down to a mechanical incentive: Harvest Adam now and kill the Little Sister, or save the Little Sister and get a better bonus down the line.<br /> In the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness, the Good path <i>is</i> the difficult path, but you're still incentivized to take it simply because psychologically having a number drop is a big deal. I mean, there have actually been studies; I wish I could find it, but one country or county or whatever switched from <i>adding</i> points for violations to <i>removing</i> points. Turns out if you take something away, people are more likely to care. If you add something, well, high score time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, for some people the game serves as an unrestrained sadist fantasy. If that's the game they want to play, and it stays confined to the game? I'm glad they have an outlet </div> </div> </div>And that's fine. But, I mean, one of the concerns that a lot of people have (and why they'd need to be sold on the game) is that Beast's reputation is &quot;it's a game about being an abuser&quot;. And since currently the only examples of <i>shock</i> are through abuse, that's a big sticking point with a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Which is why, frankly, if I were selling someone on the game I'd focus on the other aspects of it, while simply acknowledging that the &quot;be a big scary monster&quot; part is present, but can be downplayed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913822#post913822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety feeding generally ignores the need to cause significant suffering.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Shock</i> is necessary.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913823#post913823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that a lot of people keep describing feeding Hunger in vastly misleading terms like &quot;abuse&quot; and &quot;suffering&quot; is skewing the read. Before everything else, you feed the Horror through <i>shock</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913841#post913841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>All of this.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Every example of shock (including Satchel's) involves pain or harm.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Except that's not the case here. There's someone you agree with and someone you disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":".  I need to stop trying to be fancy with my BBCode 06-14-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:52:26-07:00","id":913864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913862#post913862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every example of shock (including Satchel's) involves pain or harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should I be clearer than &quot;uninjured and untraumatized&quot; when I specify that I was completely fine coming out of a frightening experience if I want you to never fucking make this claim again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913857#post913857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That you do harm and justify it with &quot;this is for your own good&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For at least the fifth time in recent memory: No.<br /> <br /> &quot;This has to happen in some fashion, so I may as well try and do some good with it&quot; is not &quot;I am doing this for your own good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Trying to get Unfortunate Necessity A to produce Positive Outcome B is not claiming Positive Outcome B is the reason Unfortunate Necessity A occurs.<br /> <br /> Preemptive damage-control is not self-deception and claiming the two are interchangeable requires something along the continuum between poor reading comprehension and outright bad faith, none of which are beneficial to a thread asking for people to make a case for why this game is worth trying. You're not helping. Start doing that or stop doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-14-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:13:46-07:00","id":913873,"title":"","content":"Wee... another lost post. New Firefox is unstable...<br /> <br /> Anyway... this is getting pointless. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> clearly doesn't want to either be sold on Beast, or seek clarification on how the game actually is. They want to spew out a bunch of misinformation about the game to knock it instead of just recognizing the game isn't for them and that's OK without having to show that there's something &quot;wrong&quot; with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:17:00-07:00","id":913874,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> The entire point of teaching a Lesson is that you're ostensibly doing it for the victim's benefit. You're <i>teaching</i> them something. I mean, nevermind that the argument is sort of silly. The Horror goes on a rampage if you have low Satiety, but it's unlikely to actually do harm unless you're a big bad powerful beastie with lots of Power and Lair. Especially when you get to Ravenous, where it's basically impossible to harm anyone, since it's a Chance die no matter how strong your Lair is. Preemptive damage control isn't self deception. Arguing that you're doing something to benefit someone when it benefits you and harms them <i>is</i>. In fact, that they're looking for justifications for their horrible actions is a reason people have for wanting to play Beast!<br /> <br /> Failing to acknowledge reasons why people don't want to play the game in the first place isn't helpful to a thread on why people should play the game, either. And don't act like I'm just threadcrapping. I came into this thread offering reasons to play the game. Heavy Arms just happened to jump on something I said when I acknowledged people's reasons for not wanting to play it. And if for some reason someone <i>still</i> hasn't made up their mind after 150 posts, that's sort of the thing you have to address. Which I not only did, I even offered a potential work around for people for whom that's a sticking point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Every time I've argued with you the last few days has been fruitless. I don't need to be sold on Beast. I don't hate Beast. I was <i>defending</i> Beast just two pages ago. I'm also not misinformed. I'm literally looking at the book. I quoted a page. I literally provided you a mechanical breakdown to show why I disagree with you. Do you just enjoy being dismissive or something? If we pretend that I am someone who needs to be sold on Beast, <i>in what way are you selling me on it?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-14-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:29:30-07:00","id":913877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913862#post913862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Except that's not the case here. There's someone you agree with and someone you disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure, and what would this past and future Beast freelancer know about the text and the game, am I right? Surely not enough to know when something is read correctly from the text or not.<br /> <br /> You'll excuse me if I don't defer to your take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-25-2020, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:38:47-07:00","id":913883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913874#post913874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> The entire point of teaching a Lesson is that you're ostensibly doing it for the victim's benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of &quot;teaching a lesson&quot; as a disconnected phrase divorced from context is, yes.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, like many things in the Chronicles of Darkness, being divorced from context renders the concept useless for understanding how it fits into the game.<br /> <br /> The &quot;teaching a lesson&quot; bit is an attempted modification to an immutable facet of Begotten existence such that it more fully reads &quot;using feeding your Hunger \u2014 which you have to do at some point because the alternative is dying \u2014 as an opportunity to impress upon people basic lessons in the same way that a child who puts their hand on a hot stove quickly learns not to put their hand on a hot stove.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're <i>teaching</i> them something. </div> </div> </div>As an alternative to <i>murdering them and leaving their body in a place where it will never be found</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, nevermind that the argument is sort of silly. The Horror goes on a rampage if you have low Satiety, but it's unlikely to actually do harm unless you're a big bad powerful beastie with lots of Power and Lair. Especially when you get to Ravenous, where it's basically impossible to harm anyone, since it's a Chance die no matter how strong your Lair is. </div> </div> </div>The Horror is a recurring nightmare by inclination and getting to Ravenous is better known as the point where your lack of activity has led to a direct threat to your life and a recurring signal beacon for several more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Preemptive damage control isn't self deception. Arguing that you're doing something to benefit someone when it benefits you and harms them <i>is</i>. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trying to lower the net harm done to a person by imparting experience that will ideally make them safer in the long run&quot; is not &quot;doing something to benefit someone&quot; and nobody has argued that it was in anything more than the broadest abstract of &quot;some Beasts believe the purpose given to them by the Dark Mother is to convey the wisdom of the Primordial Dream to people who would otherwise only learn it when it was too late.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:39:47-07:00","id":913885,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Did you write the Hungers? Because your &quot;here is our winner&quot; was in response to Heavy Arms saying you don't have to be a dick. Except that's kind of what all the Hungers are about. Here are our Low Satiety feedings: Robbery and mugging; various forms of intimidation; fighting or chasing someone; intimidation or assault; destroying something that will be remembered for at least a week or making a family cry. <i>That is all being a dick</i>. Even if you argue that you can do that to some criminal, or to teach a lesson, you are still being a dick, you're just making excuses for why you did it in the particular way you did.<br /> If you don't <i>agree</i> that it's being a dick, well, we're back to &quot;there's a person you agree with and a person you disagree with, not a winner&quot;. Besides, even if you did write that section, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Death_of_the_Author\" target=\"_blank\">you're the author, and therefore dead</a>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I feel like you're intentionally avoiding the thing that I'm actually trying to discuss. The theme of &quot;teaching lessons&quot; is not a strong one, and it has very little if any mechanical significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-14-2016, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:43:05-07:00","id":913889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913885#post913885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Did you write the Hungers? Because your &quot;here is our winner&quot; was in response to Heavy Arms saying you don't have to be a dick. Except that's kind of what all the Hungers are about. Here are our Low Satiety feedings: Robbery and mugging; various forms of intimidation; fighting or chasing someone; intimidation or assault; destroying something that will be remembered for at least a week or making a family cry. <i>That is all being a dick</i>. Even if you argue that you can do that to some criminal, or to teach a lesson, you are still being a dick, you're just making excuses for why you did it in the particular way you did.<br /> If you don't <i>agree</i> that it's being a dick, well, we're back to &quot;there's a person you agree with and a person you disagree with, not a winner&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh, it's like I have to personally write a section to have a point instead of being in the conversations with the various writer and the developer himself whenever they talk about how people have misconstrued the Hungers and how they can clarify these subjects in future books.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that the text is plenty clear on the subject.<br /> <br /> You'll excuse me if I do not defer to your opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-25-2020, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:47:54-07:00","id":913891,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> If it were clear, we wouldn't be having this conversation. Heck, if it was clear, there wouldn't even be conversations between the writing team about how it's misconstrued. This does, however, bode well for my hope that future books will allow feeding in ways other than causing people harm. If you're allowed to share anything with us, that might also help sell people on the book.<br /> <br /> As is, there's the strong implication that you have to harm others, and that it's the only way to feed without using alternative methods. Telling me that my opinion of the text is wrong doesn't help anything. Telling me the actual intent might. Because, again, <i>as presented in the book</i>, you have to do harm to feed, and doing more harm helps you feed better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:48:26-07:00","id":913892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913885#post913885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I feel like you're intentionally avoiding the thing that I'm actually trying to discuss. The theme of &quot;teaching lessons&quot; is not a strong one, and it has very little if any mechanical significance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not ask and neither did anybody else. This is not a thread for discussing the mechanical significance of Beasts turning their nature into an instructive element. This is a thread for selling people on Beast.<br /> <br /> You've aligned yourself with the side of the discussion that is trying to sell people on Beast rather than the side of it that is asking to be sold on Beast. You're rapidly approaching the point of having abandoned any viable claim to still engaging in that attempt.<br /> <br /> Again, start doing that or stop doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:50:31-07:00","id":913894,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> And you're making me less interested in playing a game that I didn't need to be sold on in the first place because you've got a hostile, condescending attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:13:47-07:00","id":913899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913891#post913891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> If it were clear, we wouldn't be having this conversation. Heck, if it was clear, there wouldn't even be conversations between the writing team about how it's misconstrued. This does, however, bode well for my hope that future books will allow feeding in ways other than causing people harm. If you're allowed to share anything with us, that might also help sell people on the book.<br /> <br /> As is, there's the strong implication that you have to harm others, and that it's the only way to feed without using alternative methods. Telling me that my opinion of the text is wrong doesn't help anything. Telling me the actual intent might. Because, again, <i>as presented in the book</i>, you have to do harm to feed, and doing more harm helps you feed better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had I not been around for ten years on the forums, I might agree with you about misconstruing information. Hell, had I not been here during the months of debacle over Changeling Second's Seeming Drawbacks before Changeling Second's Clarity was announced and radically changed everyone;s opinion on the matter, I might have agreed with you. Even more on point, if I had not been around for the initial Beast debacle and seen how many people misinterpretted the revised text in favor of their interpretation from the old one, I might have agreed with you.<br /> <br /> But here's a truth: no matter what you do, there will always be parts of the fanbase who will get the wrong ideas. And part of that is the nature of the medium and it's ingestion-books only have so much space, and it seems like a not insignificant portion of the population* tend to not even read the book but read pirated sections that leave out pertinent bits of context, and even then, it's hard to blame people for reading something and letting their impressions override what it actually says. But that doesn't stop the fact that we could have a book as thick as the bible explaining in a myriad of crystal clear terms how exactly Hunger works and why, and people would still misconstrue it.<br /> <br /> Fans get shit wrong. Taking the opportunity to expand it so less people get stuff wrong is always an aid, but none of that matters for the audience that has basically made up their own mind on the subject. It's not even a wholly blameable offense, given the media culture as it is today or the average habits of the fans. But, fittingly in the spirit of some of the themes of Beast, it is what it is.<br /> <br /> The first three chapters, on the subject of Satiety and the Hungers, particularly the actual section for the actual Satiety mechanic, makes it pretty clear how this all works. Chapters Five and Seven wrap the entire thing neatly in a bow. I invite you to go reread the book. Because Heavy Arms and Satchel are right according to the text.<br /> <br /> *who I must note seem to consistently be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-14-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:18:01-07:00","id":913900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913894#post913894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> And you're making me less interested in playing a game that I didn't need to be sold on in the first place because you've got a hostile, condescending attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said this before on this thread, but if you don't want to be sold on the game... Why are you here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:27:26-07:00","id":913903,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:9px\">Why are my posts getting Likes...</span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I am literally looking at the book. Even the weakest ways to fulfill your Satiety through your Hunger all involve things that many people would consider &quot;being a dick&quot;. I'm not misconstruing that. The game literally tells me what the minimum threshold is for Sating your Horror through Hunger. I'm not seeing how that could be misconstrued at all. If anything, I feel like I'm the one being misconstrued. I said a thing, then showed how it was supported by the text. I'm not relying on what 4chan or RPGnet said about the leaked version or the Kickstarter. I'm looking in the book, as it currently exists (albeit probably not the final edit, but I doubt a few extra commas will change anything).<br /> <br /> Again, if there's something you feel I'm not &quot;getting&quot;, or something you feel I should know, explain it to me, don't just keep telling me I'm wrong. If there's a way to feed through Hunger that doesn't involve causing harm. <i>Explaining</i> that would be selling someone on the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> Because I was pointing out how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10158_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10158\" data-vbnamecard=\"10158\">TheStranjer</a> was patently wrong about the game and giving plenty of reasons why people might want to play it. You know, I was <i>selling someone on the game</i>. I didn't need to be sold on the game because I already know why I might be interested in it, presumably the same as you. I was in the thread to give other people reasons they might want to play, but then I happened to mention a flaw and get dogpiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-14-2016, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:39:02-07:00","id":913911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913857#post913857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why it's dissonant. That's the only story you can tell. As written, a Beast is not able to feed &quot;safely&quot;. It's not like Vampire where the parasitism metaphor can be stretched to the point that you do very little harm and feed safely from your willing blood dolls. You <i>have</i> to do harm. And since you need to get Potential Satiety over your current Satiety, that often means doing a lot of harm. That you do harm and justify it with &quot;this is for your own good&quot; is why a lot of people see Beast as an abuse metaphor. And it would be nice if you could move beyond that. Consider for a moment &quot;shock&quot;:</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't have to cause harm. A tyrant can literally feed by just being visibly and clearly better than other people in their job. Or are you arguing that it's harmful to be competently at your job? A collector can own a pawn shop or actually be a collector and buy stuff from people. A ravager can be a white hacker and destroy someone's sense of security by demonstrating how easily their security can be bypassed. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913857#post913857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, let's put aside how reasonable a conclusion it is whether or not &quot;lock your doors&quot; constitutes a lesson, as if all Beasts were members of <s><a href=\"http://metalgear.wikia.com/wiki/Dead_Cell\" target=\"_blank\">Dead</a></s><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Cell\" target=\"_blank\">Red Cell</a>, testing out security weaknesses by staging fake terrorist attacks. <i>Shock</i> is a moment of profound realization. Why does this have to come at the result of harm? Why does only negative emotion strengthen the Primordial Dream? Yes, yes, it's the Darkbad Shadowlands of the Temenos, but that's part of the problem. It's kind of arbitrary. Why shouldn't a Beast be able to work <i>with</i> their Horror when they change their outlook and work towards actually doing good in the world? If the Beast can potentially learn positive, helpful traits (even if they really only benefit those they have Kinship with), why can't they alter their Beast to not feed from misery? Maybe an example would be in order.<br /> <br /> You're a Beast. You buy into the notion of teaching Lessons. You could try to teach a lesson against assault by assaulting someone. It's big, bad, harmful, gorges the Beast, and says &quot;see how you like when it's done to you&quot;. That's more or less what the book encourages you to do. But let's be honest, in the real world if people having bad things done to them ever actually taught them a lesson, we wouldn't live in such a crappy world that isn't a <s>World</s>Chronicle of Darkness. More often than not, the lesson people get taught is &quot;no one cares about you&quot; or even &quot;this is normal, so it will be okay when you do it&quot;. There's a reason abused kids grow up to be abusers. It's because their parents taught through example that abuse is an acceptable response.<br /> But, <i><b>what if</b></i> instead of beating someone up or raping them or stealing their shit or abusing your authority over them, you instead make them empathize? What if instead of tormenting them you make them feel <i>for</i> someone <i>else</i>, instead of for themselves. What if you do something like <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6s3Fx0lq9Ws\" target=\"_blank\">this ad</a> to cause <i>shock</i>? What about making someone realize the gays are just like them? The book would have you teach a bully a Lesson the old fashioned way, bullying them right back and making them to afraid to retaliate, but why can't you feed from the <i>shock</i> of showing them that the people they torment are just like them? I mean, I know the reason; &quot;teach a Lesson&quot; was thrown in at the last minute to appease people because Beast's first draft was received negatively. It's not a bad idea, but by necessity as a last minute addition, it's pretty much tacked on.<br /> <br /> Hopefully in a Player's Guide or STG, we will see ways to feed that don't have to directly involve harming people. Even if it was <i>harder</i> to feed this way, it would at least be something working towards that theme of teaching a lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've figured out the issue here. Let me clarify this one more time. Your Horror doesn't give a crap what you do so long as it gets fed. You want to use that towards a greater good, fine it's with you every step of the way as your faithful hunting dog. Maybe you have to rein it in because it wants to do more than you do, but so long as it gets some jerky strips at the end of it the Horror is cool with what you want to do. No the book isn't saying &quot;your lesson has to be done as horribly as possible.&quot; You want to stop a bully fine just go in their and no sell everything they try to do. Then you make it clear that you could destroy them, but you don't think that would be right. You give them a warning that they may want to reconsider doing this again lest they come against someone less merciful. Maybe they learn the lesson you were aiming for and lay off the bullying, maybe they miss the point and the conclusion they come to is not to screw with you again. The lessons a Beast tries to teach are decided by the Beast and are fully capable of changing to match the character's desires and situation. The lesson does not have to be some epic life changing statement. It is not Epic Motivation.<br /> <br /> As for non-harmful methods of feeding. It's called family dinner pretty sure it's been mentioned before. Seriously we have a thread where a guy mentions feeding off a changeling getting glamour by pranking the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:39:52-07:00","id":913912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913903#post913903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SIZE=9px]<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> Because I was pointing out how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10158_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10158\" data-vbnamecard=\"10158\">TheStranjer</a> was patently wrong about the game and giving plenty of reasons why people might want to play it. You know, I was <i>selling someone on the game</i>. I didn't need to be sold on the game because I already know why I might be interested in it, presumably the same as you. I was in the thread to give other people reasons they might want to play, but then I happened to mention a flaw and get dogpiled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise for misunderstanding, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:41:35-07:00","id":913913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913903#post913903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the weakest ways to fulfill your Satiety through your Hunger all involve things that many people would consider &quot;being a dick&quot;..</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting deer makes you a dick?<br /> <br /> &quot; Low Satiety: Almost any target counts for this level of Satiety. If she wants flesh or blood, any human willing to put up a fight or give chase will do. It doesn\u2019t matter if the prey poses any significant challenge or risk. <b>Even an animal target </b><b>can sate the Horror at this level.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Convincing people to see your point of view, or dropping names, makes you a dick?<br /> <br /> &quot;Low Satiety: Any show of power applies for a low Satiety meal. <b>Namedropping to convince a police officer to give a warning instead of a traffic ticket might apply, or convincing a small-press publisher</b> <b>to stop hiring a freelance writer due to his inflammatory political views</b>. Shouting or staring someone down, or even just threatening to punch them if they don\u2019t shut up would also apply.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:42:25-07:00","id":913914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913911#post913911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for non-harmful methods of feeding. It's called family dinner pretty sure it's been mentioned before. Seriously we have a thread where a guy mentions feeding off a changeling getting glamour by pranking the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing that and having quite the chuckle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T00:25:20-07:00","id":913934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> These are the examples in the book of the lowest benchmark for feeding through Hunger (and, again, I'm only talking about Hunger. I've repeatedly tried making it clear that I'm not talking about Family Dinner, since feeding through Hunger is the one that Beasts try to justify):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyrants</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety: Any show of power applies for a low Satiety meal. Namedropping to convince a police officer to give a warning instead of a traffic ticket might apply, or convincing a small-press publisher to stop hiring a freelance writer due to his inflammatory political views. Shouting or staring someone down, or even just threatening to punch them if they don\u2019t shut up would also apply.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Collectors (emphasis mine)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety: The Collector can seek out anything that generally fits within the scope of his desire. A Collector who hoards gold can walk into any jewelry shop and steal (<b><i>but not buy</i></b>) something, or mug an upper-middle-class person to take the ring she wears, and walk away sated.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravagers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety: For low Satiety, if it bleeds, it works. If someone is hurt significantly in a way they\u2019ll remember for at least a week, it\u2019s enough. If the destruction is enough to a family cry \u2014 burn a car, kill a pet, cut down an old tree \u2014 the Horror can feed. The Beast doesn\u2019t have to remain anonymous, but doing so keeps the focus on the destruction, rather than the destructor (and, obviously, keeps the authorities off her tail).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Predators</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Satiety: Almost any target counts for this level of Satiety. If she wants flesh or blood, any human willing to put up a fight or give chase will do. It doesn\u2019t matter if the prey poses any significant challenge or risk. Even an animal target can sate the Horror at this level.</div> </div> </div> </div>At best as a Collector who owns a pawn shop, you could be the scummy guy who takes advantage of people to get their goods. &quot;You're desperate and this is worth a lot, but best I can do is 20$&quot;. You also can't &quot;just be a regular collector&quot;, either; <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hoard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some simply toss them in a room and lock the door; <i>the hunt is the beginning and end of their care for the item</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>At best, you can feed your Hunger by being a dick to people who deserve it. I've already said Beast is good for playing a vigilante Vampion style character.<br /> <br /> The only reason we're on this whole tangent where everyone's just shy of calling me a troll and telling me I should leave the thread is because I said that the Lesson aspect of Beast is poorly integrated in the first place. Telling me that it's &quot;just justification&quot; doesn't open my eyes to anything, it's what I was saying in the first place. The book isn't saying your Lesson needs to be done as horribly as possible, the book is saying your <i>Feeding</i> is going to be better the more horrible you make it, and that you're supposed to justify it or make yourself feel better by saying you taught a lesson.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> While sating your Hunger for Prey by hunting an animal is a socially acceptable way of doing things, that's far from shooting my entire argument in the foot. I mean, Prey is the one that even outright says: &quot;the Beast does not have to kill her prey, but <i>she does need to harm it</i> in some way&quot;. Also, yes, I fail to see in what world intimidating someone or going &quot;my <i>father</i> wouldn't like that&quot; is not being a dick. At best I'll concede that convincing someone not to hire a writer with inflammatory opinions isn't being dickish, but then again, maybe I'm a dick.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Although, again, I'm not really trying to convince people not to play, just saying &quot;this is a reason people don't play&quot;, so maybe we should just drop this thread of conversation since it's not actually going anywhere, other than making me want to play less...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-14-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T01:18:27-07:00","id":913945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913874#post913874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;111&quot;]The Horror goes on a rampage if you have low Satiety, but it's unlikely to actually do harm unless you're a big bad powerful beastie with lots of Power and Lair. Especially when you get to Ravenous, where it's basically impossible to harm anyone, since it's a Chance die no matter how strong your Lair is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The threat of your Horror going hunting in the Dream is not that it does harm (it never does actual physical harm, just eats WP and turns it into Satiety). The risk is that dramatic failures (likely when Ravenous with that automatic chance die), or exceptional successes (likely when Starving as you increase in power and as your Horror targets the same individuals repeatedly), attracts the attention of Heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Failing to acknowledge reasons why people don't want to play the game in the first place isn't helpful to a thread on why people should play the game, either. </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between acknowledging it and correcting it because it's wrong, and acknowledging it and letting them continue to think that their impression is correct when it isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And don't act like I'm just threadcrapping....<br /> ...Every time I've argued with you the last few days has been fruitless. I don't need to be sold on Beast. I don't hate Beast. I was <i>defending</i> Beast just two pages ago. I'm also not misinformed. I'm literally looking at the book. I quoted a page. I literally provided you a mechanical breakdown to show why I disagree with you. Do you just enjoy being dismissive or something? If we pretend that I am someone who needs to be sold on Beast, <i>in what way are you selling me on it?</i> </div> </div> </div>1) Just because you started off not-threadcrappy doesn't mean you haven't turned your post threadcrappy. You don't get a free pass just because you said something &quot;right&quot; first.<br /> <br /> 2) Well, it tends to be fruitless to argue with someone that can actually out argue you on the actual facts. You seem to be very set on posting various statements as &quot;facts&quot; without every actually supporting them (even when you quote the books, you never tie them together properly), and then using every non-rules breaking underhanded rhetorical trick in the book to duck being called out on when you're wrong.<br /> <br /> 3) Sure, I tend to like dismissing shit that should be dismissed. Your posts tend to be full of such things. As I've said before, even if you don't mean to, you post like a concern troll (even if you don't seem to know what that means, seriously Google it). I'm completely convinced by our interactions that you would purposefully post a &quot;defense&quot; of Beast solely as a flimsy shield to then justify a spree of bashing the game under the guise of, &quot;but this is what a person that needs to be sold might say!&quot; If you were really a person that was interested in being sold, or just pretending to be that person, you would have acceded to all the clarifications, explanations, and so on that myself and others have stated. Instead you've repeatedly doubled down on points. The whole, &quot;Now I feel like playing the game even less&quot; thing just adds to my impressions that you want to bash the game, and are now trying to blame the people that are defending it for your dislike because of a &quot;distasteful&quot; discussion with us that's mostly actually your doing.<br /> <br /> Basically, you're getting treated like you are, because we're not idiots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T01:31:58-07:00","id":913950,"title":"","content":"what the christ","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T01:45:19-07:00","id":913954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913945#post913945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, you're getting treated like you are, because we're not idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a little far, perhaps we should tone this down a bit and act like the mature people we are. That goes for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T02:05:14-07:00","id":913959,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of dog piling of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> happening. For the record, IMO <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2998_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2998\" data-vbnamecard=\"2998\">Aspel</a> has a different interpretation of the text than others. This should be something for discussion and debate. The text does have areas that invite different reads. These may or may not conform with authorial intent, and people can and should talk about it.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of us need to be dicks about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 06-14-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:06:58-07:00","id":914041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=913959#post913959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any of us need to be dicks about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if we want Satiety :V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:38:33-07:00","id":914381,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bEnough of the dogpiling and arguing, if it continues I'm closing down the thread. Everyone stop being dicks, there's no satiety to be gained from it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:42:29-07:00","id":914431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=914041#post914041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if we want Satiety :V</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that was pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:18:36-07:00","id":914477,"title":"","content":"Alright, to add some constructive content, I'd like to suggest an alternate approach to the ideas of what it means for a Beast lacking Integrity and their morality someone suggested many pages ago.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd say that the reason Beasts don't have Breaking Points is that the Horror is made of sterner stuff than the numinal organ that beings of the Chronicles call a soul. Normal humans, who have these instead of Horrors, find that the soul become strained when the person is forced to do or witness things that damage their self-image either by striking a personal chord (the five questions) or by things that strain the psyche (killing or witnessing the supernatural), wounding their Integrity (the health bar of the soul, in a way), and thus causing psychological damage. The Horror is immune to this sort of strain, meaning that a Beast is not guaranteed to suffer psychological damage because of things they do.<br /> <br /> Wrapping around to this thread's point, it means that right and wrong are both more and less of a pressing issue for Beasts. If you go around murdering people, it won't cause your Integrityesque to go down. And yet that doesn't mean you can't tell right from wrong, it just means that you have to chose what you'll do, knowing that the only thing you'll likely lose is a clear conscious.<br /> <br /> Really, I think Beast seems like a good game for exploring morality in part <i>because</i> there's no &quot;sanity/morality meter&quot; to point to. You have to decide how to live with what you are, and you don't have any mechanics to point to for an easy answer (note that easy answers are not always the right one, especially in 2e). What will you chose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:06:37-07:00","id":914563,"title":"","content":"<br /> Wow, this exploded while I was away.<br /> <br /> All right, attempting to address this constructively. I see at least three separate points that are being discussed as though they're the same thing.<br /> <br /> 1: The majority of Beasts are going to end up feeding in ways that are at least somewhat abusive because the mechanics incentivize it and there isn't a whole lot of text on viable alternatives outside of family dinner. This makes many players kind of uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I don't think even the most ardent supporters of Beast are arguing against this? It's a dark game with some heavy themes, and it's not going to appeal to everyone.<br /> <br /> 2: It's impossible for Beasts to feed in a positive or even neutral manner.<br /> <br /> Somehow point one always seems to warp into point two in these discussions, and while I agree with the former I flatly dispute the latter. I have provided, and seen from other people, a number of examples to the contrary. <br /> <br /> 3: 'Lessons' seem kind of tacked on and lacking in mechanical weight, and don't do a lot to convince many players that Beasts are any less harmful.<br /> <br /> Well, yes, and I think that's thematically appropriate. Remember that most Beasts spent a significant part of their formative years as humans, and the human half of the gestalt entity they've become is likely to noooot be exactly comfortable with the things their Horror wants. The teaching aspect is one way many Beasts try to live with what they have to do. It's not &quot;I'm hurting you to teach you a lesson&quot; it's &quot;I'm trying to make this into a lesson so that I'm not just committing random acts of cruelty&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:47:42-07:00","id":914631,"title":"","content":"Opening up a side route that bears consideration: Beasts are the fixers of the wider supernatural community.<br /> <br /> They're metaphysically incentivized to seek out and make connections with as many other monsters as they can, they have a widely-useful bargaining chip to lean on if unnatural charisma doesn't grease the wheels enough, and the nature of Primordial Pathways encourages them to travel to other planes and places and hunt there to bring them closer to home.<br /> <br /> One of the fun things Kinship brings to the table in this manner is that more world-wise Beasts are encouraged to be the guy who knows a guy no matter where you have to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:02:55-07:00","id":915156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=914563#post914563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2: It's impossible for Beasts to feed in a positive or even neutral manner.<br /> <br /> Somehow point one always seems to warp into point two in these discussions, and while I agree with the former I flatly dispute the latter. I have provided, and seen from other people, a number of examples to the contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen many examples so far that were not contradicted by the book itself, so uncommon as to be unsustainable or frightening in the ethical implications and thus undeserving of the term 'neutral'. I, for one, do not want someone sustained supernaturally from punishment <b>anywhere near</b> a legal and judicial system. Citing promotions as a method of feeding Power belies how frequently Beasts need to feed and how rare promotions are. Collecting things no one wants, or even buying items, completely misunderstands how Feeding functions and contradicts the rules for Hoard on page 109. Prey <b>requires</b> harm explicitly, though at least at Low Satiety you can restrict yourselves to animals. Most of the ones I can think of that are viable are based on Ruin, actually.<br /> <br /> I really liked your post on page 9 though, it mirrors some of my own thoughts on reading <i>Beast </i>and relating it to sadistic urges. It reminded me of a scene in the documentary <i>Harmontown</i> where Dan Harmon explains how sometimes when arguing with his (then) girlfriend he just knows the exact words to bring her to tears, he can't help himself. He doesn't like it's a part of him, but cannot change it either. The <i>Harmontown </i>podcast itself feels a little like Changeling/Beast crossover come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:15:28-07:00","id":915278,"title":"","content":"Regarding the whole &quot;teaching lessons&quot; part, I am reminded of this comment by Extra Credits on God Of War. The gameplay in that series is mostly combat and puzzles. Is solving puzzles a weird thing for a divinity of bloody strife to do so often? Sure, but it's better than to make the gameplay only consist of over the top hack and slash.<br /> <br /> Beast benefits from &quot;teaching lessons&quot; like God Of War benefits from puzzles, loosely speaking. The big difference is that the puzzles are not tied to the themes. Beast would be <i>less</i> interesting if there was no internal conflict leading to rationalizations, on the part of Beasts <i>and</i> Heroes. Can you imagine how dull it would be if both sides were totally OK with what they did, all the time?<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not all about Feeding, which bears emphatic repeating. There's the Jack Of All Trades aspect, which allows you to create a very unique monster when you use it right. Each Atavism is available to all Beasts, and Nightmares do a lot more than simply cause fear. Lairs are very customizable, and it is possible to change your personal approach to your Hunger, or even change the Hunger itself (that requires some in-character justification and roleplaying it out, though). You can homebrew a Merit that gives a second Hunger and it won't break the game. Your notions of who your true Kin are can be challenged and adapt.<br /> <br /> Another important fact is that the Devouring does not remove all your humanity. You no longer use Integrity, but you do have a Life along with your Legend. Nothing forbids you from changing those traits either.<br /> <br /> Your Beast does not have to be a static monster, like a page torn from a folklore book and given life by a halfhearted ritual. They should have all the splendor and terror of man and monster alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-15-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:33:32-07:00","id":916272,"title":"","content":"I really fell in love with Beast: the Primordial in its draft phase. I enjoyed that the game had no shame in portraying a monster and I felt that the game's meaning was informed just as much by what wasnt said (lack of Integrity, for example) as what was said. Then in the final draft, Teaching Lessons was introduced to provide &quot;purpose&quot;, but this clashed hard (in my view at least) in a game that was fundamentally about searching for purpose (ie: building your Legend). <br /> <br /> But this is a Sell Me thread, so let me explain why I'm okay with the Teaching Lessons, in principle if not how its been implemented in the text. <br /> <br /> Teaching Lessons has nothing to back it up. There are no mechanics that I can see which tie into it and therefore as far as the mechanics of the game is concerned, Teaching Lessons does not matter. This is to highlight that Teaching Lessons has absolutely zero impact on the monster that is your true self. It doesn't care, and therefore on a level? You don't care. <br /> <br /> Teaching Lessons is, strictly, an ideology established by Beasts in order to placate their conscience and self image. It is a toothless philosophy, and this is a good thing for storytelling purposes. This is because in a world without inherent meaning beyond the Hunger and the Feast, meaning is built by those who strive to find purpose outside of that monstrous cycle. And this is telling stories at the heart of it. <br /> <br /> A critical error of the book that was published is that only one such philosophy of purpose was established and because there's only one philosophy presented, it's assumed that its the only philosophy that exists. But there can be more philosophies to discover. Ideologies compete with each other, and this is a critical area where Beasts can argue and fight over with each other, presenting greater conflict and drama for your stories. <br /> <br /> A strength of Beast is that it speaks loudly in the absence of what isn't said and there is much more to explore in the darkness. So you get to have fun with that and be a real monster in the process. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:36:57-07:00","id":916435,"title":"","content":"Well said.<br /> <br /> My only quibble is that while the game could have done more philosophies besides the lessons (but it was a fairly rushed second draft so I tend to give the authors some leeway there, it's not like they had a lot of time or space to develop multiple ideologies), the philosophy presented is vague and broad enough to have a huge number of points to argue about among the Beasts that hold to it.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to come up with a large number of basic sub-ideologies around this concept, all with enough points of agreement and dissent from each other to make for a few game instances worth of philosophic drama. Even without a platter of options for Beasts to select from regarding philosophies, I feel like most Beasts (and esp. PC Beasts) are all going to have their own unique spin on the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:53:29-07:00","id":916442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=916435#post916435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well said.<br /> <br /> My only quibble is that while the game could have done more philosophies besides the lessons (but it was a fairly rushed second draft so I tend to give the authors some leeway there, it's not like they had a lot of time or space to develop multiple ideologies), the philosophy presented is vague and broad enough to have a huge number of points to argue about among the Beasts that hold to it.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to come up with a large number of basic sub-ideologies around this concept, all with enough points of agreement and dissent from each other to make for a few game instances worth of philosophic drama. Even without a platter of options for Beasts to select from regarding philosophies, I feel like most Beasts (and esp. PC Beasts) are all going to have their own unique spin on the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thread to discuss possible alternative philosophies would not go amiss, methinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T00:39:51-07:00","id":917226,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else seem to notice that, if we use The Nightmare Before Christmas as an analogy, people seem to think that being a Beast means you have to be Oogie Boogie, whereas players generally want to play them like Jack Skellington? You are/want to be the king of the town, scaring people, embodying fear...because that's your job, your new being, you've come to terms with your new hunger, and you're looking to do it in a way that is in some way beneficial for everyone (such as embodying Halloween).<br /> <br /> The more irate critics of the game seem to just see the game as just being cruel, murdering and eating the normal people (and yet not complaining how Vampire and Werewolf does this far more casually), while saying that Heroes are evil because they stop you (while likewise ignoring how Hunters also go this route...just more sympathetically). Does this seem like a weird paradox to you guys, or am I misreading things?<br /> <br /> Also I want to make a pumpkin themed Eshmaki now. Let the Pumpkin King rise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T00:49:39-07:00","id":917228,"title":"","content":"Everyone hail to the Pumpkin King...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T01:04:11-07:00","id":917230,"title":"","content":"In all seriousness though, I think that one of the main reasons people feel so much more strongly about Beast feeding as opposed to Werewolf or Vampire is because of the necessity of fear and arguably therefore suffering. It's like the difference between terrorising an animal before slaughtering it and giving it a quick, clean death. Now, I'm not saying that a werewolf in Basu-im is going to be anything like clean or 'nice' in killing its victims (it's more likely to claw their guts out and eat them while the unfortunate is still alive) but pain and fear aren't its object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T01:09:05-07:00","id":917233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917226#post917226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more irate critics of the game seem to just see the game as just being cruel, murdering and eating the normal people (and yet not complaining how Vampire and Werewolf does this far more casually), while saying that Heroes are evil because they stop you (while likewise ignoring how Hunters also go this route...just more sympathetically). Does this seem like a weird paradox to you guys, or am I misreading things?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair to the irate critics, the book gives a wide variety of examples of things Beasts do and many of them are quite cruel and end in death, while both vampires and werewolves have mechanical issues that do not make murdering and eating humans a casual affair. And I don't believe there's been much in the way of people saying Heroes are evil in this thread. It was a common complaint about the pre-rewrite version, and that was because they were meant to be considered evil and pathetic, but were also created by the Beast, however inadvertently, and not in control of themselves <br /> <br /> But yeah, at least two sides are coming at the game from different angles and this is likely why there's likely so much contention over it. Because they're both right. One's focusing on the example where the Beast finds people and cripples them, the other where the lawyer Beast defends people who would otherwise go undefended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T01:32:54-07:00","id":917241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917226#post917226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else seem to notice that, if we use The Nightmare Before Christmas as an analogy, people seem to think that being a Beast means you have to be Oogie Boogie, whereas players generally want to play them like Jack Skellington? You are/want to be the king of the town, scaring people, embodying fear...because that's your job, your new being, you've come to terms with your new hunger, and you're looking to do it in a way that is in some way beneficial for everyone (such as embodying Halloween).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's our job, but we're not mean....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:27:59-07:00","id":917653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917233#post917233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair to the irate critics, the book gives a wide variety of examples of things Beasts do and many of them are quite cruel and end in death, while both vampires and werewolves have mechanical issues that do not make murdering and eating humans a casual affair. And I don't believe there's been much in the way of people saying Heroes are evil in this thread. It was a common complaint about the pre-rewrite version, and that was because they were meant to be considered evil and pathetic, but were also created by the Beast, however inadvertently, and not in control of themselves<br /> <br /> But yeah, at least two sides are coming at the game from different angles and this is likely why there's likely so much contention over it. Because they're both right. One's focusing on the example where the Beast finds people and cripples them, the other where the lawyer Beast defends people who would otherwise go undefended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another problem: the feeding examples given are overwhelmingly depressing. I mean, if I picture myself in a game as the asshole cabbie example or the old woman in the suburb and... I have no idea what's supposed to be fun about stranding people somewhere or lording over a suburb. Everyone who IS sold on Beast, what are you actually excited about getting to do in the game? This thread has essays in it about the high concept of what's supposed to be fun/compelling, but most of the examples given in the preview are... not exactly becoming of legendary monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:55:39-07:00","id":917665,"title":"","content":"Conflating Feeding with everything that's supposed to be fun about the game, or what's supposed to be &quot;becoming&quot; of legendary monsters is a pretty weird way of framing things in the first place.<br /> <br /> I think that's part of the problem with a lot of the criticism of the game. Feeding (which is important, but it is not like it is a massive part of the book either) is the only thing that gets focus. Besides the potential fun for getting creating in feeding, there's all the fun in being a legendary monster (just like any of the other game lines) via things like Lair and Atavisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:01:06-07:00","id":917671,"title":"","content":"What am I excited about getting to do? I'm excited about using the game as a metaphor to work through my struggles with intrusive thoughts. To deal with existence as a person with a literal monster in their head that they have to appease to one degree or another. For one character, this means really going off the grimdark end and torturing Heroes for fun, seeing the worst side of the splat. For another, it means joining a freehold and trying to become a Fae crushing guardian. Sometimes it means joining a big group of diverse supernats and dealing with possessions and serial killers and whatever bad weird entities the CoD has to offer. And occasionally hunting one another for fun because eh everybody has regeneration and is fine two hours later, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:01:26-07:00","id":917672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917653#post917653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has essays in it about the high concept of what's supposed to be fun/compelling, but most of the examples given in the preview are... not exactly becoming of legendary monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, supernatural identity tangle notwithstanding, the legendary monster is not what is doing the feeding.<br /> <br /> As with a lot of other elements of Beastly metaphysics, Satiety is gained through sympathy \u2014 it's why Family Dinner works even if you're an unacknowledged passive observer of a feeding rather than an active participant and it's why the hungry Horror gets fed when other people are made to feel panic and need. The Horror is the archetypal vector human instinct attributes to the losses feeding creates.<br /> <br /> Stealing a house key twice a month or breaking a window every other Tuesday may not be the stuff of epics, but the monster proper only gets fussy about wanting fancy heists and elaborate coups when you're alone and trying to overeat; petty inconveniences keep the lights off in the Lair week-to-week the same way luring drunks into alleys or instigating road rage serves as basic upkeep for vampires and changelings.<br /> <br /> The chief problem the first draft had, in my view, is that its presentation was more readily appropriate for long-established and powerful Beasts; those are the ones best suited to seeing eye to eye with the Firstborn and making a habit of roving serial murder. The final draft's greater focus on Kinship really is a better headspace to approach the fresher Begotten specimens, and not just because of Family Dinner \u2014 having the feeding habits of other supernaturals closer to hand helps to keep the intensity of gaining Satiety in context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T14:21:15-07:00","id":918246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917672#post917672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stealing a house key twice a month or breaking a window every other Tuesday may not be the stuff of epics, but the monster proper only gets fussy about wanting fancy heists and elaborate coups when you're alone and trying to overeat; petty inconveniences keep the lights off in the Lair week-to-week the same way luring drunks into alleys or instigating road rage serves as basic upkeep for vampires and changelings.<br /> <br /> The chief problem the first draft had, in my view, is that its presentation was more readily appropriate for long-established and powerful Beasts; those are the ones best suited to seeing eye to eye with the Firstborn and making a habit of roving serial murder. The final draft's greater focus on Kinship really is a better headspace to approach the fresher Begotten specimens, and not just because of Family Dinner \u2014 having the feeding habits of other supernaturals closer to hand helps to keep the intensity of gaining Satiety in context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed!<br /> <br /> Also in answer to the question about what kinds of things we were looking forward to. For me its the big stuff. One of the things that I've learned in games set in modern games generally and CofD specifically is that the player exist as people in the world and thus have to deal with mundane consequenses to their actions (which is something that im sure most people posting here know already lol).<br /> <br /> IMHO Stories of the build up to doing a big thing with minimal fallout and far ranging effects (within the scope and theme of the game of course) are the thing. but then again, I'm the player that spends 4 months planning, bribing, and coercing before &quot;Red Wedding-ing&quot; the angelic cult that has been hassling the other players or driving a Toyota Carolla with a trunk full of hedgespun C-4 through the front door of a Belials Brood meetup. I also understand that's not everyones bag. That being said, the story of a Ravager Using the Leverage of the community of kin to Level a G-M Facility for a &quot;friend of the family&quot; sounds pretty exciting to me too.<br /> <br /> sorry for the spelling errors and rushed structure, still at work. cheers all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:36:14-07:00","id":919455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917226#post917226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else seem to notice that, if we use The Nightmare Before Christmas as an analogy, people seem to think that being a Beast means you have to be Oogie Boogie, whereas players generally want to play them like Jack Skellington? You are/want to be the king of the town, scaring people, embodying fear...because that's your job, your new being, you've come to terms with your new hunger, and you're looking to do it in a way that is in some way beneficial for everyone (such as embodying Halloween).<br /> <br /> The more irate critics of the game seem to just see the game as just being cruel, murdering and eating the normal people (and yet not complaining how Vampire and Werewolf does this far more casually), while saying that Heroes are evil because they stop you (while likewise ignoring how Hunters also go this route...just more sympathetically). Does this seem like a weird paradox to you guys, or am I misreading things?<br /> <br /> Also I want to make a pumpkin themed Eshmaki now. Let the Pumpkin King rise...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the book <i>is</i> selling the reader on playing Oogie Boogie most of the time, it's just that twisting those rules to play Jack Skellington is cooler and more interesting. It's not that different from how some Exalted fans love a particular interpretation of Infernals that completely ejects half the text of that book.<br /> <br /> And you are misreading the criticism of Beast rather badly, unfortunately. Comparing it to how Vampire and Hunter deal with similar topics in a more mature manner is common, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T03:31:27-07:00","id":919624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917653#post917653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has essays in it about the high concept of what's supposed to be fun/compelling, but most of the examples given in the preview are... not exactly becoming of legendary monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a stripper who feeds off clients during private shows, or a ghetto vigilante draining muggers and gangbangers in the city's back alleys, or a small-time drug dealer trading coke for blood aren't exactly things Dracula would do either, yet I've had vampire characters in my various campaigns (both oWoD and CofD) who did just that for their nightly fix. Just like your starting Requiem character isn't even close to being Dracula, your starting Beast character is neither Cthulhu nor Smaug. Nothing's stopping your fledgling vampire from becoming a legend that will overshadow Dracula one night... but that's in the future, and to reach that future, you need to drink blood tonight. Nothing's stopping your Beast character from becoming a legendary monster someday... but the Horror is hungry <i>now!</i><br /> <br /> Deconstructing legendary monsters by scrutinizing the often annoying and weirdly mundane problems of their everyday existence has been a theme in WoD ever since the original Masquerade game, and Beast is no different. Just as it is for humans, it takes time and effort to prepare a truly exquisite meal for a Beast - and just like humans, most Beasts don't have time to prepare such a treat each and every time they're hungry. Then, there are other considerations, ranging from ethical (more elaborate meals tend to harm others more, and not every Beast is up to it) to pragmatic (more satisfying feedings tend to attract more unwanted attention).<br /> <br /> Note that this doesn't stop you from pulling off epic shit each and every time you feed - it just means you'll be spending more time and effort, and taking greater risks with each feeding than the average Beast. Which may pay off in the long run if becoming a legend is your goal. Or it may get you killed. Your risk, your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T12:58:12-07:00","id":921102,"title":"","content":"Actually thinking about it Jack Skellington isn't a horrible interpretation for a Beast character. I mean consider Jack steals Christmas because he wants something new and thinks he can do the job as well if not better than it's current holder. In a way he's a nicer version of the Grinch, since his screwing up the holiday is from unintentional actions and a misunderstanding of the situation.<br /> <br /> Think like a tyrant who tries to demonstrate clear and absolute superiority in his field because the person figures it'll help the others know it's okay to count on itself and not push themselves past their limits. Not gathering that the repeated establishing of itself as the best and the others shouldn't try to rise above their place is seen as demeaning and insulting as opposed to comforting and helpful. Or the nemesis who deals with a group of thugs to try and avoid causing any problems that might arise from a police confrontation without considering the ramifications that might arise from how it takes out the thugs.<br /> It isn't a terrible idea. Play a Beast who is honestly trying to make the world better, but can't seem to grasp that for one reason or another they're really not helping the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T13:46:17-07:00","id":921670,"title":"","content":"I'd say Nightmare Before Christmas is about a Beast going through an existential crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T14:03:41-07:00","id":921683,"title":"","content":"Can a Beast meditate and have a conversation with their Horror? Do they merge with them when they sleep? Is the Horror an Other like a Geist, or is it the actual soul of the Beast? Is a Brood supposed to contain multiple Beasts, or should it be one Beast and a bunch of others?<br /> <br /> Has it ever been clarified if Beasts have always been Beasts and just become aware of it (like Werewolves), or is it a transformation of a mortal into something else (like Vampires)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T14:56:15-07:00","id":921703,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can really <i>talk</i> with the Horror; the best description I've seen of it conceives it as like the animalistic Id of the Beast. You can meditate in order to take control of it when you're not inside your Lair, but you don't really talk with it. <br /> <br /> As I understand it, a Brood can contain both all Beasts and Beasts with supernaturals, though I think the former is more common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T15:26:53-07:00","id":921718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=921683#post921683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been clarified if Beasts have always been Beasts and just become aware of it (like Werewolves), or is it a transformation of a mortal into something else (like Vampires)?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that it is the latter, referred to as the Devouring. Though some Beasts enter the Devouring willingly and some Beasts also believe it to be a predestined process (which if true would make it more akin to the former).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T16:48:34-07:00","id":921749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=921683#post921683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast meditate and have a conversation with their Horror? Do they merge with them when they sleep? Is the Horror an Other like a Geist, or is it the actual soul of the Beast? Is a Brood supposed to contain multiple Beasts, or should it be one Beast and a bunch of others?<br /> <br /> Has it ever been clarified if Beasts have always been Beasts and just become aware of it (like Werewolves), or is it a transformation of a mortal into something else (like Vampires)?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the original dragt Beasts had always been Beasts even before the Homecoming. Various things occurred and it was decided to make it more ambiguous. So now it's a known that Beast has a closer connection to the Primordial Dream than normal people, but whether this is because they're actually a Beast and don't know it or if it just makes them a target for the Devouring is unknown. <br /> <br /> Conversations are presently not likely due to the portrayal. At the moment I'd view it like checking your raw physical and emotional state. You're probably not gonna be discussing baseball with your Horror, but it'll give you a sense like,I'm hungry; I'm tired; I'm in serious pain; I want to kill someone; and so on and so forth. <br /> <br /> As far as otherness goes, the Horror is basically you. (Just probably not the nicer part of you.) You can merge into it and run around the lair as the Horror, or you can let it run on it's own and just watch through its eyes. So there is a slight degree of seperation, but nothing so far suggests it to be as explicitly different a being as a Geist is.<br /> <br /> As far as broods go I'll cite page 57 of the corebook.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A brood can host any combination, not just Family members. Even other creatures, such as vampires and werewolves, are welcome to join. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:42:42-07:00","id":922286,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> You can be Devoured by another Beast or your own Horror can Devour you. I believe the second is more common. Personally, I think that Sleeping Beauty fought back against her own Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:34:26-07:00","id":923053,"title":"","content":"I am having a harder then I would of normally thought time explaining beast; and I don't know if that is a good thing or a bad thing. For me, and my players(I don't know if I'm playing it right mind you, but I try) its about being in a strange family. Every monster is a part of this family, and like it or not when the people put their minds to something they do it. Last thing anyone wants is them putting their minds to getting rid of everyone under the bed.<br /> <br /> Beast has a kinship with other horrors, this kinship grants a certain ease with other monsters they encounter and can lead to strange encounters and moral quandaries(Ive yet to have a player not make some sort of moral code, they make great aspirations). In our game we met a swarm of 'glass crabs' a swarm of little sea monsters that was eating all the dead bodies floating to shore(they didn't like the light, tourists laying on the beach at night complained of sharp sand). When we first saw them it looked like white sand reached up from the beach and swallowed a cat. When the swarm first saw us it said. &quot;Rip and tear. Cut the meat. Feed the Family&quot; and offered us part of its bounty. They were cool and friendly to us, we were family and with a pound of hamburger they gave us the info we needed, but our interaction raised the question.<br /> <br /> Can we let these little guys go? yea they eat dead bodies now, but what will happen when the serial killer is stopped and no more corpse float in? What happens when their is enough of them to grab a whole human? They're not smart, if we told them to avoid killing people would they listen? Could they remember?('how long before hunters show up' was a running theme) A lot of questions no clear answer. We ended up telling them to move up the beach away from people and back to the dead fish, but I think they might come back if they get hungry again.<br /> <br /> I think beast is about strange interactions with the monsters you call family and trying to get everybody to get along for five bloody minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:31:45-07:00","id":923115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=921683#post921683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been clarified if Beasts have always been Beasts and just become aware of it (like Werewolves), or is it a transformation of a mortal into something else (like Vampires)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devouring sucks and is just a knock off of Vampires embracing. Go with the Homecoming.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, though. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:58:42-07:00","id":923251,"title":"","content":"The Homecoming is uninteresting and is just a knock off of every other &quot;special snowflake realizes their specialness&quot; splat in both versions of the WoD. Go with the Devouring,<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, though. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:37:34-07:00","id":923276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923251#post923251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just a knock off of every other &quot;special snowflake realizes their specialness&quot; splat in both versions of the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what? The only one I can think of where you start out special is Geist and the realization can be skipped straight over to death if there's no geist around to bargain with you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:16:42-07:00","id":923295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923276#post923276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like what? The only one I can think of where you start out special is Geist and the realization can be skipped straight over to death if there's no geist around to bargain with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's werewolves (Uratha and Garou), I didn't even know Sin-Eaters started off special. But honestly, both the Devouring and Homecoming are fine. My reading tells me that the Devouring is more symbolic anyway: it's revelatory rather than destructive, and the revelation comes from without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:19:55-07:00","id":923296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923251#post923251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming is uninteresting and is just a knock off of every other &quot;special snowflake realizes their specialness&quot; splat in both versions of the WoD. Go with the Devouring,<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, though. ^.^</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;special snowflake realizes their specialness&quot; doesn't really fit any splat other than Beast, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:21:52-07:00","id":923297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923295#post923295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's revelatory rather than destructive</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unless you subscribe to the notion that's its more similar to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/917816-of-vampirism-death-and-immortality-or-do-you-really-want-to-be-a-vampire\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:28:32-07:00","id":923301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923296#post923296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;special snowflake realizes their specialness&quot; doesn't really fit any splat other than Beast, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Devouring is not an analog to the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Beast is a particular response to being consumed by a Horror. Becoming a vampire is a consequence of the virulent nature of vampirism.<br /> <br /> One flawed comparison is not better than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:34:40-07:00","id":923307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923301#post923301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Devouring is not an analog to the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Beast is a particular response to being consumed by a Horror. Becoming a vampire is a consequence of the virulent nature of vampirism.<br /> <br /> One flawed comparison is not better than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are listing them as if they are wholly different when that is not actually clear. The only real difference is that Beasts think they were special beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:40:10-07:00","id":923309,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning more towards the Homecoming, with the stipulation that it comes under extreme circumstances. It takes an atrocity to awaken the Horror, be it committed to or by the Beast. Whether through grief, rage, or terror - they reach for reserves they didn't know they had and they tear their Soul in the process. Being kidnapped into slavery, losing all means of survival overnight, being betrayed by one's friends or losing a loved one make very relatable characters. Such a Homecoming gives the PC a strong motivation and provides the game a plot hook right from the start. Characters who committed something so grievous that it turned them into monsters are much darker, but no less compelling, whether they embrace or regret their actions.<br /> <br /> I'm rather attached to this reinterpretation since it ties Beasts closer to the world around them and makes them stand out as individuals. As written, the Homecoming had too little devoted to it, even though it's such a momentous occasion. It gave the impression that it's somehow random. The Devouring made the Beast condition more controllable, <s>while paradoxically caring little for a would-be Beast's attitude</s>, which I think does a disservice to the feel of the game. Trying to trigger such an intense Homecoming is, of course, a very uncomfortable affair. An alternative method would be to take the character bodily into the Primordial Dream and hope that the Horror within them stirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 06-29-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T09:43:37-07:00","id":923311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923307#post923307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are listing them as if they are wholly different when that is not actually clear.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/923055-where-are-all-heroes?p=923108#post923108\">No, it's pretty clear</a>. The Embrace doesn't require that the prospective vampire be accepting of their new state or even remotely conscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:54:41-07:00","id":923362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923295#post923295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's werewolves (Uratha and Garou),</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Garou, though the stories I read did suggest they were very angry kids and very special wolves, but for Uratha if you're counting seeing a werewolf as making you a special snowflake the term is losing some of the cynicism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-29-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:15:45-07:00","id":923375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=923362#post923362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak for Garou, though the stories I read did suggest they were very angry kids and very special wolves, but for Uratha if you're counting seeing a werewolf as making you a special snowflake the term is losing some of the cynicism.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point was that most Uratha are born Uratha, much like most Beasts are born Beasts. The Devouring and the Homecoming, much like the First Change, is probably going to happen before a Begotten dies whether it's assisted or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Or did you mean that &quot;special snowflakes&quot; can only be the kinds of templates that have very few drawbacks, because I'd consider a Begotten to have as many drawbacks as being an Uratha, but like being an Uratha it's good to &quot;know&quot; what you really are. The book does talk about being a Beast as being worth the drawbacks, but I don't think that's a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T20:32:42-07:00","id":923666,"title":"","content":"Excuse me for changing the topic for a moment. I thought of another angle potential players can look at for playing.<br /> I mean the obvious angles include:<br /> <br /> Being the monster: I think we can all agree it is in no way hard to play one of the Begotten as every bit the dangerous psycho Heroes think they are and one might go for in a revenge fantasy. At least without building the Beast in a way to avoid being able to do it easily.<br /> <br /> Well intentioned Beast: You really are trying to make the world better, but supernatural powers aside, you're still human though and sometime your plans don't go as well as you think they will. &quot;All I'm saying is maybe next time you break into a crime lord's place and removing every follicle of hair on their body and leaving the straight razor on the nightstand as a notice of how easy it would be to kill them,as a reminder of why they shouldn't cross certain lines. You might want to be sure you won't drive them to greater heights of paranoia and violence.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ripping off the band-aid: Look sometimes being nice isn't helping.Some bullies won't stop bullying until they've had their ribs broken by a target. Some people will work so hard at the rat race that they are actually likely to literally work themselves to death if no one stops them. (Do you have any idea how many Nightmares would sound like a panic attack or a breakdown when you tell a therapist?) What you do isn't really nice and you'll admit, but you try to be utilitarian about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-15-2016, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}